{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project","id":155803,"title":"Scion 2.0 Project","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-01T12:14:42-07:00","id":155803,"title":"Scion 2.0 Project","content":"<div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Scion 2.0</b></span></span></span></a></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hello Everyone,</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We are proud to announce the </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scion 2.0 </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">website\u2019s release to the public. We have spent the last month working away at it, moving our rules over to the site from a large series of Google Documents, and filled in the blank spots with some pieces from the now closed John\u2019s Scion Resources.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We still have a lot of work ahead of us to complete the full revision of the system, including revising every single Purview, Pantheon Specific Purview, and Epic Attribute to better fit into </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scion 2.0</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. We have finished several projects already, which are detailed below.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The base system of the game is entirely completed, save that some things may be tinkered with slightly in the future, but additionally Animal, Arete, Atman, Chaos, Dexterity, Enech, Mystery, Stamina, Strength, and Water have been entirely completed. Other material is in the heavy playtesting phase and will hopefully be released soon, but we have included a few teasers among the unrevised Attributes and Purviews.</span></span></span> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/purviews/chaos\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chaos</span></span></a></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Guides and Retainers</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Additionally, we have provided a list of possible Guides and Retainers for Scions sorted by Pantheon, which can be found through the link and the Birthrights section of our site. We also have a section displaying the Relics we have used in our games so people can have a better grasp on our pricing system. In the immediate future we are going to be taking requests for potential Relics from mythology that people want to see on the site.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Future Goals</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Our number one goal following launch will be getting the Divine Pronunciation guide up and running, along with ongoing revisions of all the Purviews, Pantheon Specific Purviews, and Epic Attributes. Along the way we fully intend to add all the PDF pantheons researched and written by John\u2019s Scion Resources.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We are planning to finish up some other goals, such as rewriting the Virtues to be more thematic. This includes some extremities which make very little sense. Updating the Scent the Divine tables, adding family trees, and creating the previously mentioned Relics page.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We are incredibly sorry that we have not included the Amatsukami and the Celestial Bureaucracy, for they do have some amazing figures and myths, but we are just not comfortable with them in the state they are in at the moment. We would need to entirely overhaul their Pantheon roster, and their Pantheon Specific Purviews, before we could feel comfortable with having them up on the site. This remains a goal for the distant future, as we stockpile research materials from those regions.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Questions</span></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If anyone has any questions, suggestions, or comments to us, feel free to post them here or send them to </span></span></span><a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#d784b4beb8b9a6a2b2a4a3beb8b9a49790bab6bebbf9b4b8ba\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"a9facac0c6c7f8dcccdaddc0c6c7dae9eec4c8c0c587cac6c4\">[email&#160;protected]</span></u></span></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. We are more than happy to discuss things with you, help explain things, or listen to any suggestions you give us.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We do hope everyone enjoys what we have completed so far, and we hope people continue to enjoy the additional parts of the game we revise over time. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Welcome to the Scion 2.0 Project.</span></b></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-01-2014, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T12:49:07-07:00","id":155850,"title":"","content":"Congrats on the full release! I'm still looking through it, as it's a lot to digest. But great work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T12:55:46-07:00","id":155854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project#post155803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We are incredibly sorry that we have not included the Amatsukami and the Celestial Bureaucracy, for they do have some amazing figures and myths, but we are just not comfortable with them in the state they are in at the moment. We would need to entirely overhaul their Pantheon roster, and their Pantheon Specific Purviews, before we could feel comfortable with having them up on the site. This remains a goal for the distant future, as we stockpile research materials from those regions.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Understandable. When I read the write-up for the Bureaucracy in first edition Scion: Companion, I felt that most of the gods' thoughts of complete domination of the three Worlds seem to be more a threat than the Titans themselves. That's why I had that thread about them. I would've felt uncomfortable playing a Scion of one of the Bureaucrats because, in the back of my mind, there wouldn't be a sense of honor about this. Thanks for taking a closer look at them.<br /> <br /> Plus, what's Atman? I haven't seen that purview before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T12:59:06-07:00","id":155856,"title":"","content":"Also, I noticed that the picture for Chaos has a French Revolution painting part in the circle. Does this mean that we'll be seeing the National Pantheons in future books or is that just for Aestheic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T13:07:24-07:00","id":155861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155856#post155856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I noticed that the picture for Chaos has a French Revolution painting part in the circle. Does this mean that we'll be seeing the National Pantheons in future books or is that just for Aestheic?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an aesthetic choice that plays with the themes of the French Revolution uniting many different classes against the nobles, and successfully overthrowing them. Chaos has been completely and dramatically overhauled so that it barely even resembles its previous incarnation. The theme is no longer randomness. It is now the breakdown of social and spiritual order. This is expressed heavily through social change and rebellion against ruling governments, and their supporters.<br /> <br /> We wanted the public launch of the Scion 2.0 Project to start off with a bang, and a brand new Chaos is our show piece","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T13:08:11-07:00","id":155862,"title":"","content":"Read the Chaos write-up. First, interesting that Chaos now has the Gremlins Boon that the Yankee Pantheon's Unity Puriview once had. and second, looking at Butterfly Effect, I thought that it would be like the Cause and Effect ability from Demon the Descent. You know: You do one unrelated thing and it leads to a mind or life-changing event? The write-up seems to apply that the Boon allows you to gleam intent off a fellow Chaos user. (IMHO)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T13:18:35-07:00","id":155864,"title":"","content":"Saw the write-up for the Orisha. Sad to see favorites like Damballah, Erzulie, and Baron Samedi go like that. Plus, the Loa of first edition was my first look into the African pantheon, so seeing Shango being the head makes me a bit apprehensive. Sorry about that. How are the Loa different from the Orisha and will we be seeing a write-up of the Loa in a future book as an alternative American pantheon to the Orisha, being that it makes me think that the Loa were actually former members of the Orisha that were thrown out by Shango and the Orisha during the Slave trade of the 1600s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T13:46:53-07:00","id":155892,"title":"","content":"Forgive the odd formating but I'm on a phone. The actual Loa will probably see light on our website as lesser gods along with other pantheon favorites that we couldn't release with the launch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T14:10:18-07:00","id":155938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155854#post155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Understandable. When I read the write-up for the Bureaucracy in first edition Scion: Companion, I felt that most of the gods' thoughts of complete domination of the three Worlds seem to be more a threat than the Titans themselves. That's why I had that thread about them. I would've felt uncomfortable playing a Scion of one of the Bureaucrats because, in the back of my mind, there wouldn't be a sense of honor about this. Thanks for taking a closer look at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is terribly sad that we can't manage to get them up. We have a Chinese History expert on hand, but even with him, it is exceptionally difficult to do things for the Shen. For the Amatsukami, we don't even have a resource like him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155854#post155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, what's Atman? I haven't seen that purview before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Atman is based on Brent not Broken's Atman as he has hosted on Modern Mythos, but we have just changed things around to work in Scion 2.0. The way RAW Samsara worked was a bit off, and out of line with Hindu philosophy, or so we have been told. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155854#post155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the Chaos write-up. First, interesting that Chaos now has the Gremlins Boon that the Yankee Pantheon's Unity Puriview once had. and second, looking at Butterfly Effect, I thought that it would be like the Cause and Effect ability from Demon the Descent. You know: You do one unrelated thing and it leads to a mind or life-changing event? The write-up seems to apply that the Boon allows you to gleam intent off a fellow Chaos user. (IMHO)</div> </div> </div> </div>Butterfly Effect is designed to allow someone who is investing into Chaos to know when either there are people being swept up in their actions, or to know when someone has been influenced by Justice. Additionally, it can also let you know when someone has been charmed, or other such abilities, but its primary function is just to let someone who has Chaos keep tabs on who is thinking properly, and who is not. Effectively, who has 'free will' at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155854#post155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saw the write-up for the Orisha. Sad to see favorites like Damballah, Erzulie, and Baron Samedi go like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is too bad that Damballah is not included in the Orisha, but he's not actually from the same Pantheon as they are. He is a God from a Pantheon of the Fon peoples, not the Yoruba. He has an entire Pantheon of fellow Gods, so that is why he is not included with the Orisha.<br /> <br /> We will have Baron up there when we write up lesser Gods, but, personally, I adore the Scholarly theory that Baron Samedi and his wife are the Irish God Samhain and Brigid given to the slaves from interactions with Irish farm workers who were coming over at the same time in one of the great Irish diasporas. Erzulie is actually in the Pantheon though, she is Oshun. Erzulie is just a different name for her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155854#post155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, the Loa of first edition was my first look into the African pantheon, so seeing Shango being the head makes me a bit apprehensive. Sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shango is 'technically' the Pantheon Head, but people don't listen to him particularly well. He gets mad about it, and will try to beat the other God or Goddess up for it (except Eshu), but he's really just King because he decided he should be and the others go along with it because it's easier. This is mostly represented as Shango having really, really, really bad Charisma, but high Manipulation.<br /> <br /> I don't remember who was the leader of the Loa in RAW, can you remind me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=155854#post155854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the Loa different from the Orisha and will we be seeing a write-up of the Loa in a future book as an alternative American pantheon to the Orisha, being that it makes me think that the Loa were actually former members of the Orisha that were thrown out by Shango and the Orisha during the Slave trade of the 1600s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the Loa are the Orisha but with different names honestly. You are entirely welcome to play the Loa and Orisha as two seperate Pantheons for that, but the Gods are pretty much all the same people, but with different names. It's pretty much the same as the Roman and Greek Gods being the same people. Shango and Ogun are the same as Shango and Oshun from the Loa, obviously. Erzuile is Oshun, Legba and Kalfu are both Eshu, and Eshu is probably happy to appear as either of them. Agwe is Olokun, though sometimes Olokun is a Goddess. It's an Orisha thing, they don't really participate in Gender that often.<br /> <br /> Baron Samedi (Lesser God), and Damballah (different Pantheon) are the only two who didn't make the transition. But, Baron is a cool guy, he will be back, don't worry about it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.ca/2013/02/the-african-face.html\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a post from the creators of the Orisha about why it is important to have the Orisha represented as their older, original version rather than the Loa (Who they can represent as well, just like Ares can be Mars, probably when they are visiting areas where they are worshiped as the Loa rather than the Orisha).<br /> <br /> If you have any other questions about the Orisha, be sure to let us know. They are very cool, having their Fate in their head, chosen at their creation, drunk creator Gods explaining why some people are ugly, it's really great.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T16:27:22-07:00","id":156077,"title":"","content":"This makes me sad that the American counterparrts, like Baron Samedi, are considered &quot;lesser gods&quot; to the other Orisha. From the way they were written up, it seemed that the Orisha and the Loa seemed to be inverted aspects of each other. The Orisha empasized war, trickery, and small community while the Loa. from what I read in first edition Scion, emphasized large community, wisdom, and love, with vengence and evil being minor aspects.<br /> <br /> As with the exclusion of Damballah because he's from a different tribal pantheon, I call that a cop-out. I remember that when tribes in the savannahs of Africa were conquered, their gods were absorbed into their own, much like the Vanir were absorbed into the Aesir. To exclude a god, even if it's a lesser god, because of which tribe he came from, would be like excluding Baldur from the Aesir because he was Vanir, and totally making Ragnarok pointless.<br /> <br /> Who knows, perhaps Damballah was the first &quot;lesser god&quot; to end up in the New World and formed the Loa to spite Shango and the Orisha who considered him a non-entity.<br /> <br /> Damballah was one of my favorite Loa in first edition Scion, and even though he's not &quot;Yoruban&quot;, he'll always be the head of the Loa to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T17:11:23-07:00","id":156093,"title":"","content":"One of the biggest reasons that we went for the Orisha is because of the research JR put into them. Scion RAW Loa weren't that well researched, and while I also miss the Loa; we would rather them be released in a supplement update with decent research and devotion instead of what we habe currently. If people want stats for the Loa, their RAW writeups should work. Also! I don't know if this is miscommunication but we are not associated with the official Scion 2ed. We're just fans with a lot of time on our hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T17:18:35-07:00","id":156098,"title":"","content":"Yes, well with the dissolution of the JSR site this 2.0 project (as well as whatever managed to migrate here to the forums) is now the most playtested and research mass of rules patches to the Scion RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T17:58:09-07:00","id":156109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156077#post156077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes me sad that the American counterparrts, like Baron Samedi, are considered &quot;lesser gods&quot; to the other Orisha. From the way they were written up, it seemed that the Orisha and the Loa seemed to be inverted aspects of each other. The Orisha empasized war, trickery, and small community while the Loa. from what I read in first edition Scion, emphasized large community, wisdom, and love, with vengence and evil being minor aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is a difference in values, but it was likely caused by the sudden traumatic shift the culture experienced with the Triangle Trade, and, of course, cultural evolution and some cross-cultural pollination with Christianity. Just like with the Romans and Greeks, the interpretations of the Gods were drastcically different. For example, the Roman Ares and Aphrodite were far less childish and were incredibly helpful and supportive Deities compaired to their Greek counterparts.<br /> <br /> You are entirely welcome to run the Orisha in any way you would like, taking any of the ideas mentioned here, or anything else. The Orisha Pantheon is just a representation of them Pre-Contact, just as the Tuatha are Pre-Contact, and the Theoi are Pre-Roman. We prefer to take a snap shot of the Pantheon at the height of their independent culture, so that is why the Orisha are represented as they are on the site.<br /> <br /> In your own games, you could rule that the Orisha have changed their ways, totally, go for it. I would be happy to help you work some of that stuff out, though I wouldn't be as helpful as I could be with the Irish, who are my expertise.<br /> <br /> As for Baron, we don't really have any true myths from him, so while he is incredibly cool, and a really interesting figure, we just can't rationalize him being on equal footing with these figures who are far older, and we have a large amount of myths about displaying great feats of power.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Baron is the only one of the 'American' Loa who we have ruled as a Lesser God. All the other Loa asides from Damballa are Gods of the Orisha. Damballa is just a Major God from a different root culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156077#post156077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As with the exclusion of Damballah because he's from a different tribal pantheon, I call that a cop-out. I remember that when tribes in the savannahs of Africa were conquered, their gods were absorbed into their own, much like the Vanir were absorbed into the Aesir. To exclude a god, even if it's a lesser god, because of which tribe he came from, would be like excluding Baldur from the Aesir because he was Vanir, and totally making Ragnarok pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very sorry if we have offended you, but this is just how we have chosen to represent the Orisha.<br /> <br /> Damballah is a Major God of his Pantheon I am fairly sure, but he is from an entirely seperate Pantheon, from a separate culture. The Vanir and Aesir were worshiped at the same time by the same culture, while the Yoruban people never worshiped Damballah, he was worshiped by his own culture, which was very separate. While there are some examples of Gods being worshiped cross-cultures, such as Lugh, Damballah was not a God of the Yoruba. And, since we have chosen to specifically represent the Orisha as they were pre-contact, he is not involved. It would be much like including Lugh in the Aesir.<br /> <br /> You are entirely welcome to represent him in whatever way you would like, and not use the Orisha we have represented on our site, it's entirely fine. But, this is just how we have specifically chosen to run it in our own games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156077#post156077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who knows, perhaps Damballah was the first &quot;lesser god&quot; to end up in the New World and formed the Loa to spite Shango and the Orisha who considered him a non-entity.<br /> <br /> Damballah was one of my favorite Loa in first edition Scion, and even though he's not &quot;Yoruban&quot;, he'll always be the head of the Loa to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I never, ever said Damballah was a Lesser God. I said he was from an entirely different culture, I am very sorry if I did not manage to explain that properly. You are entirely welcome, as I ave said, to run him in whatever way you would like for your own game though. Don't let our own fun spoil yours, we would never want that. I really am truely sorry if we have managed to offend you though.<br /> <br /> I hope that explanation helps Jackalope.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe one day we will write up Damballah's Pantheon in order to have more African Pantheons (Though we would prefer to hit East Africa first to have a more even spread of two North [Elohim not up yet], one West, one East), but, for now, he is not one of the Orisha for us. He's just from a different Pantheon. You are, again, totally able to run him however you would like, and if I can help you at all with that, just ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-01-2014, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:14:34-07:00","id":156115,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I'm sorry for the rant. My first impression of Shango, thanks to first edition Scion as the Loa of Vengence, made me think he also had the title of God of Black Supremists. And the fact that he's the actual head of the African pantheon made me think that this pantheon was run by a racist asshole. Still, not all the Orishans are bad and I would be happy to try out a Scion of Esha or any of the elemental gods. Again sorry for the tantrum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:31:56-07:00","id":156119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156115#post156115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I'm sorry for the rant. My first impression of Shango, thanks to first edition Scion as the Loa of Vengence, made me think he also had the title of God of Black Supremists. And the fact that he's the actual head of the African pantheon made me think that this pantheon was run by a racist asshole. Still, not all the Orishans are bad and I would be happy to try out a Scion of Esha or any of the elemental gods. Again sorry for the tantrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I can totally understand that they are close to your heart.<br /> <br /> You should totally read Shango's real myths. He is a serious hot head, and has some Vengeance issues (but not more so than the rest of his Pantheon. Eshu is worse though.), but is actually quite brilliant. I doubt Shango would really have much to do with the Supremicy of anyone but himself. He's got that thing the Storm Kings all got, you know, the &quot;I am the Greatest and everyone else clearly sucks for the fatal flaw of not being me.&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> He would actually be one of the coolest Divine Parents I think, assuming you don't get any ideas of overthrowing him. He takes that really badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:35:57-07:00","id":156121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156115#post156115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I'm sorry for the rant. My first impression of Shango, thanks to first edition Scion as the Loa of Vengence, made me think he also had the title of God of Black Supremists. And the fact that he's the actual head of the African pantheon made me think that this pantheon was run by a racist asshole. Still, not all the Orishans are bad and I would be happy to try out a Scion of Esha or any of the elemental gods. Again sorry for the tantrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Supremacy Movement Shango would ever have interactions with is the Shango Supremacy Movement, for he is the most manly and handsome of the gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T18:39:09-07:00","id":156122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156121#post156121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only Supremacy Movement Shango would ever have interactions with is the Shango Supremacy Movement, for he is the most manly and handsome of the gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least until Eshu shows up and clears his throat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T21:14:03-07:00","id":156229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>griffinguy24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156122#post156122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least until Eshu shows up and clears his throat</div> </div> </div> </div>True! Not everyone can use their phallus as a giant bridge for people to cross a river. Just a shame he went flaccid half way through and many of them drowned. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T05:08:55-07:00","id":156400,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, I am really enjoying reading the guides and retainers section. It's a nice bite of mythology there. Thank you for taking the time to create it, and put it up for us.<br /> <br /> And holy shit! The new chaos is going to be a rockstar at my table!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T09:54:06-07:00","id":156623,"title":"","content":"I can see the arguments for replacing the Loa with the Orisha, made both here and by John &amp; Anne, but it seems like there is a real opportunity being missed here. (Not mind you, that it is one that I think can, or even should, really be capitalized on when you are overhauling things from the ground up). Namely the formation of new(er) pantheons.<br /> <br /> Loa are explicitly divided into nanchons. It seems like an easy fix to USE that and say the Petro Loa are the Orishas in their new world masks. But then there are the Rada. Explicitly younger, often angrier and different (mostly) from the Petro. How about having the Rada be an example of a new pantheon that formed in the wake of a significant event? The &quot;duplicate&quot; deities, aren't. They are examples of children of the older Orisha/Petro. Which can seem a little weird in some cases - Erzulie Danto (Rada) seems like she should be older than Erzulie Freda/Oshun (Petro), but considering their different foci, it makes perfect sense that they would do so. <br /> <br /> Then we have a group of Legend 12 Gods that were actually Scions that made it up through the ranks as it were. As many players (and to a degree, the developers) envision their own Scions doing. In fact, that might explain the Loa that are not Orisha derived. (Like Damballah). They are &quot;joiners&quot; from other pantheons (or gods with an inter-pantheon presence, which is another topic entirely). That would even go to explaining the other nanchons. They are obviously derived from the mythologies of other cultures than the Yoruba. Might they be like the Petro? Explicitly those Gods with New World faces? Or like the Rada? Newly ascended Scions that are the children of non-Orisha African Gods associated with enslaved peoples from non-Yoruba peoples?<br /> <br /> The big outlier is, of course, the Ghede meaning the good Barons, Mamman Brigitte. I so don't buy this &quot;Celtic immigrant theory&quot;. It's super bad from a comparative myth standpoint and wouldn't even past a basic sniff test AT ALL if it weren't for the &quot;Where the Hell do they come from?&quot; problem with the Ghede. Irish immigrants sharing the very few and fragmentary stories about at least one pretty vague hero myth? It seems MUCH more likely that, if the Irish immigrants (which weren't really in the right time and place to even have had this effect at all on voodoun as it was forming) would have reinforced the Catholic Saint attributions. (Brigit and Brigitte being the same? Isn't it more likely at one remove that Brigit is the same as St. Brigid who is identified with someone else who is Mamman Brigitte? Both Gods being deliberately confused for the same non-God as a mask for very separate mythic identities and roles with a few similarities in common?). So where do the Ghede come from, Scion-wise? Well there are some Orisha gods like the Ghede that get left out in the wash.... Sopona/Shapona/Omulu/Babalu-Aye, the god of smallpox. He is definitely a dark guy and not really &quot;lesser deity&quot; kind of stuff. Or, maybe the Ghede are some new gods born from the Titan/Primal force of Death? Things were definitely bad enough for the slaves that Death titanspawn would have been... interested. Interested enough to get their destinies entangled with mortals and become less Aspects and more Fatebound Gods? Interested enough to spawn a few children with some mortals who ascended alongside their Rada contemporaries/allies? A combination of the two (Ex. the Baron and Mamman Brigitte from category two and Papa Ghede from category one)?<br /> <br /> An aside: IMO, saying that Lugh is Llew is Lug is NOT the same as saying Ares is Mars. Lugh and Llew don't have even vaguely similar roles, stories or functions. We know really close to next to nothing about Lug. Are they related in a cultural sense? Sure, just like Zeus, Indra, Thor and Tarhunt are - though the split is newer and the cultures are chronologically and culturally closer together. We shouldn't confuse linguistic similarity and misty past connections for identifying them as the same person. Being the child of Lugh would be a connection with very very different stories and attributions (and related game mechanics) than children of Llew. It does a disservice on the order of replacing the Orisha with the Loa to equate them all. Or worse. <br /> <br /> Now Mannanan and Manawydan being the same guy.... that I will listen to and can make a case for... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:32:29-07:00","id":156771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156623#post156623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see the arguments for replacing the Loa with the Orisha, made both here and by John &amp; Anne, but it seems like there is a real opportunity being missed here. (Not mind you, that it is one that I think can, or even should, really be capitalized on when you are overhauling things from the ground up). Namely the formation of new(er) pantheons.<br /> <br /> Loa are explicitly divided into nanchons. It seems like an easy fix to USE that and say the Petro Loa are the Orishas in their new world masks. But then there are the Rada. Explicitly younger, often angrier and different (mostly) from the Petro. How about having the Rada be an example of a new pantheon that formed in the wake of a significant event? The &quot;duplicate&quot; deities, aren't. They are examples of children of the older Orisha/Petro. Which can seem a little weird in some cases - Erzulie Danto (Rada) seems like she should be older than Erzulie Freda/Oshun (Petro), but considering their different foci, it makes perfect sense that they would do so.<br /> <br /> Then we have a group of Legend 12 Gods that were actually Scions that made it up through the ranks as it were. As many players (and to a degree, the developers) envision their own Scions doing. In fact, that might explain the Loa that are not Orisha derived. (Like Damballah). They are &quot;joiners&quot; from other pantheons (or gods with an inter-pantheon presence, which is another topic entirely). That would even go to explaining the other nanchons. They are obviously derived from the mythologies of other cultures than the Yoruba. Might they be like the Petro? Explicitly those Gods with New World faces? Or like the Rada? Newly ascended Scions that are the children of non-Orisha African Gods associated with enslaved peoples from non-Yoruba peoples?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an absolutely brilliant idea Ajax, and I am sure it could be something that could shine in a game that someone devotes the main theme to exploring these differences between the cultures. I think examining things like the Orisha / Loa split, the Theoi / Deorum, and the Deva / Yazata (the largest of them, I would wager) in games is fascinating. I really would love to see a game centered around the Deva / Yazata divide, I am sure the Divine Politics would be amazing, especially with the suspicious few figures who seem to appear on both sides.<br /> <br /> But, currently, we are intending to keep the website as pure mythology. I have been thinking of doing a section of the site for story hooks though, and I think that would be an excellent one to put up there when I eventually get around to that. Assuming you are alright with me using your idea, of course. But, for that fact, we are probably going to keep the Orisha as they are, also for the fact that we already have a ton of stuff on our plate at the moment and taking on a Pantheon Revision at the same time as redesigning all of the Epics and Purviews and Pantheon Specific Purviews may kill us.<br /> <br /> I was going to mention Damballah possibly being one of those Gods who just pokes his head into other cultures. Like how the Bogovi talk about Thor being Thor, and the Romans mention a &quot;Crow Goddess of War&quot; or something along the lines of that in regards to the Gauls off being Gauls. I think looking at those Gods in the light of Scion would be something very cool, and also something that happens frequently when you have cross-Pantheon Bands that reach Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Still, lovely idea Ajax.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156623#post156623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big outlier is, of course, the Ghede meaning the good Barons, Mamman Brigitte. I so don't buy this &quot;Celtic immigrant theory&quot;. It's super bad from a comparative myth standpoint and wouldn't even past a basic sniff test AT ALL if it weren't for the &quot;Where the Hell do they come from?&quot; problem with the Ghede. Irish immigrants sharing the very few and fragmentary stories about at least one pretty vague hero myth? It seems MUCH more likely that, if the Irish immigrants (which weren't really in the right time and place to even have had this effect at all on voodoun as it was forming) would have reinforced the Catholic Saint attributions. (Brigit and Brigitte being the same? Isn't it more likely at one remove that Brigit is the same as St. Brigid who is identified with someone else who is Mamman Brigitte? Both Gods being deliberately confused for the same non-God as a mask for very separate mythic identities and roles with a few similarities in common?).</div> </div> </div> </div>The theory that Baron and Madam Brigitte are the results of a cross cultural exchange is one that I don't really buy into academically, but one I adore for Scion, for an explanation about Baron's existence. Though, it is not going to be anything but a possible rumor put up on his God Page when we eventually do Lesser Gods so people can chose to use it, or ignore it as they want. There are a number of theories that are kind of dodgy in a academic sense, but are lovely for stories in Scion. Such as Conall Cernach's possible somehow connection to Cernunnos which I've still not decided if I like or not from a real world standpoint, but think it is a very cool little tidbit that could be used in Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156623#post156623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An aside: IMO, saying that Lugh is Llew is Lug is NOT the same as saying Ares is Mars. Lugh and Llew don't have even vaguely similar roles, stories or functions. We know really close to next to nothing about Lug. Are they related in a cultural sense? Sure, just like Zeus, Indra, Thor and Tarhunt are - though the split is newer and the cultures are chronologically and culturally closer together. We shouldn't confuse linguistic similarity and misty past connections for identifying them as the same person. Being the child of Lugh would be a connection with very very different stories and attributions (and related game mechanics) than children of Llew. It does a disservice on the order of replacing the Orisha with the Loa to equate them all. Or worse.<br /> <br /> Now Mannanan and Manawydan being the same guy.... that I will listen to and can make a case for... )</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, Llew was a God is incredibly different from the Irish Lugh, though I'm fairly sure they both get raised by Manannan and Manawydan respectively. Though, it has been ages since I looked at the branches and my knowledge of them is really horrible. I hope one day we will write up the Welsh, and then he will very definatly be a different God. Not sure about Manannan, as you said, though. He's problematic.<br /> <br /> I should have probably used Mithra or Epona as a cross cultural Deity, but I had the Irish on my head from rearranging a bookshelf of my Irish Mythology reference books and I just defaulted to him. As I said before, The Morrigan may also have been one, since you don't get a lot of battlefield frenzy crow Goddesses who are not her or one of her aspects. But, that falls issue to the whole problem of the Gauls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:40:53-07:00","id":156779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156400#post156400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, I am really enjoying reading the guides and retainers section. It's a nice bite of mythology there. Thank you for taking the time to create it, and put it up for us.<br /> <br /> And holy shit! The new chaos is going to be a rockstar at my table!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am very glad you like it Charles. I really enjoyed writing up the Guides and Retainers, I mostly did it to relax after working on the other things. I hope to do something similar for Relics soon, and if anyone has any suggestions for mythological items they would like to see up there, just post them here and I will try to fit them in. Since I am horrible at true mechanics, I am mostly going to be on the bench working on little projects while Aynie and Iry work out the Purviews and Knacks, so, don't worry that any manpower is going to be lost in me doing that.<br /> <br /> Also, please let us know what you think of Chaos after seeing it in use, we are very proud of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-02-2014, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T12:50:16-07:00","id":156836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156771#post156771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is an absolutely brilliant idea Ajax, and I am sure it could be something that could shine in a game that someone devotes the main theme to exploring these differences between the cultures. I think examining things like the Orisha / Loa split, the Theoi / Deorum, and the Deva / Yazata (the largest of them, I would wager) in games is fascinating. I really would love to see a game centered around the Deva / Yazata divide, I am sure the Divine Politics would be amazing, especially with the suspicious few figures who seem to appear on both sides.<br /> <br /> But, currently, we are intending to keep the website as pure mythology. I have been thinking of doing a section of the site for story hooks though, and I think that would be an excellent one to put up there when I eventually get around to that. Assuming you are alright with me using your idea, of course. But, for that fact, we are probably going to keep the Orisha as they are, also for the fact that we already have a ton of stuff on our plate at the moment and taking on a Pantheon Revision at the same time as redesigning all of the Epics and Purviews and Pantheon Specific Purviews may kill us.<br /> <br /> I was going to mention Damballah possibly being one of those Gods who just pokes his head into other cultures. Like how the Bogovi talk about Thor being Thor, and the Romans mention a &quot;Crow Goddess of War&quot; or something along the lines of that in regards to the Gauls off being Gauls. I think looking at those Gods in the light of Scion would be something very cool, and also something that happens frequently when you have cross-Pantheon Bands that reach Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Still, lovely idea Ajax.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It's yours and everybody else's. Posting on an open forum means throwing out there for everyone to do with it what they will. No worries. <br /> <br /> If it was my dissertation topic, I'd be jealously guarding. And then my advisor would probably steal it anyways. Wait! That already happened....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156771#post156771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The theory that Baron and Madam Brigitte are the results of a cross cultural exchange is one that I don't really buy into academically, but one I adore for Scion, for an explanation about Baron's existence. Though, it is not going to be anything but a possible rumor put up on his God Page when we eventually do Lesser Gods so people can chose to use it, or ignore it as they want. There are a number of theories that are kind of dodgy in a academic sense, but are lovely for stories in Scion. Such as Conall Cernach's possible somehow connection to Cernunnos which I've still not decided if I like or not from a real world standpoint, but think it is a very cool little tidbit that could be used in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still viscerally hate it. I don't know why. It just seems so implausible on so many levels and seems to diminish everyone involved. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156771#post156771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, Llew was a God is incredibly different from the Irish Lugh, though I'm fairly sure they both get raised by Manannan and Manawydan respectively. Though, it has been ages since I looked at the branches and my knowledge of them is really horrible. I hope one day we will write up the Welsh, and then he will very definatly be a different God. Not sure about Manannan, as you said, though. He's problematic..</div> </div> </div> </div>Llew was raised by Gwydion after that whole premie birth thing, shoved into a box until he was due, etc. etc. <br /> <br /> Manannan sure seems like he could be Manawydan who just got fed up with how things had gone in Wales and relocated to the Isle of Man (or made it). Then got caught up in the Tuatha De crap. It even links into what they say in Companion, that he's a god from a different pantheon who is strongly associated. After what happened to Ireland with that mess with his sister, I can see why he might feel he owed these new kids something. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T13:40:46-07:00","id":156885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156836#post156836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. It's yours and everybody else's. Posting on an open forum means throwing out there for everyone to do with it what they will. No worries.<br /> <br /> If it was my dissertation topic, I'd be jealously guarding. And then my advisor would probably steal it anyways. Wait! That already happened....</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I'm very sorry to hear that Ajax. Unfortunately, that is not as uncommon as it should be and isn't policed properly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156836#post156836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still viscerally hate it. I don't know why. It just seems so implausible on so many levels and seems to diminish everyone involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eah, someone may like it. Stranger things have happened in our crazy history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156836#post156836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Manannan sure seems like he could be Manawydan who just got fed up with how things had gone in Wales and relocated to the Isle of Man (or made it). Then got caught up in the Tuatha De crap. It even links into what they say in Companion, that he's a god from a different pantheon who is strongly associated. After what happened to Ireland with that mess with his sister, I can see why he might feel he owed these new kids something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of Companion's stuff is so weird for the Tuatha, though they are right tecnically that he is not a member of the same Tuath (family/clan) that the Tuatha de Danann are from. The way I have actually seen it explained In-Universe is that Manannan got more involved with the Welsh after CuChulain and Fand had their affair, since in Welsh mythology he is married to Rhiannon.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T16:30:02-07:00","id":157039,"title":"","content":"The new website looks pretty good. Why did you guys go with the old art instead of the fancy new art JSR uses?<br /> Not the pictures in the circles. Those are awesome. But the god pictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:00:22-07:00","id":157084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=156885#post156885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Some of Companion's stuff is so weird for the Tuatha, though they are right tecnically that he is not a member of the same Tuath (family/clan) that the Tuatha de Danann are from. The way I have actually seen it explained In-Universe is that Manannan got more involved with the Welsh after CuChulain and Fand had their affair, since in Welsh mythology he is married to Rhiannon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... I can't see it going that direction. <br /> <br /> The Mabinogi has Manawydan hanging out with his family. As in brothers and sisters. The people he grew up with. That argues for origin not immigration. <br /> <br /> He has a big adventure with his brothers in Ireland which leads to everyone there dying. Which sounds like the things that happen regularly in the Book of Invasions, arguing that that whole thing came about before the Fir Bolg or the Tuatha De showed up. In fact, pretty much HAS to, since there aren't any of those plagues that devastated the inhabitants of Ireland after the Sons of the Partholon and the Sons of Nemed. Essentially an argument that Matholwch was a King of Ireland during one of those two periods or he was a Fomorian.<br /> <br /> Then he marries Rhiannon. Who picks and chooses her husbands and gets rid of suitors and lovers (and husbands?) whenever she feels like it. Maybe she just didn't want to move to the Isle of Man? Maybe he moved to the Isle of Man when she rejected/replaced him? Maybe she has another name amongst the Tuatha? Maybe Rhiannon IS Fand... After all, going after Cuchulain, a young strong virile warrior seems SO like the same woman who went after Pwll....<br /> <br /> In fact, maybe Mannanan is trying to help out in Ireland BECAUSE of the crap that went down in Ireland that was so bad there were only seven survivors. Maybe he has some real or sense of obligation.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, Manannan fools around too, with Caintige. He has another wife Aine, who is also alleged to be his daughter. (Hopefully foster-daughter... probably, in fact, since her father is elsewhere listed as Egobail, who is listed as a foster-son of Manannan, multi-generational fosterage perhaps?)<br /> <br /> There's also some other linguistic, archaeological, etc. evidence that indicates one over the other, but that's technical crap that probably only appeals to someone like me.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:29:34-07:00","id":157130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157039#post157039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new website looks pretty good. Why did you guys go with the old art instead of the fancy new art JSR uses?<br /> Not the pictures in the circles. Those are awesome. But the god pictures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Half of it was because of copyright issues; and the other half of it was that we don't actually like Genzoman's art for the gods. Sure, some are great, but it's a bit too much T&amp;A and not enough mythical representation. Not to mention site storage. Google Sites isn't very keen on massive image repositories. Perhaps in time we'll migrate over to somewhere else if there's a need.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T17:59:50-07:00","id":157148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157039#post157039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new website looks pretty good. Why did you guys go with the old art instead of the fancy new art JSR uses?<br /> Not the pictures in the circles. Those are awesome. But the god pictures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We will, hopefully, one day go through and use some lovely art for all of the Gods and Goddesses. Unfortunately, this is going to take a lot of time, and we decided to spend our time hashing out mechanics instead. It's one of the many things I want to do in my numerous 'small' projects. The Orisha, Tuatha, Bogovi, and Yazata are the most difficult to find proper period pictures of, since their cultures didn't really do much of it, much of it hasn't been digitized, or much of it was destroyed.<br /> <br /> If we could have all ancient art, I would be going for that angle, but those four just break the pattern. So, eventually, we will try for all new art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T18:59:47-07:00","id":157250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157084#post157084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some other linguistic, archaeological, etc. evidence that indicates one over the other, but that's technical crap that probably only appeals to someone like me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely appeals to me! I know you are just proposing a fan theory about how events between the Welsh and the Irish may have gone down, but I would love to see a bunch of evidence that might support that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T19:18:35-07:00","id":157288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157084#post157084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some other linguistic, archaeological, etc. evidence that indicates one over the other, but that's technical crap that probably only appeals to someone like me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with Twich. If you have any of that on hand, I would love to read it. I spent yesterday relaxing after a month of working on the site by reading some essays about Cernunnos' and his strange absence from Ireland. I'm a horrible dork, and I love to read interesting stuff like that.<br /> <br /> But, if it would be any trouble for you to get your hands on it, no worries. If it's behind a pay wall, toss me the info and I will try to see if it's in my University's online library's resources.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T08:03:43-07:00","id":157857,"title":"","content":"So it looks like you guys are throwing out Dying Boxes, is that right? I see bashing and lethal are aesthetic choices for players, while filling your Health Boxes with Aggravated Damage up to your incap box is what kills you. Why this change?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:06:56-07:00","id":157907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157857#post157857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it looks like you guys are throwing out Dying Boxes, is that right? I see bashing and lethal are aesthetic choices for players, while filling your Health Boxes with Aggravated Damage up to your incap box is what kills you. Why this change?</div> </div> </div> </div>No single overwhelming reason inspired the change, but a large number of small reasons that began to add up!<ul><li>Dying Boxes were a strange mechanic that showed up almost nowhere else.</li> <li>Dying Boxes were equal to your mundane stamina only, which means someone with Stamina 5 had the same amount as someone with Stamina 5 / Epic Stamina 5, which did not make sense.</li> <li>Dying boxes were mysteriously immune to bashing damage, even if it was a mighty giant smashing you with a club twenty times the size of your body.</li> <li>Dying boxes were mysteriously immune to the attack that put you into the dying state. You could take ten billion damage in one attack and it would still only reduce you to dying. This is actually kind of awesome in a way, but also makes no sense.</li> <li>Dying boxes were healed whenever anyone stabilized you, and there was no limit to how many times someone could be brought back and forth between incapacitated and dying. The difficulty to stabilize becomes trivial at demigod.</li> <li>Dying boxes were lost at a rate of one every action, but the roll to stop bleeding is reflexive and trivial, which created a strange rules conflict.</li> </ul>These are just a few of the issues with Dying Boxes. While any one or two of them could easily be fixed, you had to be a rules lawyer to keep track of them all!<br /> <br /> Changing the point of death to <b>'Full Aggravated'</b> goes a long way towards cleaning up and addressing many of these issues. The rule is much smoother to use and easier to remember; it uses established mechanics that players are familiar with; you can actually be killed by someone smashing you into paste; people can be killed by a single overwhelming attack; bashing and lethal damage actually have a harder time killing you now, you cannot be infinitely stabilized, etc.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that this works in tandem with the new rules on aggravated damage only reducing your Soak DV by 1/2!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:09:26-07:00","id":157910,"title":"","content":"I confess that after reading Jim Butcher's take on him in his latest book, I like the less negative tone towards Hades. Rather refreshing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:12:31-07:00","id":157917,"title":"","content":"I feel that everything you said should remarkably affect what Damage Conversion, Divine Damage Conversion, and Unbreakable do as Knacks. How can we House Rule them to make them, well, useful again (especially Damage Conversion)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:38:12-07:00","id":157965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157917#post157917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that everything you said should remarkably affect what Damage Conversion, Divine Damage Conversion, and Unbreakable do as Knacks. How can we House Rule them to make them, well, useful again (especially Damage Conversion)?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Unbreakable</b> is already an incredibly useful knack, since there is no limit on the amount of legend you can invest towards soaking something if you want to be extremely epic about it. It also has functionality above Self-Healing because it naturally mitigates &quot;Bad Touch&quot; effects, such as poisons and drugs getting into your bloodstream, magical injuries that resist being healed, some horrible creature laying eggs in you, or other dreadful consequences that taking damage might cause.<br /> <br /> <b>Divine Damage Conversion</b> also remains powerful, because aggravated damage is twice as effective as lethal damage, and three times as effective as bashing damage at making you dead. Just reducing aggravated down to lethal means you are going to be able to take twice as much damage, unless you are right at the point where any lethal you take is spilling over into aggravated anyway. Of course, reducing the damage from aggravated to lethal means the attack no longer causes you to suffer 1/2 Soak DV. This is not a big deal if you are also heavily invested in Epic Dexterity, but can mean an enormous difference to someone with Epic Stamina as their primary defense.<br /> <br /> <b>Damage Conversion</b> does need to be investigated. While it does a good job making your enemies have to deal twice as much lethal damage to take you down, once you get to the point where bashing damage is spilling over into lethal it ceases to be useful. It also does not perform double duty protecting you from having your Soak DV reduced the way that Divine Damage Conversion does. Damage Conversion is still completely playable, but it could use a splash of something to make it special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:50:57-07:00","id":157975,"title":"","content":"But even reducing lethal to bashing in general is sort of useless with the new rules. I feel like it should ignore a level or two of bashing/lethal per legend spent, or something of the sort.<br /> <br /> Also, with Retainers, we're having trouble reconciling their mundane attributes for the sake of roleplaying. It seems that if the retainer has 5 dots, all of its mundane attributes would be treated as having 8 dots. This will usually make the retainer better in everything than the Scion, which doesn't make sense roleplaying-wise if it's, say, a white-tailed deer, a child, or a flock of seagulls. And we need a way to stat retainers mostly for purposes of roleplaying them. So far, I've just said to make the retainer make sense for its legend and what the player wants it to be like, but something more concrete would be better, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:19:14-07:00","id":157994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157975#post157975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even reducing lethal to bashing in general is sort of useless with the new rules. I feel like it should ignore a level or two of bashing/lethal per legend spent, or something of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I made my first combat monster underneath the new rules, I distinctlyt remember telling Iry the same thing. &quot;What's the point of ever reducing lethal?&quot; Then we ran the first combat scene, and let me tell you, the ability to have 7+ Health levels because you've knocked an attack down from lethal to bashing has saved my character a dozen times over. Attacks that would kill her now leave her battered but alive enough to pull through.<br /> <br /> Reducing an attack to bashing is essentially granting yourself the entirely of your health pool to soak an attack. A character with Epic Stamina 2 has 9 Health Levels of Bashing, of Lethal, and (finally) of Aggravated that must be filled up before they die. This, in Scion 2.0, makes Aggravated horrifically powerful as it is THE attack you use if you want someone dead.<br /> <br /> As an attacker, you want your attacks to matter. As the defender, you want as much protection as you can get, and those health boxes are the final line of defense. Trust me, Reducing Damage to Bashing is a beeeeeautiful thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157975#post157975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, with Retainers, we're having trouble reconciling their mundane attributes for the sake of roleplaying. It seems that if the retainer has 5 dots, all of its mundane attributes would be treated as having 8 dots. This will usually make the retainer better in everything than the Scion, which doesn't make sense roleplaying-wise if it's, say, a white-tailed deer, a child, or a flock of seagulls. And we need a way to stat retainers mostly for purposes of roleplaying them. So far, I've just said to make the retainer make sense for its legend and what the player wants it to be like, but something more concrete would be better, I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Retainer at 5 dots only has the maximum amount of mundane attributes for the Epic(s) chosen for it. Lemme go hunt down a retainer at 5 dots that I've used and has been roleplayed.... aha. Here. <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ament / \u201cAmy\u201d</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sasha found Amy as an abandoned pup on the outskirts of Giza in the aftermath of a firefight</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Dice</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: 16 on Skilled Rolls / 8 on Other Rolls</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Epics: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Epic Dexterity, Epic Intelligence</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Purviews:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Skilled Abilities</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Stealth and Survival</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Powers: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cat\u2019s Grace, Language Mastery</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Perks</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Twin Sight: </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sasha might not be able to understand Ament (or Amy, as she calls her) but for some reason Sasha can see whatever the little she-jackal sees.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Descendant of Anubis: </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If killed, Ament resurrects herself at the nearest graveyard, becoming reformed from the shadows of the headstones.</span></span><br /> <br /> Now, Amy the Jackal was a cunning little brat who liked to trick people into thinking she was actually a physical manifestation of Anubis. Why? Because it amused her. Because I did not chose Epic Manipulation for her, she only gets to roll 8 dice on such trickery. 8 dice. That's it. The actual meat and gristle of her attributes+abilities doesn't matter because as a Retainer, she doesn't have them.<br /> <br /> The only Attributes that you can &quot;count&quot; towards being topped off for Amy is her Dexterity and her Intelligence. The rest is probably average to low. It does take some getting used to, but roleplaying the retainer off of the skilld abilities and chosen perks/epics is one of the easier ways to do it. Mundanely-statting them just isn't possible within the system.<br /> <br /> We run retainers for the sense they should be for the system, but if players want concrete, then run the retainers by their skills/epics. If a Retainer has Manipulation associated, then they're going to be extremely crafty. If they've got Epic Intelligence, then they're smart (and in Amy's case, snobbish). <br /> <br /> Iry can step in on both of these to elaborate, and Watcher can go even further with Retainers as Zoe was one for his character for an incredibly long time and can talk about how she was roleplayed and depicted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:37:13-07:00","id":158030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157975#post157975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even reducing lethal to bashing in general is sort of useless with the new rules. I feel like it should ignore a level or two of bashing/lethal per legend spent, or something of the sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring a level or two of bashing/lethal is exactly what we are playtesting right now. I recommend giving it a try at your own table and we can compare notes to see how well it works out. One of our goals for the Scion 2.0 Project is combining as many of the best practices that we can, and that includes listening to other groups.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157975#post157975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, with Retainers, we're having trouble reconciling their mundane attributes for the sake of roleplaying. It seems that if the retainer has 5 dots, all of its mundane attributes would be treated as having 8 dots. This will usually make the retainer better in everything than the Scion, which doesn't make sense roleplaying-wise if it's, say, a white-tailed deer, a child, or a flock of seagulls. And we need a way to stat retainers mostly for purposes of roleplaying them. So far, I've just said to make the retainer make sense for its legend and what the player wants it to be like, but something more concrete would be better, I'm sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Retainers function on a broad thematic level instead of having a lot of crunch. When the story calls for them, they step into the spotlight and shine almost as bright as the Scion themselves. When the story does not call for them, they fade into the background and add color or commentary to a scene.<br /> <br /> Retainers have their unskilled dice as attributes <b>ONLY</b> when mechanically necessary. At all other times they have whatever is most thematic for them to have, including whatever the player envisioned for the Retainer. You are absolutely right that a Retainer should be roleplayed in whatever way makes the most sense. Mechanically necessary applies to things like calculating movement speed, Dodge DV, Soak DV, and Mental DV.<br /> <br /> To give you an example, a Retainer 5 is going to be pretty powerful compared to a starting Hero (this was also true in RAW, by the way). A beautiful swan skilled in integrity and presence would have the following stats when travelling with a Legend 2 Hero: \u200bMove 8, Dash 14, Dodge DV 4, Soak DV 4, and Mental DV a rocking 11. However, the beautiful swan is going to be as intelligent as the player wishes. It could be no smarter than an average swan, or it could be as smart as an average human because it was blessed that way by a god, or was a human to begin with that was transformed into an animal, or it could be far smarter than any human.<br /> <br /> In a sense, you can think of their mundane attributes as roleplaying <b>MAXIMUMS</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T15:10:56-07:00","id":158326,"title":"","content":"The bits about Retainers help a lot, thanks!<br /> <br /> With your current system, we're going to try Damage Conversion like this: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spend one legend and reduce bashing/lethal damage by your dots in Epic Stamina</span></span></span><br /> <br /> But we're still having some trouble with getting rid of Dying boxes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dying Boxes were a strange mechanic that showed up almost nowhere else.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by this? I'm not too sure it matters if other games do this, unless &quot;nowhere else&quot; means something different.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dying Boxes were equal to your mundane stamina only, which means someone with Stamina 5 had the same amount as someone with Stamina 5 / Epic Stamina 5, which did not make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>JSR house ruled long ago that your Dying Boxes are the sum of your dots in mundane Stamina and your dots in Epic Stamina, so this has been a non-issue.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dying boxes were mysteriously immune to bashing damage, even if it was a mighty giant smashing you with a club twenty times the size of your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not... exactly. If you continued taking bashing damage after filling all your boxes with it, it began stacking to lethal damage, AND you were unconscious.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dying boxes were mysteriously immune to the attack that put you into the dying state. You could take ten billion damage in one attack and it would still only reduce you to dying. This is actually kind of awesome in a way, but also makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/06/agg-damage.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> blog post, it seems JSR did allow for damage to continue into the dying boxes. The ST in my current game has that happen, too, so we sort of took care of it already.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dying boxes were healed whenever anyone stabilized you, and there was no limit to how many times someone could be brought back and forth between incapacitated and dying. The difficulty to stabilize becomes trivial at demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this a problem? We actually had a player die because our healer was out cold and nobody knew how to stabilize in character. Plus, it'll always take somebody's action or at least their time to do it, so it's always a choice. Do you want your players to die? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dying boxes were lost at a rate of one every action, but the roll to stop bleeding is reflexive and trivial, which created a strange rules conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, here's the Bleeding rule from Scion: Hero.<br /> <br /> Bleeding: A character who takes a lethal or<br /> aggravated wound is bleeding. Over time, significant<br /> blood loss can be just as deadly as being stabbed another<br /> couple of times. Unless a character (or a friend) binds<br /> the wound to stop the bleeding, the character loses<br /> another level of lethal damage every (Stamina) minutes.<br /> Stanching a wound requires a (Wits + Medicine) roll at<br /> difficulty equal to the number of lethal or aggravated<br /> levels associated with that wound. <b>A player of a Scion<br /> may make a (Stamina + Fortitude) roll at difficulty 2<br /> to stop his character\u2019s own bleeding. Doing so is an<br /> involuntary, reflexive action a character performs on<br /> her normal action.</b> Mortals, on the other hand, need<br /> attention, lest they bleed to death.<br /> <br /> I even bolded the part that the writers had bold in the book. Since it takes an action to do this, and an incapacitated player cannot perform any actions, they also cannot stop their own bleeding. So there is no rules conflict at all, the way I see it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=157907#post157907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing the point of death to <b>'Full Aggravated'</b> goes a long way towards cleaning up and addressing many of these issues. The rule is much smoother to use and easier to remember; it uses established mechanics that players are familiar with; you can actually be killed by someone smashing you into paste; people can be killed by a single overwhelming attack; bashing and lethal damage actually have a harder time killing you now, you cannot be infinitely stabilized, etc.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that this works in tandem with the new rules on aggravated damage only reducing your Soak DV by 1/2!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think doing this actually makes it even easier for players to die. In your system, there's no recourse. Your player has no chance of recovery once they've exhausted Divine Damage Conversion and other knacks, or is unable to use them. They just immediately die when they get hit with enough aggravated damage. The other system at least gives players a chance. Our group is probably not going to use this particular part of the Scion 2.0 system. We're also still even weary about saying bashing and lethal are aesthetic. What we see in this new system is nerfing lethal damage simply because you all believed bashing damage was nerfed originally. The logic seems too strange, but I can still see where you're coming from initially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T00:36:54-07:00","id":158810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With your current system, we're going to try Damage Conversion like this: <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spend one legend and reduce bashing/lethal damage by your dots in Epic Stamina</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free to give it a try, but please keep a sharp eye on defensive scaling. You may even want to prevent that from stacking with Roll With It. Let us know how it goes!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by this? I'm not too sure it matters if other games do this, unless &quot;nowhere else&quot; means something different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that it violates the KISS rule, creating a new set of sub mechanics that require memorization and are ultimately unecessary. There are almost no other mentions of dying boxes anywhere else in the Scion game line, except a small blurb in Eric's Adventure(God) and fighting Loki(Ragnarok).<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">JSR house ruled long ago that your Dying Boxes are the sum of your dots in mundane Stamina and your dots in Epic Stamina, so this has been a non-issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is putting a patch on a leaky boat, instead of getting a better boat.<br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not... exactly. If you continued taking bashing damage after filling all your boxes with it, it began stacking to lethal damage, AND you were unconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, dying boxes cannot take bashing damage so there is nothing to wrap around.<br /> \u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to <a href=\"http://johnsscionresources.blogspot.com/2013/06/agg-damage.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> blog post, it seems JSR did allow for damage to continue into the dying boxes. The ST in my current game has that happen, too, so we sort of took care of it already.</div> </div> </div> </div>That goes back to patching a leaky boat. It is a patch that works, but it requires so many additional patches that the mechanic is not worth keeping in general.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this a problem? We actually had a player die because our healer was out cold and nobody knew how to stabilize in character. Plus, it'll always take somebody's action or at least their time to do it, so it's always a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can result in more healing than the Health Scion can dish out, and more than once I have seen situations where an attack sends a character into dying, then gets stabilized, then gets sent into dying again, then gets stabilized, then gets sent into dying again, then gets stabilized (you can see where this is going). Not just at my own table but several other tables as well.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want your players to die? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, we actually have quite a bit less death than JSR games. See below for some number crunching!<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I even bolded the part that the writers had bold in the book. Since it takes an action to do this, and an incapacitated player cannot perform any actions, they also cannot stop their own bleeding. So there is no rules conflict at all, the way I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stopping the bleeding &quot;is an involuntary, reflexive action a character performs on her normal action&quot;. Incapacitated characters become unconcious. Unconcious characters enter the state of Inactive. Inactivate characters &quot;do not take notable actions&quot;. This part is actually bolded in the book.<br /> <br /> So right there you have three rules conflicts. Inactive is on the list of normal actions, so can you stop bleeding when you are inactive? Stopping bleeding is not just reflexive but completely involuntary, so does it happen regardless of being inactive? Is it a notable action? Basically, the way we think the rules work tends to not reflect the way the rules actually work, and the rules are a bit of a freaking mess (we all knew that).<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think doing this actually makes it even easier for players to die. In your system, there's no recourse. Your player has no chance of recovery once they've exhausted Divine Damage Conversion and other knacks, or is unable to use them. They just immediately die when they get hit with enough aggravated damage. The other system at least gives players a chance. Our group is probably not going to use this particular part of the Scion 2.0 system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's crunch some numbers!<br /> <br /> Hero Joe has Stamina 3, Epic Stamina 3, and Fortitude 3.<br /> Demigod Joe has Stamina 6, Epic Stamina 6, and Fortitude 6.<br /> God Joe has Stamina 10, Epic Stamina 10, and Fortitude 10.<ul><li>In JSR, Hero Joe requires 28 Bashing, 17 Lethal, OR 17 Aggravated to be killed.</li> <li>In Scion 2.0, Hero Joe requires 33 Bashing, 22 Lethal, OR 11 Aggravated to be killed.</li> <li>In JSR, Demigod Joe requires 58 Bashing, 35 Lethal, OR 35 Aggravated to be killed.</li> <li>In Scion 2.0, Demigod Joe requires 69 Bashing, 46 Lethal, OR 23 Aggravated to be killed.</li> <li>In JSR, God Joe requires 126 Bashing, 73 Lethal, OR 73 Aggravated to be killed.</li> <li>In Scion 2.0, God Joe requires 159 Bashing, 106 Lethal, OR 53 Aggravated to be killed.</li> </ul>So right away you can see that it is harder to die from Bashing and Lethal damage than in JSR, but you might be thinking that it is easier to die from Aggravated? Don't forget that Scion 2.0 handles aggravated soak differently!<ul><li>In JSR, Hero Joe has 3 Soak vs Agg.</li> <li>In Scion 2.0, Hero Joe has 3 Soak vs Agg.</li> <li>In JSR, Demigod Joe has 7 Soak vs Agg.</li> <li>In Scion 2.0, Demigod Joe has 11 Soak vs Agg.</li> <li>In JSR, God Joe has 12 Soak vs Agg.</li> <li>In Scion 2.0, God Joe has 28 Soak vs Agg.</li> </ul>It becomes clear that things are a little more dangerous at Hero when dealing with Aggravated damage, but aggravated soak is better at Demigod and above. When you start adding armor, knacks, and boons your aggravated soak pulls even further ahead of JSR.<br /> <br /> But the heart of the Scion 2.0 Project is taking the parts that you want to use and leaving behind the things you do not want to use. If you and your players feel more comfortable with rules you are more familiar with, I can hardly blame you! I just wouldn't want you to make that choice based on the wrong impression.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=158326#post158326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're also still even weary about saying bashing and lethal are aesthetic. What we see in this new system is nerfing lethal damage simply because you all believed bashing damage was nerfed originally. The logic seems too strange, but I can still see where you're coming from initially.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly not sure what you mean by this. I never thought bashing damage was nerfed originally, I just never thought it was fair that a character who chooses a massive warhammer has to do so much more damage than someone who chooses a sword. Especially when those weapons are perfectly good at murdering people in real life. The ability to make a choice between bashing and lethal damage when using weapons that were designed to kill people helps to make all weapon choices valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 06-04-2014, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T15:47:15-07:00","id":159419,"title":"","content":"Not at all arguing either side of this, but those numbers for our system seem wonky. <br /> <br /> Hero Joe would have 7 bashing, 6 Lethal, and 4 agg soak. With 11 health boxes and 6 dying boxes.<br /> If we're talking about one MASSIVE swing it should take 44 bashing to kill him.<br /> 7 is soaked, takes 11 to fill bashing, another 11 fills lethal(he takes an automatic dying box). Then he can fill all but one of his dying boxes with dmg(4 more), then he can make all his lethal agg(10 more). Those can be done however the scion likes rotating as needed if this werent a one shot hit. Then he takes his final dmg in either dying box or final agg, doesnt matter. <br /> So with that in mind, it takes 32 lethal.<br /> Agg is much quicker though, if its just a full agg attack the character disintegrates at 15 agg, unable to wrap or put dmg in dying boxes.<br /> <br /> Demigod is similar:<br /> 100 bashing to die, 74 Lethal to die, or (8 agg soak) 31 agg to die. (I see why you're getting the bashing and lethal wrong, cause Im not sure we mention anywhere about wrapping and dying boxes, but Im not sure what you're missing about agg dmg).<br /> <br /> God is much different because we double health levels at god.<br /> So God Joe has 56 bashing, 51 lethal, and 12 agg soak. But he has 106 health levels, and 20 dying boxes.<br /> To one shot with bashing would take: 392 bashing<br /> Lethal: 281<br /> Agg: 118 <br /> <br /> Again, I have no opinion either way, just wanted to get numbers correct cause they seemed pretty off knowing how much I wreck pcs in the face with giant amounts of dmg. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T16:50:07-07:00","id":159448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=159419#post159419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hero Joe would have 7 bashing, 6 Lethal, and 4 agg soak. With 11 health boxes and 6 dying boxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both sides are assuming equal soak except aggravated, since we have special rules for aggravated soak. I am sorry I got the Hero Joe aggravated soak wrong! Where is the 4th dot of aggravated soak coming from? I know you round down the &quot;every five mundane stamina&quot;. Do you give them 1 point by default?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JSR</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=159419#post159419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then he can fill all but one of his dying boxes with dmg(4 more), then he can make all his lethal agg(10 more). Those can be done however the scion likes rotating as needed if this werent a one shot hit. Then he takes his final dmg in either dying box or final agg, doesnt matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a really big deal! Was this ever shown in a blog, because I cannot find this information anywhere on the site? It does change things rather dramatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:45:36-07:00","id":161933,"title":"","content":"Disclaimer: I'm just taking a first glance at the things you've listed in your OP as completed. Given that I'm trying to be fairly in-depth, I'll limit myself to Chaos in this post.<br /> <br /> Generally, you seem to have opted to make the existing disparity between purviews and epics not better but worse. We already know that leveling purviews is a superbly bad choice in most circumstances, generally until late demigod or god level. What I see when I page through your purview revisions is a general reduction in both utility and power. You might argue that you've just adjusted them to a common standard - but it appears that you choose RAW Fertility as your standard for that adjustment.<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos I</u><br /> I like <b>Anarchy</b>. But given that you have all kinds of things scaling with number of boons, this power should do the same to stay relevant in the face of high-level bonuses. I'd also strongly suggest changing the use limitation OR dramatically increasing the power of the boon. If a player can use it only once per game, resistance should be all but guaranteed - and if it isn't, there's no reason to limit use so strongly.<br /> <b>Chaos Theory</b>: If it is intended that the ST just mentions one important outcome (and not the most important or the most deleterious) you should add that as a disclaimer.<br /> I don't think there was any reason to get rid of Eye of the Storm. Or do you have copyright concerns about leaving existing boons in?<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos II</u><br /> <b>Breakdown</b>: Can you name a situation in which a dot of Epic Strength (comes with a free demolishing knack if the player cares) is not far more versatile and universally superior to this boon while being just as good for destroying objects? I strongly suggest changing the automatic 1L damage to &quot;inflict structural damage sufficient to make the object or structure nonfunctional&quot;, so a Scion of Chaos can short-circuit the bad guy's elevator at will without having to punch through X health levels first. That kind of effect is significant enough to warrant a legend cost depending on sturdiness of the structure involved, with maybe an upper limit for things it can demolish if you're feeling stingy.<br /> <b>Criticus</b>: The penalty seems very small, does not stack with other uses, and the duration is ridiculously short. I think there are much better uses for miscellaneous actions than spending 1L on this boon that doesn't even have guaranteed success. Again, one dot of Epic Appearance with Blinding Visage gives the user far more bang for the XP. This may have uses if you're trying to stack the maximum penalty on someone, but .. really I see little reason to buy or use this.<br /> <b>Discord</b>: I like the idea of this boon and bonus susccesses are a nice idea when you're leading a rebellion. However, given scion's extreme power curve (as you did not seem to change the Epic Attribute autosuccess progression) the net effect will be small. Still, it's free.<br /> <br /> Any reason you don't list &quot;Hornet's Nest&quot; here?<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos III</u><br /> <b>Butterfly Effect</b>: The flavor text does not fit the actual effect. An agent of law could use this boon just as well to rat out compelled revolutionaries, and that kind of blanket &quot;detect mind control&quot; effect does seem like it should go to Epic Perception or Manipulation, not Chaos.<br /> <br /> <b>Gremlins</b>: Gremlins need more stats then &quot;boons they have&quot; if they're supposed to perform any kind of action. Without stats, I can't evaluate their usefulness beyond the fact that one of their boons is of questionable value.<br /> <br /> <b>Libertine</b>: This has a typo (&quot;poer&quot;, I assume you meant &quot;power&quot;). I have a slight problem with presupposing that every bringer of chaos has meaningful ideals of his own. Other than that, something as specific as the ability to use MDV against Justice boons seems like it is a level one boon, not level *three*. It should be melded with <b>Anarchy</b>.<br /> I have yet to find edited XP tables on the site, so this looks<i> badly</i> out of whack if you're using the RAW ones.<br /> <br /> Again, what I felt was one of the few useful hero-level boons got shafted.<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos IV</u><br /> <b>Babel</b>: Again, our design goals diverge. I do not feel one has to be a demigod to give a person sensory aphasia - with epic Intelligence and Dexterity, I could justify doing that with a well-timed punch to the skull. I'd place it at Chaos II for a single-target, minutes-long effect. Chaos III for multi-target with potentially longer duration.<br /> Otherwise it looks okay.<br /> <br /> <b>Firebrand</b>: Making larger-scale effects restricted to demigods seems to be an overall design decision, so I'll accept it for this one and just reiterate my comments on Anarchy and Libertine.<br /> <br /> <b>Rising Action</b>: With no limitations whatsoever, except a general caveat that it gives the storyteller an excuse to mess things up for you even more, this looks like it could disrupt play a lot (even more so than VtM Dementation).<br /> It also looks like something that would be better placed in Magic - very similar to Deus Ex Machina.<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos V</u><br /> <b>Disorder</b>: I like it. However, the notion that evidence is needed for a conviction is not universal, even less so by mythic standards, so perhaps it should have the option to activate it in advance - so the user is not even a likely suspect?<br /> <br /> <b>Paranoia</b>: The idea is good, but it has a rather long delay before it does anything. What's more, it scales <i>negatively </i>with Chaos boons possessed - because you specified that the lashing out occurs at the end of that time period, more Chaos boons cause a bigger delay. While that may be more useful in some circumstances, there are certainly those were you need the paranoia to take effect *soon* or even *now*. The user should just be able to specify the delay. I at least can't fathom why a demigod of chaos should not be able to make his enemies strike at their allies in the midst of combat for an appropriate legend cost.<br /> If you want to give rewards for careful planning, it should read like &quot;If the Scion foregoes the immediate outburst and lets the paranoia burn slowly, the subject of this power suffers from even more distrust of their allies. Each day, they extend their suspicions to one more person they are closely associated with and prepare their retaliation, before they lash out against all at once at the end of the duration - thus alienating them from far more of their allies and and inflicting far greater damage. However, this also increases the window of time in which other boons or knacks might defeat this affliction.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Sabot</b>: This should not be a demigod boon and it should not cost Willpower. Otherwise it's better than Breakdown. Still, since this is the use of a specialized purview and not Epic Strength, I suggest bypassing object health levels and just making it nonfunctional. You could keep two boons and reserve the bigger ones for big machines or whole facilities, or more controlled sabotage.<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos VI</u><br /> <b>Bacchanalia</b>: A blunt instrument, but possibly useful. I like it better than RAW's Instant Riot.<br /> Rebellion: Your example mentions treating wounded - if you're in any way serious about that, it will take more than one scene. Ditto for &quot;taking up arms&quot; against some organization. It should have a far longer duration, perhaps longer on targets with lower legend.<br /> <br /> <u>Chaos VII</u><br /> <b>Apostate</b>: Actually pretty nice.<br /> <br /> I'll get to Lord of Misrule later (hopefully tomorrow) but for now I'm hungry and most of my concerns have been adressed. I'm sorry for being the resident curmudgeon, but I feel I'm most helpful when I speak my mind frankly. I do appreciate your effort and hope you can reform the mess that is the Scion rules.<br /> <br /> PS: Any reason why Loki doesn't have Fire anymore? I've never read a source except the usual ones for laypeople (all of which of course stated he was the god of fire), so I'm genuinely curious why you changed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2601,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","user":"Nachtigallerator","date":".  Derped on XP costs. My bad. 06-07-2014, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T15:00:31-07:00","id":161987,"title":"","content":"As you are talking about mechanical balance, especially concerning chaos, I'll allow Iry and Watcher to really have a shot at answering your questions tonight but I can assure you that we have not reduced the utility of purviews or used RAW Fertility (of all things, that's a terrible purview) as a standard. Rather, we went towards our remake of Water.<br /> <br /> Hero-level boons are no longer blatant in our system. We do not want the overt-supernatural there until you've hit demigod, so while the scope of those hero boons might appear to be nerfed, we've attempted to make them useful over a myriad of situations. You'll notice that we've gone for removing much of the dice/success bloat that was Scion, so perhaps that's why it looks nerfed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 06-07-2014, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T15:02:38-07:00","id":161989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, you seem to have opted to make the existing disparity between Purviews and Epics not better but worse. We already know that leveling purviews is a superbly bad choice in most circumstances, generally until late demigod or god level. What I see when I page through your purview revisions is a general reduction in both utility and power. You might argue that you've just adjusted them to a common standard - but it appears that you choose RAW Fertility as your standard for that adjustment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very happy to answer all of your questions here, and to explain our choices, and Iry should come in later to explain the deeper levels of the mechanics of things for that is not particularly my department, but I do wonder why you find that we have increased this disparity? I don't think we have reduced the utility or power of all of the Purviews, personally, but you are welcome to hold that opinion, entirely. But, why do you believe this? I am just curious, in case that there has been a misunderstanding at come point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like <b>Anarchy</b>. But given that you have all kinds of things scaling with number of boons, this power should do the same to stay relevant in the face of high-level bonuses. I'd also strongly suggest changing the use limitation OR dramatically increasing the power of the boon. If a player can use it only once per game, resistance should be all but guaranteed - and if it isn't, there's no reason to limit use so strongly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anarchy is a Rank One Boon, and is at level with all other Boons of that Rank. It is likely to even come up more often than the Elemental Immunities as well. All of the 'Immunity' Boons have the 'Once per game' disclaimer attached to them as well. At any Rank, a +6 to your MDV to resist a power is a very hardy bonus indeed. At Hero, if you use it, you are likely going to be flat out immune to any attempt to influence you if you are invested in any of the MDV Epic Attributes.<br /> <br /> The average defenses, and average number of successes gained by Legend, with base Willpower, assuming someone is keeping their relevant Abilities and Attributes maxed out is as follows.<br /> <br /> Legend 2: 9 MDV v. 6 Successes<br /> Legend 3: 10 MDV v. 7 Successes<br /> Legend 4: 12 MDV v. 9 Successes<br /> Legend 5: 22 MDV v. 19 Successes<br /> Legend 6: 27 MDV v. 24 Successes<br /> Legend 7: 33 MDV v. 30 Successes<br /> Legend 8: 40 MDV v. 37 Successes<br /> Legend 9: 48 MDV v. 45 Successes<br /> Legend 10: 57 MDV v. 54 Successes<br /> <br /> This disparage of 3 in favor of MDV can be increased to a disparage of 5 by raising your total Willpower through increasing your Virtues.<br /> <br /> But, as you can see, when facing off against someone of equal Legend, the defender is already going to win with equal investment of Experience, and if someone wishes to channel Virtues, Fates, or their Deed, all it takes is equal investment to resist the power. With Anarchy, someone can resist the influences of someone above their own Legend, by one or two Dots, with a fair chance of Success. The reason it is not a flat out resist, or that you can use it repeatedly, is that everyone would then take the first Dot of Chaos for no other reason than to just have it to buff their MDV constantly, which we feel is against the spirit of what we would like out of a Resistance Boon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chaos Theory</b>: If it is intended that the ST just mentions one important outcome (and not the most important or the most deleterious) you should add that as a disclaimer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose we could?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there was any reason to get rid of Eye of the Storm. Or do you have copyright concerns about leaving existing boons in?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have no copyright concerns. We are a fan site, we are not making money, and we are changing things, but ultimately we just want to revise everything. The reason Eye of the Storm is not included is that we felt that an immunity to Chaos was fundamentally against the idea of the concept. Additionally, we don't have very many examples of Chaos Gods not being effected by Chaos themselves. Since they often represent what the society they are from deems chaotic, it would imply that they are very much not immune to Chaos. So, we felt like an Immunity Boon of being able to resist people trying to make you stop being Chaotic made more sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Breakdown</b>: Can you name a situation in which a dot of Epic Strength (comes with a free demolishing knack if the player cares) is not far more versatile and universally superior to this boon while being just as good for destroying objects? I strongly suggest changing the automatic 1L damage to &quot;inflict structural damage sufficient to make the object or structure nonfunctional&quot;, so a Scion of Chaos can short-circuit the bad guy's elevator at will without having to punch through X health levels first. That kind of effect is significant enough to warrant a legend cost depending on sturdiness of the structure involved, with maybe an upper limit for things it can demolish if you're feeling stingy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is neither better, or worse, to take a Dot of Epic Strength and take one of the destruction Knacks. If someone wishes to use their Epic Strength to destroy an object, and someone wishes to use their Chaos, both should have the option to do so. Eventually, someone with Epic Strength will be able to outshine someone with Chaos since breaking things is a relatively minor part of Chaos that we are not even sure should be present in the Purview, but at this Rank, they should be on par.<br /> <br /> If we gave Breakdown a 1 Legend cost, and gave it the ability to destroy anything in one fell swoop, a Legend 4 Scion could take down Big Ben by pointing at it and paying one point of Legend. That, we believe, is more powerful than a Rank 2 Boon should be. Though, you are welcome to change it for your own games.<br /> <br /> A situation in which a Dot of Epic Strength, taking Holy Rampage as your free Knack would not be more useful / versatile than tanking Breakdown would be if the object has exceptionally high Soak DV. Holy Rampage, for no cost, will allow you to half the Soak DV of the object, which may still be above your capabilities at Hero, but someone with Breakdown can, as the name would imply, slowly break down the object. There are cases where Epic Strength will be more useful, and where Breakdown will be more useful. And, additionally, we do not believe having cross over is a bad thing to a minor degree such as this. Though, you are welcome to do it in any way you wish to. This is just our own personal belief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Criticus</b>: The penalty seems very small, does not stack with other uses, and the duration is ridiculously short. I think there are much better uses for miscellaneous actions than spending 1L on this boon that doesn't even have guaranteed success. Again, one dot of Epic Appearance with Blinding Visage gives the user far more bang for the XP. This may have uses if you're trying to stack the maximum penalty on someone, but .. really I see little reason to buy or use this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind we have not yet revised Epic Appearance, so it may be out of sway with the rest of the Website. Along with all of the other unrevised sections. At base, a target will receive -4 Dice to all actions for being blinded, and while, at base, this will outdo Criticus, when you have Chaos 10, you can give someone a penalty of -10 Dice. Even at Legend 5 you are outdoing Blinding Visage, which, again, has not been revised yet and will be reigned in when we eventually get to it.<br /> <br /> Additionally, our Botching rules play incredibly heavily on the importance of your number of Dice. If you are able to remove 10 Dice from someone at God, you can potentially be dooming them to Botching if they don't have extra dice from some source.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Discord</b>: I like the idea of this boon and bonus susccesses are a nice idea when you're leading a rebellion. However, given scion's extreme power curve (as you did not seem to change the Epic Attribute autosuccess progression) the net effect will be small. Still, it's free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is what we call an 'Aura'. All Purviews have Auras of some sort or another, and all are roughly equal in power. They are incredibly useful at Hero, and can play very important, or very lethal roles. But, at higher Legends, they slightly patter out. But, I would like to point out, once again, that the balance between offensive and defensive Social Attacks is a very thin one, and a +2 can throw that balance off. When you need every little bit, it can be quite helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason you don't list &quot;Hornet's Nest&quot; here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hornet's Nest's spiritual successor is Chaos Theory. Hornet's Nest's spontanious knowledge of how to disrupt things the most, we believe, was a more interesting power if you could recieve it earlier, and it did not need a roll. Therefore, we changed it so that you had to ask more direct questions, and additionally in the proccess, it became more versitile. It can still be used for its old function, if a Player is willing to ask multiple questions, possibly having taken a Relic that makes it free to use Chaos Theory so they may ask to their heart's content, but it is still able to be used in other areas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Butterfly Effect</b>: The flavor text does not fit the actual effect. An agent of law could use this boon just as well to rat out compelled revolutionaries, and that kind of blanket &quot;detect mind control&quot; effect does seem like it should go to Epic Perception or Manipulation, not Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>An Agent of Law can, and will likely be able to do this, yes. This will be because Justice will be receiving a similar power. We felt that it also belonged in Chaos so someone could learn if their powers were Successful or not, since normally a Scion will have no knowledge of this unless it as an incredibly blatant Mind Effecting power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gremlins</b>: Gremlins need more stats then &quot;boons they have&quot; if they're supposed to perform any kind of action. Without stats, I can't evaluate their usefulness beyond the fact that one of their boons is of questionable value.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Creatures created or summoned by the Rank 3 Powers of many Purviews are intended to be used for very minor tasks, and therefore full stats would only increase the paperwork for a Storyteller, and a player. We believe in decreasing this as much as we possibly can, so the creatures have no direct stats. It is up to the Storyteller to decide if the creatures are capable of something, or if they are not, while keeping in mind what sort of creature they are. A Leshy, for example, may not be as easily convinced to set a fire as a Salamander, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Libertine</b>: This has a typo (&quot;poer&quot;, I assume you meant &quot;power&quot;). I have a slight problem with presupposing that every bringer of chaos has meaningful ideals of his own. Other than that, something as specific as the ability to use MDV against Justice boons seems like it is a level one boon, not level *three*. It should be melded with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, thank you for catching that, I will change it as soon as I finish this reply.<br /> <br /> Not all bringers of Chaos will have ideals, but many do. Dionysus' has ideals of revelry, The Morrigan, her spite unbound by Nuada, Tezcatlipoca, disrupting the world so that he is always able to do whatever Tezcatlipoca does. We thought of this being a Rank One Boon, but we didn't believe it would come up as often at such low a level, and therefore we gave Rank One a more blanket resistance which can be stacked ontop of this.<br /> <br /> You are entirely welcome to change the order of these in your own game, but, for us, we are quite comfortable with them as they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Anarchy</b>.<br /> I have yet to find edited XP tables on the site, so this looks<i> badly</i> out of whack if you're using the RAW ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do not use RAW, it is right <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/character-creation#TOC-Experience\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, I am sorry you could not find it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, what I felt was one of the few useful hero-level boons got shafted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are totally welcome to that belief! Personally, I am far more excited to use this Chaos than RAW Chaos, and I believe Hero has some incredibly interesting powers, but you are welcome to hold an opposing belief to myself. I am very sorry you feel this way though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Babel</b>: Again, our design goals diverge. I do not feel one has to be a demigod to give a person sensory aphasia - with epic Intelligence and Dexterity, I could justify doing that with a well-timed punch to the skull. I'd place it at Chaos II for a single-target, minutes-long effect. Chaos III for multi-target with potentially longer duration.<br /> Otherwise it looks okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could duplicate this effect with some incredibly exact blows, and exceptional knowledge of the way the brain processes language, but, they would be some quite difficult rolls for someone to do on the fly, at Legend 5. And, additionally, it is incredibly overt to do so physically. With Babel, you can use this Boon on a target without running up and punching them in the head.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Firebrand</b>: Making larger-scale effects restricted to demigods seems to be an overall design decision, so I'll accept it for this one and just reiterate my comments on Anarchy and Libertine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighty, I believe you will have many problems with our other Immunity Boons than, but, just differences in opinion, entirely normal thing. I believe that Firebrand is exceptionally powerful, in reference to the MDV v. Average Social attack chart. But, opposing oppositions are not a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Rising Action</b>: With no limitations whatsoever, except a general caveat that it gives the storyteller an excuse to mess things up for you even more, this looks like it could disrupt play a lot (even more so than VtM Dementation).<br /> <br /> It also looks like something that would be better placed in Magic - very similar to Deus Ex Machina.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire point of this Boon is to allow a Chaos player to disrupt play. Of course, they, being in a social contract with their Storyteller and other players, should not do this all the time, for that would be obviously rude and not very nice. A sure way to be thrown out of a gaming group. But, that is the entire point of the Boon. And, its similarities to Deus Ex are intentional, though Deus Ex has the caveat that you now owe someone very important, and that you are saved from whatever situation you are in. This has neither of those, and is only an agent of great change. Which, we believe, is what Chaos should be able to do.<br /> <br /> Once again, we are entirely fine with minor levels of cross over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Disorder</b>: I like it. However, the notion that evidence is needed for a conviction is not universal, even less so by mythic standards, so perhaps it should have the option to activate it in advance - so the user is not even a likely suspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iry will have to talk about that one. It would be entirely possible to take a Relic for that effect, but this Boon could disrupt 'evidence' in any number of ways. Cast doubt in the mind of the Mystery God, and other ways of disrupting the 'evidence', be it physical or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Paranoia</b>: The idea is good, but it has a rather long delay before it does anything. What's more, it scales <i>negatively </i>with Chaos boons possessed - because you specified that the lashing out occurs at the end of that time period, more Chaos boons cause a bigger delay. While that may be more useful in some circumstances, there are certainly those were you need the paranoia to take effect *soon* or even *now*. The user should just be able to specify the delay. I at least can't fathom why a demigod of chaos should not be able to make his enemies strike at their allies in the midst of combat for an appropriate legend cost.<br /> <br /> If you want to give rewards for careful planning, it should read like &quot;If the Scion foregoes the immediate outburst and lets the paranoia burn slowly, the subject of this power suffers from even more distrust of their allies. Each day, they extend their suspicions to one more person they are closely associated with and prepare their retaliation, before they lash out against all at once at the end of the duration - thus alienating them from far more of their allies and and inflicting far greater damage. However, this also increases the window of time in which other boons or knacks might defeat this affliction.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The increasing delay in the effect of the Boon is actually intentional. The longer you are away from the target, the more likely they will firstly not think of you as the cause, and additionally increasing the chance that they will move to somewhere where they will do more damage. A few days after the battle, at home with their SO, for example. If it were only hours, or ticks, it could be useful in the direct combat, but we decided we preferred to have it be long reaching. To bring Chaos to places the Chaos Scion has not even been.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sabot</b>: This should not be a demigod boon and it should not cost Willpower. Otherwise it's better than Breakdown. Still, since this is the use of a specialized purview and not Epic Strength, I suggest bypassing object health levels and just making it nonfunctional. You could keep two boons and reserve the bigger ones for big machines or whole facilities, or more controlled sabotage.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are actually not particularly happy with Sabot as a concept. We feel that it harkens back to old Chaos too much, and we don't agree with much of old Chaos. Iry will have to come in and explain the pricing, but my comments about Breakdown still stand. I believe this is just a differing opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rebellion: Your example mentions treating wounded - if you're in any way serious about that, it will take more than one scene. Ditto for &quot;taking up arms&quot; against some organization. It should have a far longer duration, perhaps longer on targets with lower legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is likely a difference on how long we run a Scene, compared to yourself. A Scene can last multiple Sessions for ourselves, though Iry can explain this far better than I can. So, I welcome him to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry for being the resident curmudgeon, but I feel I'm most helpful when I speak my mind frankly. I do appreciate your effort and hope you can reform the mess that is the Scion rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is quite alright. I believe the majority of the issues are being caused by just differences in how we run things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: Any reason why Loki doesn't have Fire anymore? I've never read a source except the usual ones for laypeople (all of which of course stated he was the god of fire), so I'm genuinely curious why you changed that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Loki and Fire is a very dodgy subject. He never presents any Fire based powers in any of the Legends in which he is present, we have no evidence of him being worshiped as a Fire God, and is never refered to as a Fire God in any of the Eddas. The Evidence modernly used for him being a Fire God is a fairly old, and fairly dodgy linguistic link between his name, &quot;Loki&quot; and the word &quot;Logi&quot; which means Fire. Some scholars believe that his name being &quot;Loki&quot;, so close to &quot;Logi&quot; means he is a Fire God, but we don't really follow that train of thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-07-2014, 09:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T15:49:48-07:00","id":161995,"title":"","content":"Hey, quick question regarding specialties. Are we only able to ever get specialties for our associated abilities, or is the restriction simply on the free specialties you get at character creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T15:56:48-07:00","id":161999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161995#post161995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, quick question regarding specialties. Are we only able to ever get specialties for our associated abilities, or is the restriction simply on the free specialties you get at character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can grab a Specialty in any Ability if you pay the Experience cost for it (3 exp), but you get one free Specialty for each Associated Ability you have at least one Dot in. There are no restrictions on these Abilities, if your Divine Parent is Lugh, your Thrown doesn't have to be for Spears, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T16:04:51-07:00","id":162002,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the quick answer, Watcher. Just FYI, I've also sent an e-mail to you guys with a few more questions. Of note, feel free to re-post anything you e-mail to me over here in this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T16:16:40-07:00","id":162025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=162002#post162002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the quick answer, Watcher. Just FYI, I've also sent an e-mail to you guys with a few more questions. Of note, feel free to re-post anything you e-mail to me over here in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will probably do so, either here or on the site in a FAQ. And, we are in the process of replying to the email, you should have it by tomorrow unless something comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T16:19:15-07:00","id":162026,"title":"","content":"That'll be fine. Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T02:50:52-07:00","id":162313,"title":"","content":"Re disparity: The few powerful boons in early levels were removed - either because they do not fit your idea of purview power or because you judged them as too overt, I can't tell. Now these were clearly some outliers, but my point that investing in epic attributes just gives more benefits than investing in purviews until quite late in the game still stands. That is true for RAW Scion, and your rework has made it more true by removing the few desirable boons at early levels. I do not see how you have improved the situation in other respects.<br /> <br /> @Anarchy: Again I need to explain my principles, which are likely not the same as yours are. If we look at a power such as Detail Variation, I think we both can agree that it's very basic, but that it also never becomes truly useless. This is my idea of a well-made low-level effect. The effect is limited, but it is limited because it's quite specific, not because it's small. The same goes, with some caveats, for RAW Fire Immunity. Again the benefit is limited by being specific, but it does stay applicable throughout the whole game. I must however concede that +6 against any mental effect is big. Thinking about it, I'm not sure it could not be limited to exclude mental influences from Chaos boons and others that are directed at increasing disorder - resisting any mental influence isn't very &quot;Chaos&quot; to me, just as detecting any mental influence just isn't. Universally applicable social powers are what Epics should be for.<br /> <br /> @Chaos Theory: I realize that the danger inherent in it is obvious at your gaming table, but if this rework is meant as a resource for a larger audience, my feeling is that you should always add a word of warning for powers with this kind of backfire potential, similar to the caveat that Deus Ex Machina has.<br /> <br /> @Eye of the Storm: I can see your point. Again, perhaps the immunity boon could be reworded not to apply to influences that are meant to make the Scion behave more chaotic - right now, it's not as directed as I think you intented it to be.<br /> <br /> @Breakdown: The dot of Epic Strength is better because it can destroy structures and do much more than just that, even if you just take the destruction knack. Breakdown on the other hand is much worse because it costs the same as the second dot of Epic Strength and does only one narrow thing and will never improve at doing that.<br /> Your point about Big Ben only applies if the change were badly written. It should be no problem at all to specify a maximum size of object to be affected, or just restrict it to &quot;machines&quot; (any construction with moving parts) up to a certain size of your liking.<br /> <br /> @Criticus: My reading of the text on the site is fairly clear in that the penalty is -1 success. It's described as &quot;cumulative&quot;, but the next sentence specifies that it does not stack with itself, so the only thing it could stack with for a larger penalty are penalties from other sources. I am however not a native speaker, so it may well be that I misunderstand a key paragraph.<br /> <br /> @Hornet's Nest: Understood. I liked how it was aimed at disruptive changes, admittedly - as broad as Chaos Theory is, it will require more thinking on part of the ST and better communication between all parties. &quot;How can Scion X be the most disruptive here&quot; is a question the ST can prepare in advance for. &quot;What is one interesting thing that will happen if he mispronounces the giant's middle name&quot; is much more unexpected.<br /> It's great if it works at your table, of course.<br /> <br /> @Gremlins: I can see the reasoning in that, but I'd still like to know the barest bones of their combat stats and what dicepool they would use to go about making mischief.<br /> <br /> @Libertine: Of course you are comfortable with the way it is yourself, given that you have made this public. You are entitled to your own opinion and you are entitled to play the game in any way you want. I would never try to infringe on that. I thought this was an opportunity to offer you feedback from someone else's perspective. The way I see the game, a purely passive bonus that applies only in the rare situation of being hit with a Justice boon - even rarer than Fire Immunity - is not adequate if the same XP would give a player the third dot of an Epic Attribute. As long as the cost structure is this way, this is the comparison I think one has to make.<br /> Anyhow, if the result of this conversation is that you give me an answer that is both obvious and does not interact with the argument I put forth - that you think it's fine the way it already is, but of course I may change it privately - then this is a conversation both of us have nothing to learn from.<br /> <br /> @Babel: The point is that this costs the same as the fourth dot of an epic attribute. For giving one person a few minutes of sensory aphasia, this seems overpriced.<br /> <br /> @Firebrand: I'll just ask this here, I think - are the other immunity boons really all &quot;once per game&quot;? If you have already reworked Water, it doesn't seem to be this way. Again, you have made the Chaos immunity power universally applicable. Were it a limited &quot;against powers aimed to make the Scion stop disruptive behaviour&quot; MDV bonus, the persistent model might work out. I'll admit that heroes are pretty much the poster children of disruptive behaviour, but making them even more disruptive is not something Anarchy should block.<br /> <br /> @Disorder: I thought of &quot;evidence&quot; of something physical because that is the easiest to imagine to just &quot;go missing&quot;. If it works on someone else's convictions too (would MDV apply then?), I think that ought to be in the text. Again, you can obviously use it just fine, but for the benefit of your larger readership.<br /> <br /> @Paranoia: As I said - the delay can be useful in *some* situations. In others, you are trying to sabotage enemy operations and don't have that many days of time left! In that situation, you have the bizarre scenario that a less powerful Scion of Chaos can use this power successfully, while Loki can not - because he absolutely HAS to take advantage of the full duration. That does seem like a glitch to me, hence my suggestion of limiting the *maximum* possible delay, but giving the user the option not to use all of that.<br /> <br /> @Sabot: I'll reiterate what I said about breakdown here. Though at this experience cost, Sabot should totally be the go-to boon if you insist on breaking Big Ben in some manner. Given that &quot;Big Ben&quot; refers to just one (admittedly very large) bell in Westminster Palace, I think it's totally okay to crack it to splinters with a demigod boon. Demigod Strength would do the same thing and preferably use it as a throwing weapon too.<br /> <br /> @Rebellion: Ah, yes. I'm still in the &quot;a scene is fifteen minutes or one action-packed sequence&quot; mindset. Do you plan on writing that out, too? It might be important to properly use your boons on another table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T04:43:37-07:00","id":162359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=162026#post162026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So, is weapon accuracy no longer a thing? Is it absorbed into weapon damage? Or is something happening that you guys didn't put up?</span></i></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weapon Accuracy is no longer a thing in Scion 2.0. You can use the higher of the weapon\u2019s Damage or Accuracy as you see fit. We are going to revise the weapons at some point, but that is a distant project that will come after everything else has been revised.</span></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=162026#post162026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Do you guys do different things besides stunts to regain Willpower? Is there a timing, like with healing, or some other mechanic? How do you do it</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">?</span></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Just like normal Scion, everyone regains all their willpower at the end of the story. You can also regain willpower through stunts, knacks, and boons that grant willpower. Even non-player characters are gaining small stunts and regaining willpower at the end of every scene or whenever they accomplish goals.</span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=162026#post162026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I see you do stunting a bit differently, but it seems kind of confusing. Do you no longer give dice for stunts at all? Do players have to wait until the end of the scene to hear how their stunts went? Please explain how you're doing it and what you've changed from RAW, if you don't mind.</span></i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">It\u2019s actually a lot more simple! You award a big pile of stunt at the end of every scene, and whenever the band accomplishes something awesome within a scene. For a Legend 2 band the average would be 6 Stunt, but you can easily award more if your players are describing things in a really impressive way, or if you just want a higher powered game.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stunts no longer award dice, mostly because it very quickly becomes a trivial bonus and one more thing everyone needs to add when they are figuring out how many dice they need to roll.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> A lot of people use cheat sheets for that kind of thing, but it still slows the game down a little bit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">More importantly, awarding everything at once helps the players to stay in character instead of breaking the flow of the game and asking how many stunt dice they get. It also helps to balance things out between outgoing players who frequently ask for stunts and shy players who have a really hard time asking for stunts.</span></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=162026#post162026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Also, and this can be a separate response (because the three sections before this are of utmost importance to me), what are you all thinking on the Dying Boxes issue now that John replied on Onyx Path?</span></i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We are still thinking the same thing. The entire mechanic is a leaky boat that should simply be replaced with a shiny new boat instead of a bunch of patches.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apparently John already allows damage to wrap around into aggravated, so he is using the same 'shiny boat' in combination with dying boxes, except that he allows his players to choose if damage goes into dying boxes or aggravated boxes.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We strongly feel that our greater aggravated soak and balance of dice adders makes that kind of juggling unnecessary,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> and the rule already has an extremely strong track record because it is the same thing they use for New World of Darkness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In some sense, keeping Dying Boxes may not even make a difference in your game. The storyteller may simply increase or decrease the power of your enemies to match it. So it ultimately comes down to doing whatever your players think is the most fun!</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T06:37:17-07:00","id":162387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disclaimer: I'm just taking a first glance at the things you've listed in your OP as completed. Given that I'm trying to be fairly in-depth, I'll limit myself to Chaos in this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries! When it comes to design decisions we can take it on the chin and stand by our work. We're also entirely open to revising things that sound confusing or are proven to have problems.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, you seem to have opted to make the existing disparity between purviews and epics not better but worse. We already know that leveling purviews is a superbly bad choice in most circumstances, generally until late demigod or god level. What I see when I page through your purview revisions is a general reduction in both utility and power. You might argue that you've just adjusted them to a common standard - but it appears that you choose RAW Fertility as your standard for that adjustment.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is actually one of our goals to close the gap between epics and purviews, so that players would be far more enticed to take purviews at the lower levels. So far, most of the lower level material has been getting good reviews across several gaming tables, though the word is still out on Enech and Chaos (which are brand new).<br /> <br /> Several attributes and purviews have absolutely not been revised yet. Everything that has not yet been revised is from Gotham By Night, with choice and delicious cuts from Modern Mythos.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking about it, I'm not sure it could not be limited to exclude mental influences from Chaos boons and others that are directed at increasing disorder - resisting any mental influence isn't very &quot;Chaos&quot; to me, just as detecting any mental influence just isn't. Universally applicable social powers are what Epics should be for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to allow a little bit of overlap when it makes thematic or mythological sense for that overlap to exist. Every time I sit down to design a boon I spend hours or even days debating if a boon should exist when a similar effect already exists. But I also try to determine if I am in danger of denying a purview a perfectly appropriate boon just because something else has a similar effect.<br /> <br /> Since Chaos and Justice are entirely social constructs by nature, it is only natural that they would have quite a few effects that share a lot of design space with Epic Socials.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Chaos Theory: I realize that the danger inherent in it is obvious at your gaming table, but if this rework is meant as a resource for a larger audience, my feeling is that you should always add a word of warning for powers with this kind of backfire potential, similar to the caveat that Deus Ex Machina has.</div> </div> </div> </div>This rework is definitely meant as a resource for a larger audience. But I am somewhat curious what you mean about disclaimers and backfire potential. You mean the risk that a player may get information that is not immediately useful?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Breakdown: The dot of Epic Strength is better because it can destroy structures and do much more than just that, even if you just take the destruction knack. Breakdown on the other hand is much worse because it costs the same as the second dot of Epic Strength and does only one narrow thing and will never improve at doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two different things going on here.<br /> <br /> Breakdown is not designed to be better or worse than Epic Strength, but to approach the situation from an oblique angle. While a single dot of epic strength may be more effective than Breakdown at immediate destruction, it is much better at slowly breaking down things that are extremely durable (which may be dramatically more common outside of the mundane world), and to break things down in a way that is not immediately obvious to everyone who would see you physically attacking something.<br /> <br /> Breakdown by itself does not cost the same XP as the second dot of Epic Strength. It costs 8XP to buy the second dot of Chaos, which grants you +2 successes on all Chaos activation rolls and grants you a free boon. Further boons of any level you have access to are ONLY 6XP. Just like Epic Attributes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Criticus: My reading of the text on the site is fairly clear in that the penalty is -1 success. It's described as &quot;cumulative&quot;, but the next sentence specifies that it does not stack with itself, so the only thing it could stack with for a larger penalty are penalties from other sources. I am however not a native speaker, so it may well be that I misunderstand a key paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this may be a language issue. A single activation of Criticus is cumulative, so someone suffers -1 dice on their first action, -2 dice on their second action, -3 dice on their third action, etc.<br /> <br /> Criticus also stacks with other sources of dice penalties, but does not stack from additional activations of Criticus from yourself or anyone else.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Hornet's Nest: Understood. I liked how it was aimed at disruptive changes, admittedly - as broad as Chaos Theory is, it will require more thinking on part of the ST and better communication between all parties. &quot;How can Scion X be the most disruptive here&quot; is a question the ST can prepare in advance for. &quot;What is one interesting thing that will happen if he mispronounces the giant's middle name&quot; is much more unexpected.<br /> It's great if it works at your table, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had the pleasure of sharing the company at a lot of different tables. While the order portion of the boon was just fine, the overwhelming trend for the chaos portion of Hornet's Nest has always been slapstick and comedy. The goal with Chaos Theory was to expand Hornet's Nest so that the player could suggest the action and the storyteller could offer input on that action.<br /> <br /> Right away this makes sure that the player is okay with whatever action is being proposed, or is thinking about as a hypothetical. This gives the storyteller useful information about where the player is considering taking the game, and I personally think it is easier to answer this question because I know the plot of my game, rather than telling my player he would create the most chaos by stripping naked, uttering a bullshit prophecy, urinating in cheerios, and then murdering someone.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Gremlins: I can see the reasoning in that, but I'd still like to know the barest bones of their combat stats and what dicepool they would use to go about making mischief.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are completely expendible minions that serve a thematic role, and get squashed when faced with even the slightest bit of serious opposition. You can give them the stats of generic mortals in a pinch.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Libertine: I thought this was an opportunity to offer you feedback from someone else's perspective. The way I see the game, a purely passive bonus that applies only in the rare situation of being hit with a Justice boon - even rarer than Fire Immunity - is not adequate if the same XP would give a player the third dot of an Epic Attribute. As long as the cost structure is this way, this is the comparison I think one has to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>The cost structure has been completely changed! Purviews are purchased sequentially just like Epic Attributes, and provide a free boon along with every dot you gain. Further boons can be purchased for only 6XP per boon.<br /> <br /> I think there should be a reasonable fear that a non-player character with Justice may show up to wreck your day at any given moment, and you need to curry favor and play the social game to prevent that from happening. If someone is taking Chaos in one of my games, that tells me I need to include more authority figures and establishments to topple, because that is the kind of game they want to play. So this becomes even more true.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Firebrand: I'll just ask this here, I think - are the other immunity boons really all &quot;once per game&quot;? If you have already reworked Water, it doesn't seem to be this way. Again, you have made the Chaos immunity power universally applicable. Were it a limited &quot;against powers aimed to make the Scion stop disruptive behaviour&quot; MDV bonus, the persistent model might work out. I'll admit that heroes are pretty much the poster children of disruptive behaviour, but making them even more disruptive is not something Anarchy should block.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of the immunity boons are going to be a constant benefit that applies whenever their situation comes up. Anarchy was just so incredibly useful and versatile that it got the limitation of once per game. Another example of once per game can be found in the Psychopomp boon &quot;Open Sesame&quot; because it is similarly versatile and powerful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Disorder: I thought of &quot;evidence&quot; of something physical because that is the easiest to imagine to just &quot;go missing&quot;. If it works on someone else's convictions too (would MDV apply then?), I think that ought to be in the text. Again, you can obviously use it just fine, but for the benefit of your larger readership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disorder is intended to apply only to physical evidence, such as tracks on the ground, electronic bank or cell phone records, and all manner of forensic evidence. It is not supposed to include any kind of supernatural compulsion.<br /> <br /> It is certainly an idea that Disorder could be used pre-emptively so that nobody discovers your evidence in the first place. I'm definitely willing to investigate that further. The trick is writing the boon in a certain way that makes the player not waste tons of legend covering every potential piece of evidence. The solution may be in letting them get away with the crime without punishment, but that overlaps with social knacks in a very big way that will take serious examining.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Paranoia: As I said - the delay can be useful in *some* situations. In others, you are trying to sabotage enemy operations and don't have that many days of time left! In that situation, you have the bizarre scenario that a less powerful Scion of Chaos can use this power successfully, while Loki can not - because he absolutely HAS to take advantage of the full duration. That does seem like a glitch to me, hence my suggestion of limiting the *maximum* possible delay, but giving the user the option not to use all of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider it done!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Sabot: I'll reiterate what I said about breakdown here. Though at this experience cost, Sabot should totally be the go-to boon if you insist on breaking Big Ben in some manner. Given that &quot;Big Ben&quot; refers to just one (admittedly very large) bell in Westminster Palace, I think it's totally okay to crack it to splinters with a demigod boon. Demigod Strength would do the same thing and preferably use it as a throwing weapon too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sabot should be able to absolutely shatter Big Ben like tissue paper, since Chaos 5 is granting +11 successes to all Chaos activation rolls! It is important to use the damage metric instead of a default &quot;stuff stops working&quot; metric, because you can keep damaging extremely tough things until they stop working, but you cannot beat extremely high difficulties.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Rebellion: Ah, yes. I'm still in the &quot;a scene is fifteen minutes or one action-packed sequence&quot; mindset. Do you plan on writing that out, too? It might be important to properly use your boons on another table.</div> </div> </div> </div>The duration of a scene is actually covered in Scion: Hero (page 171).<br /> <br /> <i>Scene: A period of game time characterized by a common theme or a single important event. One long night spent club-hopping with friends and rivals could be a single scene, even though the game\u2019s focus cuts between characters and might skip hours at a time. One combat is usually one scene.</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=161933#post161933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I'm sorry for being the resident curmudgeon, but I feel I'm most helpful when I speak my mind frankly. I do appreciate your effort and hope you can reform the mess that is the Scion rules.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I think your concerns are very helpful, and a big part of what goes into having a strong community. I can be quite the curmudgeon myself, so I completely understand the importance of speaking your mind and being a 'straight shooter'. You are definitely welcome here!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T03:26:44-07:00","id":164688,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay! The weather over here is awful - I felt that I was in such danger of melting down to an amorphous blob that I didn't want to risk getting near the Chaos purview.<br /> <br /> @Purviews and Epics: You equalized the costs so that a Purview and the Boons are at least not more expensive, but that is only one half of the problem. The other half is that almost no Boon (up to and including plenty of demigod material) is comparable to what you get for the same amount of XP in Epics. This is a problem of Boon power, and I don't see how this has been adressed. Epics are inherently more universally applicable, so the more specialized Boons should not be as powerful, but more powerful in their application. With a smattering of bonuses to a few actions and active abilities that are more limited in scope and also arguably weaker or at best equal to what Epics and Knacks can do, I think the problem remains unsolved.<br /> Of course, Scion players are used to the discrepancy, and most people do not play for optimal XP usage - your boons are fresh and in many cases creative, so I'm not surprised they're getting good reviews - also with respect to balance. In my opinion, that is because the problem is on a fundamental level, and I feel that many people have already become so accustomed to it that it no longer apperas to be one.<br /> Remember when we had a boon posted on the old forums specifically for obstructing one person's journey with countless strange happenings? I don't recall the exact level it was meant to have, but it was definitely demigod or higher. Spending that amount of XP on something as incredibily specific is something we have become so used to that nobody noted the extremely limited scope as a problem.<br /> <br /> Now obviously that does not apply to all powers. Immunity to Fire is good to have and not as easily available with Epic Stamina, and your Anarchy is (although I still find it conceptually confusing) is similar. But my feeling when I look at a boon like Breakdown is that the problem is one of the basic perspective on what a Boon needs to be capable of to justify the cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Breakdown: And that is why I would submit that breakdown needs to do more. I don't know what health levels you assign to common objects and at what point you would accept that they no longer function - since the boon obviously interacts with your systems for that and I didn't find one on the site, I find it hard to judge how much immediate effect you can get out of it. That is also why I prefer a language that is clear as to the result of the boon (&quot;no longer functions&quot;) if not the mechanical effect in health levels.<br /> <br /> @Anarchy: I think we can agree to disagree. But I want to remain on record with the statement that it's really weird a son of Loki can use the boon to withstand supernatural encouragement for mischief-making.<br /> <br /> @Chaos Theory: The Scion learns ONE result of his actions. The storyteller decides which result he learns. Obviously (to me), the potential for misleading information is huge, as any amount of deleterious consequences could remain unspoken, making anyone who acts on this knowledge a butterfly of doom. Taking up my earlier example - if mispronouncing the giants middle name is going to A) get a laugh out of the dour daughter of Hel and help you gain an unlikely ally with the Aesir, as well as B) anger him so much that he ends negotiations over a prized relic with a representative of your divine parent, these are two seperate results of one action that are both not particularly obvious. If the Scion learns just A, his actions are probably different from his actions if he just learns B.<br /> Hence why I'd tag on a warning about that kind of potentially dangerously incomplete information.<br /> <br /> You are of course right about Hornet's Nest, but my point was just that it was easier to prepare for than having an interesting non-obvious answer to any sort of potential action the player can use Chaos Theory with. Have you noticed any problems with improvising that?<br /> <br /> @Criticus: Aaah-HAA! I see. By my internal dictionary, &quot;cumulative&quot; requires a specification as to *what* the effect stacks with - the way it was written, I took it as meaning that it would be cumulative with other kinds of maluses. For what you describe, I would have expected something like &quot;cumulative -1 per round&quot;.<br /> <br /> @Gremlins: Okay. I have had enough saddening experiences with players asking really obvious or nearly-obvious rule questions that I prefer to specify even what I think should be clear from the context.<br /> <br /> @Disorder: Well, with social knacks, it is still clear you *did* the misdeed in question, people just don't care about it. If you use it to disrupt the chain of evidence in a critical way, then it's not even certain who did it. You could just give it a cost to do something to the effect &quot;any phyical evidence that turns up after the deed is done will be too inconclusive to clearly implicate the Scion&quot; and make it scale with the overtness of the deed.<br /> <br /> @Paranoia: Gee, glad to be of assistance! Though I'd still love to have something like it in combat time.<br /> <br /> @Rebellion: Okay-dokey.<br /> <br /> @Lord of Misrule: How does the change to Babel affect the target's own capacity to communicate? Not at all, or is that confused too?<br /> <br /> @Insanity: I have a long-standing pet peeve about the typical RPG depiction of &quot;madness&quot;, but in a mythological context, it makes perfect sense to use it. No problems here! Though now I wonder if Hera has this Boon..<br /> <br /> @Breaking the Chain: Does &quot;permanent until she activates it again&quot; mean that the previous activation is voided (so, only one realm of chaos per god, please) or just that it needs to be reactivated to reverse it?<br /> <br /> @Revolution: I'm not quite sure this needs to be a Chaos Ten boon.<br /> <br /> I think that's what I have to say about Chaos. *Goes back to the OP to check what else is done*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T12:43:55-07:00","id":165052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the delay! The weather over here is awful - I felt that I was in such danger of melting down to an amorphous blob that I didn't want to risk getting near the Chaos purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I do apologize if some of this seems like nonsense. I just finished my exams today, and thus, am a bit out of it at the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Purviews and Epics: You equalized the costs so that a Purview and the Boons are at least not more expensive, but that is only one half of the problem. The other half is that almost no Boon (up to and including plenty of demigod material) is comparable to what you get for the same amount of XP in Epics. This is a problem of Boon power, and I don't see how this has been adressed. Epics are inherently more universally applicable, so the more specialized Boons should not be as powerful, but more powerful in their application. With a smattering of bonuses to a few actions and active abilities that are more limited in scope and also arguably weaker or at best equal to what Epics and Knacks can do, I think the problem remains unsolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as we have said before, every single Boon costs six experience, no matter the Rank, just as all Knacks do. Each Dot of a Purview is purchased just like a Dot of an Epic Attribute, and each Dot comes with a free Boon from any rank equal, or lower than the Dot purchased. A Scion is able to buy any Boon from a Rank equal, or lesser than their Purview Rank for six points of experience.<br /> <br /> This change, as we have seen in our games, has equalized purchases of Epic Attributes and Purviews compared to the original state they were in, where people favored taking Epic Attributes. Additionally, Purviews all use their Purview Rank for all of their Boons, Epic Attributes now having no influence on Boons at all.<br /> <br /> Boons to have a different scale than Knacks in our system, but that is intentional. Knacks are going to be things that are used more often than Boons, and therefore both cost less, and have less dramatic effects. While Epics still effect all of your Derived Values, Purviews can be used to replace an Epic if one takes a Relic that does so. While it would be fairly expensive (Iry would have to give a ruling on the total number of Dots for it, I don't believe anyone has done so in our games yet), someone could take a body made of granite as a Relic, and use their Earth to calculate their Block DV, or a Scion riddled with insanity could take their very madness as a Relic, using Moon, or Chaos to calculate their MDV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Breakdown: And that is why I would submit that breakdown needs to do more. I don't know what health levels you assign to common objects and at what point you would accept that they no longer function - since the boon obviously interacts with your systems for that and I didn't find one on the site, I find it hard to judge how much immediate effect you can get out of it. That is also why I prefer a language that is clear as to the result of the boon (&quot;no longer functions&quot;) if not the mechanical effect in health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>We can eventually come up with a few basic examples of health levels for objects, but I believe the current take is to hope that Storytellers assign appropriate values to such things. The difficulty about spelling out exactly what &quot;no longer functions&quot; is that would likely be a very large list, since different objects will cease to function in different ways. Iry can likely explain this better than I can though, for I really am not the mechanics person. It is very much not my expertise, and I don't have a hand in any of the direct creation of mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Anarchy: I think we can agree to disagree. But I want to remain on record with the statement that it's really weird a son of Loki can use the boon to withstand supernatural encouragement for mischief-making.</div> </div> </div> </div>I entirely understand that this is likely a situation where we can agree to disagree. But, what we are trying to encapsulate is that chaos is a breach from all forms of control. So, even Loki attempting to convince a child of theirs to be chaotic would be something it could help resist, for Loki, in that situation, would be attempting to force the Scion along a path, and Chaos does not conform to anything, not even itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Chaos Theory: The Scion learns ONE result of his actions. The storyteller decides which result he learns. Obviously (to me), the potential for misleading information is huge, as any amount of deleterious consequences could remain unspoken, making anyone who acts on this knowledge a butterfly of doom. Taking up my earlier example - if mispronouncing the giants middle name is going to A) get a laugh out of the dour daughter of Hel and help you gain an unlikely ally with the Aesir, as well as B) anger him so much that he ends negotiations over a prized relic with a representative of your divine parent, these are two seperate results of one action that are both not particularly obvious. If the Scion learns just A, his actions are probably different from his actions if he just learns B.<br /> <br /> Hence why I'd tag on a warning about that kind of potentially dangerously incomplete information.<br /> <br /> You are of course right about Hornet's Nest, but my point was just that it was easier to prepare for than having an interesting non-obvious answer to any sort of potential action the player can use Chaos Theory with. Have you noticed any problems with improvising that?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we have never had any issue with players asking unexpected questions that are not planned for, with either Mystery, or any other power that gives you information. I, personally, have asked entirely strange questions out of utter paranoia with Mystery of entirely irrelevant things and gotten an answer. If it is something that the Storyteller themselves isn't sure of at the moment, they tend to make a choice and cement that decision in the story, such as the specifics of an NPCs familial relations.<br /> <br /> We may add a warning label to it, I suppose our hope that people are able to gather as much from the Boon itself may be misplaced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Criticus: Aaah-HAA! I see. By my internal dictionary, &quot;cumulative&quot; requires a specification as to *what* the effect stacks with - the way it was written, I took it as meaning that it would be cumulative with other kinds of maluses. For what you describe, I would have expected something like &quot;cumulative -1 per round&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, it has seemed obvious to all of our players thus far. We will look into that then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Gremlins: Okay. I have had enough saddening experiences with players asking really obvious or nearly-obvious rule questions that I prefer to specify even what I think should be clear from the context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people always will need some help understanding rules. Some people have an incredibly hard time taking information in visually, and some people, such as myself, am terrified of possibly accidentally cheating, thus double check every rule the first time I use it just to be sure, no matter how obvious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Disorder: Well, with social knacks, it is still clear you *did* the misdeed in question, people just don't care about it. If you use it to disrupt the chain of evidence in a critical way, then it's not even certain who did it. You could just give it a cost to do something to the effect &quot;any phyical evidence that turns up after the deed is done will be too inconclusive to clearly implicate the Scion&quot; and make it scale with the overtness of the deed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossover to a minor degree is okay to us as long as it makes sense. While someone could possibly have the ability to have everyone forgive them (Boys will be Boys [EDIT: Just reminded Boys will be Boys has been changed to Adoring Fans] or Blame James), those effects don't actually last any longer than one Scene in our system I believe. Though, I know we have not yet reached Epic Manipulation for revision. It being a long process, and us currently poking at Itztli in a rough draft sense, and getting ready to finish all Purviews up to Rank 4.<br /> <br /> So, while with Epic Socials, one could have everyone forgive them, it will not last forever. Someone who uses Disorder can just have themselves never suspected due to lack of evidence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Paranoia: Gee, glad to be of assistance! Though I'd still love to have something like it in combat time.</div> </div> </div> </div>We thought about that, but we worry that suddenly lashing out against an ally is a bit too close to old Chaos, filled with its random loonyness, drawn from the modern conception of Chaos. For the ancient world, it was incredibly different, with Chaos being a breakdown of order, of home, and society. So, our hopes are that the Boon would strike in one of these environments, and bring chaos, breaching the order of things, and what is just, in a place that is orderly.<br /> <br /> A battlefield is already a place of chaos, and disorder. The Boon is intended to, as Chaos was believed in the long past, break the order of things in a place that is normally orderly, such as a city, a home, or so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Lord of Misrule: How does the change to Babel affect the target's own capacity to communicate? Not at all, or is that confused too?</div> </div> </div> </div>The target's capacity to communicate is unchanged with Lord of Misrule, past the normal degree of utter dysfunction Babel causes. Without being improved by Lord of Misrule, Babel disrupts one's ability to communicate. Rendering Babel actually an incredibly useful tool against generals, and dangerous social opponents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Insanity: I have a long-standing pet peeve about the typical RPG depiction of &quot;madness&quot;, but in a mythological context, it makes perfect sense to use it. No problems here! Though now I wonder if Hera has this Boon..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this form of 'madness' is entirely intentional totally fictional. Both Moon and Chaos have madness associations for ancient peoples, but the way we have divided them is thus. Moon controls actual medical disorders, psychopathy, obsessive compulsive disorder, probably also things as mundane as learning disabilities, though that falls in the territory of 'probably never going to come up ever'. Chaos, on the other hand, brings with it the gibbering Dionysian madness, one where someone is taken up by chaos, and even the ability for rational thought is shattered like a pane of glass.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Breaking the Chain: Does &quot;permanent until she activates it again&quot; mean that the previous activation is voided (so, only one realm of chaos per god, please) or just that it needs to be reactivated to reverse it?</div> </div> </div> </div>When we designed this Boon, it was three am, so I am only fairly sure I am right with this one. I believe it means that the Chaos God can dismiss the effect by using the power once again. If I am wrong, Iry will correct me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Revolution: I'm not quite sure this needs to be a Chaos Ten boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally, Revolution was a high Demigod Boon, but we decided it should be Rank Ten just so it has no limitations. Dionysus could, though he would probably never, use this Boon and have the entire Dodekatheon rise up against Zeus, Hades, and Poseidon in an instant. Set could use it to dethrone Horus, and he probably used it to dethrone Osiris since no one but Isis and Horus really cared that he just butchered the king. It is a deceptively powerful Boon, and while it can be used to overthrown a country, it can too be used to overthrow a Pantheon, no matter how beloved, feared, or respected the current Pantheon Head is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=164688#post164688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's what I have to say about Chaos. *Goes back to the OP to check what else is done*</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. I hope this made any sense at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-10-2014, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T07:50:42-07:00","id":165904,"title":"","content":"I've also written a mail to you guys, some days ago. As Varygoode, feel free to re-post anything you e-mail to me over here in this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T11:21:37-07:00","id":166112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've also written a mail to you guys, some days ago. As Varygoode, feel free to re-post anything you e-mail to me over here in this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are just in the proccess of replying. I just finished my exams, and another of us just started up another summester of Uni, so, we are slightly on our back foot for the momnet. But, we will send off that email to you soon!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T12:58:56-07:00","id":166180,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>About Plain Bonus (+2, +3 etc)</b> </u><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">They fall by their own weight once in Demigod levels... not to mention Godhood. Maybe adjust the bonifications in order to let them grow proportionally to the Scion Legend would be a fine way to ensure they don't end being meaningless in high levels. </span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">I'm looking specially at persistent bonus. They certainly are useful at Hero level... but why not make them escalate? Just so we have more and more amazing Gods <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\">Looks like an older version was put in. All the aspect boons should begin with +2 at Hero, and properly increase to +4 at God. That's just enough to continue having a very realm impact, while not flooding the system with too many dice or success adders. This is going to become more and more prevalent as we revise each of the purviews.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Resistance Attributes</u></b><br /> I know i asked about it already... but i still don't understand. Why didn't you created mental and emotional resistance Attributes (aka Resolve and Composture)? Is there any special reason behind that? Because sure, you can charm someone with your Appearance or your Charisma to not lay that nasty mind spell on you... but it feels only logical you should have the option to just resist it. I'm thinking on Gods whose concepts are like &quot;Unstoppable&quot; or &quot;Indomitable&quot;. As that was my own character concept in Scion 1.0, i'm really curious about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be misunderstanding your question, but Charisma and Appearance both have knacks that allow you to substitute your Charisma/Appearance and Epic Charisma/Epic Appearance for your MDV against sentient creatures. This represents having such an overwhelming personality that people naturally do not want to attack you, or being so staggeringly attractive/hideous that you are too distracting to attack. Both of these knacks only apply towards sentient creatures (those that can have an actual reaction to you) and do not apply towards unattended supernatural effects, animate objects, or traps that target MDV for some reason.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- One idea we had about in the last game: Have you considered giving &quot;Core Abilities&quot; (that's it, Legend-free Boons) to the Gods, depending on his Legend? They could be tied to their Titles, (Like Tezcatlipoca, The Enemy of Both Sides) and a reflection of them (for example, in Tezcatlipoca maybe the ability to use a Chaos Purview for free, as many times in a session as his Legend or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">T<span style=\"color:#222222\">hey don't have even to be Boons. You could create Purview lists with this core powers, or just give some guidelines (like for instance do not use this as an excuse for infinite lightnings or some kind of fireball Boon) to let the players come up with their own amazing ideas. It would help to personalize their Scions a great deal more!</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#222222\">We put your idea on the table and talked about it for a while, hashing out all the details and seeing what it added and what it took away from the game. We decided that it had too much potential to disrupt the legend economy. However! Once per game, you may activate a knack or boon from one of your Associated Attributes or Purviews and the base legend and willpower cost becomes free. You must still pay for any legend and willpower cost beyond the base.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Question time!</u></b><br /> - Please explain the<b> Aesir Phantom Dots</b> in Strenght and Resilience. Are they essentially normal, usual dots? I mean, they are always active, for free? Would they take a God to surpass her maximum 11 dots of strenght or stamina?</div> </div> </div> </div>Phantom dots count as normal dots for the purposes of rolling dice and calculating derived values. However, Phantom Dots are always on top of normal dots, and can go over the normal limit for Attributes, Abilities, Purviews. An Aesir with 7 phantom dots could be rocking 18 Strength and 18 Stamina!</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Concerning the Egyptian Gods...</b><br /> - Seth: I think his Associated Purview should be War, not Guardian. Of course, he protects the Solar Barge, but he makes it through violence; not really behind a shield, or keeping himself on the Solar Barge. No. He plungs into the darkness, fighting Apep with silver knifes in the deep shadows that are the titan's lair. He is prideful and violent and excessive. The God of the Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>First allow me to preface this by saying that I am no Anne, and her shoes will be sorely missed. Among the core four gaming groups that playtest the Scion 2.0 rules, we have a decent number of experts in specific fields, but none who are so well versed across such a huge variety of mythologies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\">With that said, Seth may have been an extremely violent personality, but he leads no armies and demonstrates no great military tactics beyond being badass enough to personally take on some of the greatest threats to his pantheon. I am certain he has some dots of the war purview, but being excellent at killing people does not make one a god of war. Seth not only defends the solar barque, but also serves as the warden who guards the boundaries of the southern Egyptian desert, and onetime protector to the folk of the Upper Kingdom. People would invoke his name and make rites so that they could have safe crossing the deserts, and be defended from their enemies.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Horus:<br /> I always found Horus intriguing. On one hand, he is a prideful warrior, and a deadly one. On the other side, he's cunning, and more than happy to settle things with shameless treachery when he fights Seth for Osiris Crown. But on the other hand, he's hot tempered and short sighted (he in fact comes close to kill his own mother, enraged when she interferes with one of the combats he fought against Seth) I think Epic Wits fits him perfectly. But Epic Manipulation? He's more kind of Warrior God, not so much... politician, if you excuse me. Why not emphasize his role (and create in this way a stark contrast with Seth) giving him Epic Dexterity instead?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\">Harseisis is definitely a warrior god known for his prowess in battle (especially when he loses his eyes), and I think you make a lot of good points about Epic Dexterity. There is a kind of duality in his myths, especially those regarding Seth. He reaches around to capture semen from Seth after they sleep together, which implies he had enough dexterity to avoid notice from Seth, and enough manipulation to convince Seth that his conquest was true. He puts his own semen into the salad, which once again implies he had enough dexterity to avoid notice from Seth, and enough manipulation to convince Seth that there was nothing suspicious about the salad. Tilting the scales back in favor of manipulation, Harseisis convinced Seth to have sex with him in the first place (and totally not to trick him).<br /> <br /> In short, you can see why there is a lot of back and forth. For right now, we are not going to be overhauling the pantheons because we have a huge amount of respect for the fine people who ran Gotham By Night. We stand by their research</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165904#post165904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Random thought:</u></b><br /> - I absolutely loved the description of the Lammasu, the winged bulls sent by Marduk... i mean, <b>THE GREAT AND GLORIOUS MARDUK.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><b>THE AMAZING AND POWERFUL MARDUK</b> is the only god allowed to break the Fourth Wall. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 06-11-2014, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T19:12:38-07:00","id":166445,"title":"","content":"If you are going to have an Epic Stamina knack like Devourer, I would like, nay, REQUIRE something to let me bite into anything, as I must eat a battleship for my Legend. So let it be written, so let it be done.<br /> <br /> I am following this for our own game. I like what you have done very much. You all have clearly gone through with the eyes of experienced gamers and made lots of &quot;that's f'in stupid&quot; calls and fixed it. Bravo!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T19:31:20-07:00","id":166454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raleel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166445#post166445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are going to have an Epic Stamina knack like Devourer, I would like, nay, REQUIRE something to let me bite into anything, as I must eat a battleship for my Legend. So let it be written, so let it be done.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could entirely be accomplished through Epic Strength, for biting into something is using, well, using your strength. Knacks that would work well for that are Holy Rampage, and Divine Rampage. Additionally, for example, if someone was playing a Scion with fire, and focusing on the all consuming aspect of it, they could take a Relic that changes the roll for 'consuming' things such as in this case to a Fire + Brawl roll for two Dots. Does that work for you?<br /> <br /> And thank you very much for your compliments. Let us know if you have any questions, or things that pop in in your game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-11-2014, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T21:25:36-07:00","id":166551,"title":"","content":"Yea, that should be fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T23:47:16-07:00","id":166683,"title":"","content":"I know you say on your site that Magic &amp; Prophecy will be at the end of your rewrites, but I was wondering if you folks could give a basic outline on how to conform them to your new Fates system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T01:48:00-07:00","id":166706,"title":"","content":"@Boons and Purviews: What you write is interesting, but I don't feel that it adresses my point. I already said that I can imagine you got positive feedback from your groups, including about balance. I argue that this is because with RAW Scion, we have acquired twisted expectations of the relative power level of a boon compared to how specific it is.<br /> To bring it down to a simple example, it's hard for me to imagine how any of your low-level boons that deals with mental inflence has a &quot;more dramatic&quot; effect that Instant Hypnosis, which could arguably be used to duplicate most of their effects.<br /> <br /> @Breakdown: This is a matter of principles again, but I hope it's fairly obvious. If the balance of your boon hinges on &quot;hope that the Storyteller assigns apppropriate values ...&quot; than you might not have written mechanics for it at all. Iry argued that using health levels instead of an unambigous result like &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;phyically intact yet nonfunctional&quot; or whatever you fancy as appropriate at this level was important. But if you don't provide any meaningful examples for what one less health level for an object DOES, this Boon is vaporware. I can't judge if this is balanced because it's power depends purely on the whims of the storyteller. Was that the outcome you were going for?<br /> <br /> @Chaos Theory: I would never use this boon or advise anyone to take it as written. It comes down to a big gamble on your ability to judge if the ST is feeling mischievous or not today. He may tell you X will follow from your course of action (and you can decide that Y won't), but with the number of other consequences he can leave unspoken being way more than the rest of the alphabet, you might as well just do what ordinary people do and resort to conjecture.<br /> At least that doesn't invite the ironic hand of fate/the ST as much as using a boon that gives you one piece of definitely true (but perhaps irrelevant in the face of other consequences) info. It would be a lot better if the boon gave you the results in order of importance for your current goal.<br /> <br /> @Gremlins: Maybe, but again - Iry explained their mook status as something that seemed obvious to him, but it really helps to take a more naive perspective when writing RULES (tm) - not just notes for your own table.<br /> <br /> @Paranoia: Hmm. Perhaps in War, then?<br /> <br /> @Mystery: As opposed to Chaos Theory, I would possibly use this boon, because while it doesn't specifically say the ST should not leave large, crucial pieces of info unsaid, at least I could argue that that isn't in the spirit of this boon.<br /> I still won't really like any solution for Mystery that keeps it a single-boon, once-per-story purview after r_b_borgstrom gave us his take on it as a fully fledged purview years ago. But alas, many people seem to insist for some strange reason on just fixing one of Prophecy and Mystery that way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T02:51:29-07:00","id":166784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166683#post166683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know you say on your site that Magic &amp; Prophecy will be at the end of your rewrites, but I was wondering if you folks could give a basic outline on how to conform them to your new Fates system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I know you are running some games right now, I dove in and cleaned up both the Magic &amp; Prophecy purviews to conform to our Fates system. Please keep in mind this is not a full blown revision of those purviews, just cleaning house and making sure everything functions properly under the Scion 2.0 rules. Let me know if I missed anything!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T03:51:27-07:00","id":166832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Boons and Purviews: What you write is interesting, but I don't feel that it adresses my point. I already said that I can imagine you got positive feedback from your groups, including about balance. I argue that this is because with RAW Scion, we have acquired twisted expectations of the relative power level of a boon compared to how specific it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>While many of us have plenty of experience with RAW Scion (and I am a huge rules lawyer in general), we have also spent quite a while using most of the Gotham By Night rules and their respective power levels. In fact, since we enjoy sharing Scion with new players, there are a few people in our groups who have never experienced Scion any other way except Gotham By Night and Scion 2.0!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To bring it down to a simple example, it's hard for me to imagine how any of your low-level boons that deals with mental inflence has a &quot;more dramatic&quot; effect that Instant Hypnosis, which could arguably be used to duplicate most of their effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knacks are a funny thing, because they can range from almost useless to absolute rockstars. We are going to shoot for making them a little more balanced, such as reducing the duration of many social knacks to last an entire scene instead of having nearly permanent durations. And we definitely have not gotten around to Epic Manipulation yet (though quite a few things are in the pipeline and being playtested).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Breakdown: This is a matter of principles again, but I hope it's fairly obvious. If the balance of your boon hinges on &quot;hope that the Storyteller assigns apppropriate values ...&quot; than you might not have written mechanics for it at all. Iry argued that using health levels instead of an unambigous result like &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;phyically intact yet nonfunctional&quot; or whatever you fancy as appropriate at this level was important. But if you don't provide any meaningful examples for what one less health level for an object DOES, this Boon is vaporware. I can't judge if this is balanced because it's power depends purely on the whims of the storyteller. Was that the outcome you were going for?</div> </div> </div> </div>There first thing going on here relates to mechanics. You can find information on object health levels located in Scion: Hero (page 201). We have gotten rid of hardness, but there are several examples of how many health levels various objects have, but in no way is it possible to represent every single kind of object. A character might need to break through a wooden door, a steel door, a stygian iron door, a shield door of Asgard, or a ten mile wide door leading to the depths of some horrible titan realm. Part of the passage reads:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Inanimate objects can take a set number of health levels of damage before they are destroyed. When they have lost half of those health levels, they are considered \u201cdamaged,\u201d which inhibits their natural functions. If a tool, it functions at a penalty. If a wall, it no longer keeps things out. The object is not a complete failure until it is destroyed\u2014a damaged wall keeps the flow of intruders to a trickle, for example\u2014but sometimes characters need do no more than damage an object.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The second thing going on here relates to arbitrary power levels. They exist. The storyteller decides how many health boxes her monsters have, what their defenses are, how hard they hit, and any supernatural effects they might possess. In this way, the power level of combat characters also depends entirely on the whims of the storyteller. The job of the storyteller is to decide how difficult certain challenges are, relative to the capabilities of her band, and which characters are participating in a scene.<br /> <br /> The storyteller likewise decides how much Soak DV and Health any given object has.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Chaos Theory: I would never use this boon or advise anyone to take it as written. It comes down to a big gamble on your ability to judge if the ST is feeling mischievous or not today. He may tell you X will follow from your course of action (and you can decide that Y won't), but with the number of other consequences he can leave unspoken being way more than the rest of the alphabet, you might as well just do what ordinary people do and resort to conjecture.<br /> At least that doesn't invite the ironic hand of fate/the ST as much as using a boon that gives you one piece of definitely true (but perhaps irrelevant in the face of other consequences) info. It would be a lot better if the boon gave you the results in order of importance for your current goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand your objection, but it is also true of Prophecy, Mystery, and every time your character rolls Perception, Intelligence, or Wits to discover some piece of information, understand something, or catch something said in a conversation. If your storyteller is feeling mischievous you have more to worry about than Chaos Theory, which functions as a useful tool to discern things even if your character lacks any of those other methods.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Gremlins: Maybe, but again - Iry explained their mook status as something that seemed obvious to him, but it really helps to take a more naive perspective when writing RULES (tm) - not just notes for your own table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree! Some things can seem self-evident to us, and should be pointed out if they need further explaining.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Paranoia: Hmm. Perhaps in War, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely War.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166706#post166706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Mystery: As opposed to Chaos Theory, I would possibly use this boon, because while it doesn't specifically say the ST should not leave large, crucial pieces of info unsaid, at least I could argue that that isn't in the spirit of this boon.<br /> I still won't really like any solution for Mystery that keeps it a single-boon, once-per-story purview after r_b_borgstrom gave us his take on it as a fully fledged purview years ago. But alas, many people seem to insist for some strange reason on just fixing one of Prophecy and Mystery that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a fair bit of of overlap between R_B_Borgstrom Mystery, Mephit James Mystery, Terribly Uncreative Mystery, and JSR Prophecy. At some point we may give it a complete overhaul, along with unique boons for every dot, but it successfully fits the mythological job it needs to perform right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 06-12-2014, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T04:18:40-07:00","id":166841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165052#post165052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The target's capacity to communicate is unchanged with Lord of Misrule, past the normal degree of utter dysfunction Babel causes. Without being improved by Lord of Misrule, Babel disrupts one's ability to communicate. Rendering Babel actually an incredibly useful tool against generals, and dangerous social opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher is absolutely correct. When Lord of Misrule is used, the target misunderstands everything being communicated to her, but other people continue to be unable to understand anything the target communicates at all. The person even misunderstands attempts to explain that they are making no sense. Allow me to provide a comedic example of Jane being hit with Babel + Lord of Misrule:<br /> <br /> <i>John: That bastard just uttered some nonsense and then slipped away, we have to give chase!<br /> Jane: What? You've fallen hopelessly in love with that person? He must have done something to you!<br /> John: Wh... What are you saying? I don't understand. We need to CATCH HIM!<br /> Jane: I'm not going to let you run off with him! You're clearly under his spell!</i><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=165052#post165052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we designed this Boon, it was three am, so I am only fairly sure I am right with this one. I believe it means that the Chaos God can dismiss the effect by using the power once again. If I am wrong, Iry will correct me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Activating one of the Purview Home style boons immediately ends any other previous activations of that boon. A Chaos god can only have one Breaking The Chain activate at once, but she could also have a Sunken Realm and Animal Sanctuary active at the same time (overlapping or someplace else, as she desires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T07:01:39-07:00","id":166907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166784#post166784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I know you are running some games right now, I dove in and cleaned up both the Magic &amp; Prophecy purviews to conform to our Fates system. Please keep in mind this is not a full blown revision of those purviews, just cleaning house and making sure everything functions properly under the Scion 2.0 rules. Let me know if I missed anything!</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh my gosh thank you so much! I'll let you know if there's anything missing or weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T09:04:59-07:00","id":166976,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers, Watcher, Iry. One thing, by the way. I don't know if i did &quot;sound&quot; impatient about having the answers: if it was like that, i'm sorry, didn't intend to; it was just a commentary!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166454#post166454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, for example, if someone was playing a Scion with fire, and focusing on the all consuming aspect of it, they could take a Relic that changes the roll for 'consuming' things such as in this case to a Fire + Brawl roll for two Dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was something i've already read in Scion 2.0 in some relics, i think, and i find it extremely interesting. Could you please explain this new mechanic? You can tie some action to another combination of Skill + Ability different than the one that should be logical for it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166180#post166180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like an older version was put in. All the aspect boons should begin with +2 at Hero, and properly increase to +4 at God. That's just enough to continue having a very realm impact, while not flooding the system with too many dice or success adders. This is going to become more and more prevalent as we revise each of the purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great! Then i have nothing more to say about it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166180#post166180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be misunderstanding your question, but Charisma and Appearance both have knacks that allow you to substitute your Charisma/Appearance and Epic Charisma/Epic Appearance for your MDV against sentient creatures. This represents having such an overwhelming personality that people naturally do not want to attack you, or being so staggeringly attractive/hideous that you are too distracting to attack. Both of these knacks only apply towards sentient creatures (those that can have an actual reaction to you) and do not apply towards unattended supernatural effects, animate objects, or traps that target MDV for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was Watcher's answer. It's ok i guess, but i wasn't thinking on fighting back the effect interchanging your MDV with your Charisma and/or Appearance; i get the explanation, but just feels... a little weird. I'm going for something much more straightforward and simple: How do you protray a God who is neither Charsimatic nor Amazingly beutiful / hideous, but just some serious stubborn motherf****r who just won't stand down? Take Odin, for instance. His increible Resolve, hanging from the tree nice days. Focusing in the power to achieve. Fighting back the pain, and the exhaustion. Fighting back the Laws of the World. (I'm sure i could find another examples of Composure-heavy Godly situations, but right now they don't come to mind).<br /> <br /> That's the kind of feeling i'm searching. Something like &quot;Yeah, try to play with my head. Try to seizure my heart. My soul is bathing in Icor, you fool. You cannot stop me with orders or veils&quot;. <br /> <br /> I've always felt that was weir not having Mental and Emotional Resistance Attributes in Scion, taking in account the sheer amount of Gods and Goddess adept at playing with feelings, thoughts and illusions. Why didn't you consider changing it, like NWoD? Is there some reasion behind it? Maybe they are not &quot;flashy&quot; (you could read it as &quot;impressive&quot;, in a godly way) as the other attributes?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking... maybe the answer could be some news boons in Guardian referring to resisting mind or emotional control, a la Moon?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166180#post166180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We put your idea on the table and talked about it for a while, hashing out all the details and seeing what it added and what it took away from the game. We decided that it had too much potential to disrupt the legend economy. However! Once per game, you may activate a knack or boon from one of your Associated Attributes or Purviews and the base legend and willpower cost becomes free. You must still pay for any legend and willpower cost beyond the base.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! That would fit nicely. (I admit i'm not much of a rules savvy player... i hadn't even thought about the Legend economy. It just seemed cool xD)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166180#post166180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said, Seth may have been an extremely violent personality, but he leads no armies and demonstrates no great military tactics beyond being badass enough to personally take on some of the greatest threats to his pantheon. I am certain he has some dots of the war purview, but being excellent at killing people does not make one a god of war. Seth not only defends the solar barque, but also serves as the warden who guards the boundaries of the southern Egyptian desert, and onetime protector to the folk of the Upper Kingdom. People would invoke his name and make rites so that they could have safe crossing the deserts, and be defended from their enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't think about his protector role in that way, good point. (Neither in the military tactics, Seth was seen as somewhat straightforward xD) The thing is, they way i've been reading about Seth, it seems that they prayed to him in order to protect them... in a similar way in which they prayed to Sekhmet to keep the diseases away. Not so much &quot;protect me&quot; as &quot;please please please, don't smite me&quot;. More like &quot;keep your powerful eyes off me and on my enemies&quot;. Anyway, in fact was the Warden of the Upper Kingdom, so i guess Guardian could fit, putting some aesthetical dangerous vibe in it. And what about giving him Darkness? What do you think about that? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166180#post166180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harseisis is definitely a warrior god known for his prowess in battle (especially when he loses his eyes), and I think you make a lot of good points about Epic Dexterity. There is a kind of duality in his myths, especially those regarding Seth. He reaches around to capture semen from Seth after they sleep together, which implies he had enough dexterity to avoid notice from Seth, and enough manipulation to convince Seth that his conquest was true. He puts his own semen into the salad, which once again implies he had enough dexterity to avoid notice from Seth, and enough manipulation to convince Seth that there was nothing suspicious about the salad. Tilting the scales back in favor of manipulation, Harseisis convinced Seth to have sex with him in the first place (and totally not to trick him).<br /> <br /> In short, you can see why there is a lot of back and forth. For right now, we are not going to be overhauling the pantheons because we have a huge amount of respect for the fine people who ran Gotham By Night. We stand by their research]</div> </div> </div> </div>Just in those two sexual examples i was thinking when i was saying &quot;yes to Epic Wits&quot; and &quot;no to Epic Manipulation&quot;. To me, those two actions seems more cunning (now's the moment, let's do it!) that carefully planning ahead (manipulatively lying to Set). And as i said, Seth was kind of straigtforward, not really much of a sharp-witted god. <br /> <br /> Anyway, of course i get that this is open to interpretation, and in no way i'm going to bitch about it. Is just i love the egiptian gods, and those two things seemed curious to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T10:10:54-07:00","id":167026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166976#post166976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for your answers, Watcher, Iry. One thing, by the way. I don't know if i did &quot;sound&quot; impatient about having the answers: if it was like that, i'm sorry, didn't intend to; it was just a commentary!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no worries. You have not come off as impatient at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166976#post166976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was something i've already read in Scion 2.0 in some relics, i think, and i find it extremely interesting. Could you please explain this new mechanic? You can tie some action to another combination of Skill + Ability different than the one that should be logical for it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. Two Dots of a Relic or Guide will let you change the Attribute related to a roll, or value, not the Ability. It would cost an additional, or independent two Dots to change an Ability on a roll.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a young Theoi has a bow that changes Levin' Fury from Thunder + Thrown to Thunder + Marksmanship for two Dots. Additionally, with the aforementioned madness Relic, someone could change their MDV calculation from using Intelligence/Wits/Charisma/Appearance to Justice if they so wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166976#post166976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that was Watcher's answer. It's ok i guess, but i wasn't thinking on fighting back the effect interchanging your MDV with your Charisma and/or Appearance; i get the explanation, but just feels... a little weird. I'm going for something much more straightforward and simple: How do you protray a God who is neither Charsimatic nor Amazingly beutiful / hideous, but just some serious stubborn motherf****r who just won't stand down? Take Odin, for instance. His increible Resolve, hanging from the tree nice days. Focusing in the power to achieve. Fighting back the pain, and the exhaustion. Fighting back the Laws of the World. (I'm sure i could find another examples of Composure-heavy Godly situations, but right now they don't come to mind).<br /> <br /> That's the kind of feeling i'm searching. Something like &quot;Yeah, try to play with my head. Try to seizure my heart. My soul is bathing in Icor, you fool. You cannot stop me with orders or veils&quot;.<br /> <br /> I've always felt that was weir not having Mental and Emotional Resistance Attributes in Scion, taking in account the sheer amount of Gods and Goddess adept at playing with feelings, thoughts and illusions. Why didn't you consider changing it, like NWoD? Is there some reasion behind it? Maybe they are not &quot;flashy&quot; (you could read it as &quot;impressive&quot;, in a godly way) as the other attributes?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking... maybe the answer could be some news boons in Guardian referring to resisting mind or emotional control, a la Moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if we didn't explain that clearly enough. Epic Appearance and Epic Charisma can be used for your MDV if you spend experience or use your free Knacks to buy some Knacks to do so. At base, MDV is calculated through your Epic Wits, or your Epic Intelligence. Those would be the values you are thinking of. Intelligence is an Indominable Mind, while Epic Wits is that you are working too quickly to be ensnared.<br /> <br /> Odin actually probably doesn't have an amazing MDV though, since he does not have Integrity favored. Since your Dots in Abilities limit the amount of Autosuccesses you can use from Purviews or Epic Attributes (you may only use the Autosuccesses from a number of Dots equal to the number of Dots in the related Ability). Because of this, Odin, for example, since he lacks maxed out Integrity, will not have as high an MDV as Thoth, who rocks both Epic Intelligence and Integrity favored.<br /> <br /> So, the reason that we didn't create entirely new stats for it is because they already exist. Your Epic Wits, and Epic Intelligence function as your unstoppable minds, and your Integrity is how bloody minded and stubborn you are.<br /> <br /> Emotional control resisting Purview is actually going to be Frost though. Moon brings extremes of emotion, Chaos brings wild emotions, Fire is personal incredibly extreme emotions, and Frost is a sapping of emotions. (Represented through Virtues)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166976#post166976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hadn't think about his protector role in that way, good point. (Neither in the military tactics, Seth was seen as somewhat straightforward xD) The thing is, they way i've been reading about Seth, it seems that they prayed to him in order to protect them... in a similar way in which they prayed to Sekhmet to keep the diseases away. Not so much &quot;protect me&quot; as &quot;please please please, don't smite me&quot;. More like &quot;keep your powerful eyes off me and on my enemies&quot;. Anyway, in fact was the Warden of the Upper Kingdom, so i guess Guardian could fit, putting some aesthetical dangerous vibe in it. And what about giving him Darkness? What do you think about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know of any myths, or cult worship that label him as a Darkness God, so he probably doesn't have Darkness. Do you have any of those? I'm really not that good with Egypt.<br /> <br /> And, they actually prayed to him not out of fear, but because he was the protector. Sekhmet is an uncontrollable force, and incredibly dangerous, so you would pray to her that she not smite you, but you would just pray to Set (before his worshipers got all messed up by the rise of the cult of Isis and Osiris) to have him watch over you. The Scion books make Set out to be a really horrible guy, but he's honestly not that bad at all in terms of the Divinities. All he did was kill his brother, that's, like, mundane stuff compared to most of the Gods.<br /> <br /> Hell, Horus may not even be Osiris' son and he actually isn't the true heir if someone uses the story hook on Isis' page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=166976#post166976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just in those two sexual examples i was thinking when i was saying &quot;yes to Epic Wits&quot; and &quot;no to Epic Manipulation&quot;. To me, those two actions seems more cunning (now's the moment, let's do it!) that carefully planning ahead (manipulatively lying to Set). And as i said, Seth was kind of straigtforward, not really much of a sharp-witted god.<br /> <br /> Anyway, of course i get that this is open to interpretation, and in no way i'm going to bitch about it. Is just i love the egiptian gods, and those two things seemed curious to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Horus' Epic Manipulation also comes from the fact that he cheated his way through all of the contests with Set, and not a single member of his Pantheon noticed. In a Pantheon of believers in utter justice, Horus cheated, and he cheated a lot during an /incredibly/ important thing. And, no one knows he did. No one noticed, no one questions it, not even Set when it is blatantly obvious to us in the seat of the audience.<br /> <br /> That's why Horus has Epic Manipulation. He stole his crown through cheating, and convinced an entire Pantheon of Gods with Order that he didn't. That's truckloads of Epic Manipulation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T12:25:21-07:00","id":167137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=167026#post167026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sort of. Two Dots of a Relic or Guide will let you change the Attribute related to a roll, or value, not the Ability. It would cost an additional, or independent two Dots to change an Ability on a roll.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a young Theoi has a bow that changes Levin' Fury from Thunder + Thrown to Thunder + Marksmanship for two Dots. Additionally, with the aforementioned madness Relic, someone could change their MDV calculation from using Intelligence/Wits/Charisma/Appearance to Justice if they so wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher is correct. I normally charge <b>2 Dots</b> to change an Attribute, Purview or Ability into something else. This only applies to a single knack, single boon, or similar limited benefit per purchase. Bigger effects which include changing something important like Dodge DV, Soak DV, Mental DV, or something else huge and fundamental to the game are dramatically more expensive.<br /> <br /> It is not listed anywhere on the website, but I use a <b>Scaling Dot</b> cost which requires the guide or relic to always be equal to your Permanent Legend -1 (but always a minimum of 5 Dots). These powerful guides and relics tend to have a lot more plot hooks attached to them, more dramatic consequences, and tend to become a defining signature of the character in question. But this is just a personal preference of mine, instead of something written directly into Scion 2.0. I enjoy a small number of extremely memorable guides and relics, than a large number of less sentimental ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that was Watcher's answer. It's ok i guess, but i wasn't thinking on fighting back the effect interchanging your MDV with your Charisma and/or Appearance; i get the explanation, but just feels... a little weird. I'm going for something much more straightforward and simple: How do you protray a God who is neither Charsimatic nor Amazingly beutiful / hideous, but just some serious stubborn motherf****r who just won't stand down? Take Odin, for instance. His increible Resolve, hanging from the tree nice days. Focusing in the power to achieve. Fighting back the pain, and the exhaustion. Fighting back the Laws of the World. (I'm sure i could find another examples of Composure-heavy Godly situations, but right now they don't come to mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental resistance through sheer overwhelming Resolve is covered by Intelligence. Intelligence represents the sheer force or &quot;lifting capacity&quot; of your brain. This can be roleplayed a number of different ways; the mental power house who brute forces their way through social influences and says &quot;NO!&quot; is just as valid a character concept as the brilliant researcher who analyzes the situation and comes up with an effective counter.<br /> <br /> Composure is covered by Manipulation. The roll for others to sense your motivations and discern information about your personality is (Perception + Empathy) and is contested by your (Manipulation + Empathy). Someone with a high Manipulation + Empathy score can cover their own feelings so others can only see the emotions that the character wants to portray (even false emotions); this can range from an emotionless poker face to appearing sincerely angry when you feel no such thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 06-12-2014, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T14:54:48-07:00","id":169282,"title":"","content":"@Information Gathering:<br /> <br /> <b>I do not need to be told obvious facts about all of roleplaying</b>. Please stop doing that. It is deeply frustrating to read and made me ignore this thread on purpose for a while. If you do feel I really need to be told that RPGs require trust in the storyteller, you should not have a discussion with me.<br /> <br /> Of course it is trivially true that you will always need to trust the ST with the information he gives you, and of course a jackass genie can twist any statement on it's back and make any information given misleading. But as with all trivially true statements, it also fails to matter in the argument it is presented in.<br /> <br /> My point is that this power, in the way you have presented it, does not discourage this kind of behaviour. Despite your claims that this problem holds true for all information presented by the ST ever, your adaption of Mystery has some basic jackassery protection clauses built into it, while Chaos Theory does not. So either Chaos Theory is deliberately designed to be a gateway for jackass behaviour, or this is a design oversight. Take your pick or leave it, I'll not bother further with it at this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Principles (everything else)<br /> <br /> You are still arguing beside the point. My argument is that a higher power level for boons than you have is warranted because they are often a lot more specific than epic attributes and knacks while the cost is the same. Since the pragmatic power of a tool depends on versatility and strength, boons backed up by purviews are still weaker than knacks backed up by epics.<br /> <br /> Safe for a few outliers, hero-level boons are negligible in Scion RAW. You made them cheaper, but you also got rid of all outliers, so they're still negligible if you don't want them for flavor. I don't see how GBN was any different. One good thing I have seen is putting the function of &quot;Come Hither&quot; into a Water Boon. That one is *good* because it's much more broadly applicable than you allow most other boons to be. But don't you see how it's a problem that almost any other boon is just as strong (same resistance test) but much more narrow in application?<br /> <br /> Another thing that I will stress one last time is that Scion - as well as every other thing by WW and it's successor I have read so far - is a badly designed game with even worse mechanical guidance for players and storytellers. For all the (often bad) storytelling advice, the pre-made characters and enemies are trash and too few by far for a whole Scion career. And that's with a setting that has a next-to bottomless supply of public source inspiration for monsters.<br /> Scion also has absolutely no rules for what twenty successes on an Intelligence + Medicine roll even mean. And what the hell a player would get out of taking Arete (Medicine). The underlying problem with the game is that there is no functioning framework for anything. Powers and abilities just float in a big sea of nothing and arbitrary ST decisions. Is taking Arete in academic skill X a good idea? My gut says no, but it's completely up in the air, depending on who your storyteller is. And every time I poke you to find out what your idea of the framework is, the answer is &quot;that would be up to the ST to decide&quot;. You are not designing a game that way.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine a D&amp;D campaign where the ST absolutely *has* to design the opposition, down to the hitpoints and hardness of structures by arbitrary decree or fiddling around with enemy statblocks from two or five levels lower? Or set the DC for trapfinding, tracking and discovering a secret door all by himself? D&amp;D has a website with hundreds of free monsters all over the level curve, and unless your campaign is incompatible with sixteen different kinds of dragons, you can easily find something pre-made for the supported levels.<br /> My point is not that D&amp;D is the superior game. My point is that in the design of D&amp;D, the designers at least bothered to do their goddamned job.<br /> <br /> Now some people *like* to improvise all of that and will throw out all of that guidance. But designing a game includes dealing with this kind of minutae, even if Scion ignored for the most part. Scion is an emaciated skeleton of a game. If you make it your mission to improve it, I would submit you will need to put all the missing meat on it, too.<br /> <br /> A bunch of stats for relevant objects over twelve levels wouldn't be much meat to write up, and be re-useable for many other purposes. It would also show you how well Breakdown and Epic Strength knacks perform against each other at each level and allow you to make an informed decision if that's working as intended or not. With your current position, you just leave that to the improvisational ability of the ST. And you literally do not know and apparently do not really care if your specialized Chaos boon is superior to &quot;a good whack with a legendary hammer&quot; at legend six.<br /> <br /> All you're doing at this point is rearranging the bones in the hope that the skeleton of Scion will start walking. But almost everything that needs to be done for that to happen is something you give the ST zero assisstance for.<br /> <br /> Your response to this so far boils down to &quot;we got good feedback&quot;, &quot;ultimately, it's all in the hands of the ST anyway&quot; and &quot;maybe something about knacks will change, too&quot;. Which is nice for you, but doesn't advance this discussion in a meaningful way. And since most relevant comparison points are still WIPs, literally every possible argument I can make can be deflected with &quot;It'll be balanced when we're done&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sigh.<br /> <br /> I think I'll forego any argument about design principles and restrain myself to pointing out glitches at this point. The gist of everything else I have to say is stated above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2601-nachtigallerator","name":"Nachtigallerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T17:55:12-07:00","id":169369,"title":"","content":"Nachtigallerator, I absolutely love the feedback you've given so far. I am incredibly interested in you pointing out more glitches. I'm running 2 games in Scion 2.0 and would love to continue improving things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:03:57-07:00","id":169374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I do not need to be told obvious facts about all of roleplaying</b>. Please stop doing that. It is deeply frustrating to read and made me ignore this thread on purpose for a while. If you do feel I really need to be told that RPGs require trust in the storyteller, you should not have a discussion with me.<br /> <br /> Of course it is trivially true that you will always need to trust the ST with the information he gives you, and of course a jackass genie can twist any statement on it's back and make any information given misleading. But as with all trivially true statements, it also fails to matter in the argument it is presented in.<br /> <br /> My point is that this power, in the way you have presented it, does not discourage this kind of behaviour. Despite your claims that this problem holds true for all information presented by the ST ever, your adaption of Mystery has some basic jackassery protection clauses built into it, while Chaos Theory does not. So either Chaos Theory is deliberately designed to be a gateway for jackass behaviour, or this is a design oversight. Take your pick or leave it, I'll not bother further with it at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds more like you've had experience with storytellers who are either a) assholes already and b) antagonistic to their players which has biased your outlook on anything that really leaves the fate up in the ST's hands. In which case, I'd apologize but we're not here to check and balance against jerks who like to abuse the fun of being a GM. If these boons bother you so much, ban them from the game, or request that the ST not allow them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now some people *like* to improvise all of that and will throw out all of that guidance. But designing a game includes dealing with this kind of minutae, even if Scion ignored for the most part. Scion is an emaciated skeleton of a game. If you make it your mission to improve it, I would submit you will need to put all the missing meat on it, too.<br /> <br /> A bunch of stats for relevant objects over twelve levels wouldn't be much meat to write up, and be re-useable for many other purposes. It would also show you how well Breakdown and Epic Strength knacks perform against each other at each level and allow you to make an informed decision if that's working as intended or not. With your current position, you just leave that to the improvisational ability of the ST. And you literally do not know and apparently do not really care if your specialized Chaos boon is superior to &quot;a good whack with a legendary hammer&quot; at legend six.<br /> <br /> All you're doing at this point is rearranging the bones in the hope that the skeleton of Scion will start walking. But almost everything that needs to be done for that to happen is something you give the ST zero assisstance for.<br /> <br /> Your response to this so far boils down to &quot;we got good feedback&quot;, &quot;ultimately, it's all in the hands of the ST anyway&quot; and &quot;maybe something about knacks will change, too&quot;. Which is nice for you, but doesn't advance this discussion in a meaningful way. And since most relevant comparison points are still WIPs, literally every possible argument I can make can be deflected with &quot;It'll be balanced when we're done&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sigh.<br /> <br /> I think I'll forego any argument about design principles and restrain myself to pointing out glitches at this point. The gist of everything else I have to say is stated above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your argument about Chaos vs. Epic Strength was discussed long before we ever put the purview up and we decided that they both fit in the world. It's nice to allow non-Strength characters the ability to breakdown the world around them. Not everyone wants ALL the epics. \u200bAnd if you dislike Breakdown and Sabot; take them out, honestly.<br /> <br /> I don't think you understand that Scion 2.0 is a hobby for us; that we've got full-time jobs and schooling. We're not game designers, and we're definitely not being paid to push this out on a schedule. I feel it would be a little easier to approach you in your posts if you did not treat us like your personal game-designers and badger us about not doing things the way you want them to be. You might not be intending to do so, but it really comes off as such.<br /> <br /> As for Storytellers and Improvisational Abilities; we <i>could </i>sit down and write out a GM manual for ST's for Scion, but it would be hours and hours of worktime we don't have already. With jobs and college, our revisions have already slowed down and it reads like you're demanding that we get straight to that instead. I'll stress the point again; we're not game designers with Scion 2.0 as our cash-cow. We're three (count 'em, three) folks who love the game a ton and have taken time to rework the rules so they fit in the style of gaming that we and the 20+ people scattered among our own groups (and other, RL groups that took Iry's ruleset for themselves). We don't argue design philosophy because ultimately, it is up to the ST what goes on in their own game; not us.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, it would be very lovely to have a GM Manuel/Bestiary but ... realistically, it's not going to happen. We have lives and food needs to be on tables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 06-14-2014, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:13:29-07:00","id":169377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Information Gathering:<br /> <br /> <b>I do not need to be told obvious facts about all of roleplaying</b>. Please stop doing that. It is deeply frustrating to read and made me ignore this thread on purpose for a while. If you do feel I really need to be told that RPGs require trust in the storyteller, you should not have a discussion with me.<br /> <br /> Of course it is trivially true that you will always need to trust the ST with the information he gives you, and of course a jackass genie can twist any statement on it's back and make any information given misleading. But as with all trivially true statements, it also fails to matter in the argument it is presented in.<br /> <br /> My point is that this power, in the way you have presented it, does not discourage this kind of behaviour. Despite your claims that this problem holds true for all information presented by the ST ever, your adaption of Mystery has some basic jackassery protection clauses built into it, while Chaos Theory does not. So either Chaos Theory is deliberately designed to be a gateway for jackass behaviour, or this is a design oversight. Take your pick or leave it, I'll not bother further with it at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very sorry that we have frustrated you Nachtigallerator, I don't believe that anyone intended to upset you at all, and I am quite sorry that you have taken offence to our explanation. As I said, we will be adding a warning label to Chaos Theory, but the wording of it has to be tinkered with in order to have the intention of the Boon kept true after this warning being given. <br /> <br /> I really am sorry you have taken offence to our explanations, I feel like there must have been a misunderstanding at some level since our intent was in no way to offend you, but just to explain our reasoning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Principles (everything else)<br /> <br /> You are still arguing beside the point. My argument is that a higher power level for boons than you have is warranted because they are often a lot more specific than epic attributes and knacks while the cost is the same. Since the pragmatic power of a tool depends on versatility and strength, boons backed up by purviews are still weaker than knacks backed up by epics.<br /> <br /> Safe for a few outliers, hero-level boons are negligible in Scion RAW. You made them cheaper, but you also got rid of all outliers, so they're still negligible if you don't want them for flavor. I don't see how GBN was any different. One good thing I have seen is putting the function of &quot;Come Hither&quot; into a Water Boon. That one is *good* because it's much more broadly applicable than you allow most other boons to be. But don't you see how it's a problem that almost any other boon is just as strong (same resistance test) but much more narrow in application?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do entirely understand how that would be incredibly problematic. Since Knacks are able to be used more frequently than Boons, since there are normally limitations to the use of Boons, being specific powers, and since Epics are the base system for your derived values and generally going to be used more often than base Purview rolls.<br /> <br /> But, in our eyes, as we design Boons and Knacks, while they are of course balanced against one and other, they are separate things, apples and oranges, to us, at least. Knacks and Boons progress at different scales. Epics roughly lineally, while Boons grow exponentially in scale. At the very beginning, Boons are more specialized than Knacks, this is true. But, this is an intentional design on our part. Now, we have attempted to limit the colossal degree to which they are different, and we hope to make Boons ultimately more useful at all levels of play, something which we have seen in our own games, but, it is just a design philosphy, we are not demanding that you agree with us at all.<br /> <br /> You are entirely welcome to use our system, use GBN's system, use RAW, use our system and edit it, use your own system, or do whatever you would like. We don't expect that everyone would agree with us. Everyone agreeing with us is what we actually would like to avoid. It is incredibly important to us that we have people who disagree with us, for echo chambers are exceptionally dangerous.<br /> <br /> But, at the end of the day, this is intentional. We treat Knacks and Boons as quite different things, but that does not mean you have to, this is just how we are doing things ourselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing that I will stress one last time is that Scion - as well as every other thing by WW and it's successor I have read so far - is a badly designed game with even worse mechanical guidance for players and storytellers. For all the (often bad) storytelling advice, the pre-made characters and enemies are trash and too few by far for a whole Scion career. And that's with a setting that has a next-to bottomless supply of public source inspiration for monsters.<br /> <br /> Scion also has absolutely no rules for what twenty successes on an Intelligence + Medicine roll even mean. And what the hell a player would get out of taking Arete (Medicine). The underlying problem with the game is that there is no functioning framework for anything. Powers and abilities just float in a big sea of nothing and arbitrary ST decisions. Is taking Arete in academic skill X a good idea? My gut says no, but it's completely up in the air, depending on who your storyteller is. And every time I poke you to find out what your idea of the framework is, the answer is &quot;that would be up to the ST to decide&quot;. You are not designing a game that way.<br /> <br /> Can you imagine a D&amp;D campaign where the ST absolutely *has* to design the opposition, down to the hitpoints and hardness of structures by arbitrary decree or fiddling around with enemy statblocks from two or five levels lower? Or set the DC for trapfinding, tracking and discovering a secret door all by himself? D&amp;D has a website with hundreds of free monsters all over the level curve, and unless your campaign is incompatible with sixteen different kinds of dragons, you can easily find something pre-made for the supported levels.<br /> My point is not that D&amp;D is the superior game. My point is that in the design of D&amp;D, the designers at least bothered to do their goddamned job.<br /> <br /> Now some people *like* to improvise all of that and will throw out all of that guidance. But designing a game includes dealing with this kind of minutae, even if Scion ignored for the most part. Scion is an emaciated skeleton of a game. If you make it your mission to improve it, I would submit you will need to put all the missing meat on it, too.<br /> <br /> A bunch of stats for relevant objects over twelve levels wouldn't be much meat to write up, and be re-useable for many other purposes. It would also show you how well Breakdown and Epic Strength knacks perform against each other at each level and allow you to make an informed decision if that's working as intended or not. With your current position, you just leave that to the improvisational ability of the ST. And you literally do not know and apparently do not really care if your specialized Chaos boon is superior to &quot;a good whack with a legendary hammer&quot; at legend six.<br /> <br /> All you're doing at this point is rearranging the bones in the hope that the skeleton of Scion will start walking. But almost everything that needs to be done for that to happen is something you give the ST zero assisstance for.<br /> <br /> Your response to this so far boils down to &quot;we got good feedback&quot;, &quot;ultimately, it's all in the hands of the ST anyway&quot; and &quot;maybe something about knacks will change, too&quot;. Which is nice for you, but doesn't advance this discussion in a meaningful way. And since most relevant comparison points are still WIPs, literally every possible argument I can make can be deflected with &quot;It'll be balanced when we're done&quot;.<br /> <br /> Sigh.<br /> <br /> I think I'll forego any argument about design principles and restrain myself to pointing out glitches at this point. The gist of everything else I have to say is stated above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really sorry, but I'm not entirely sure how to respond to this bit. Iry can help explain the mechanical sides to things, and I am very sorry that you are withdrawing yourself from the discussion since we really want people to question us, we utterly despise the idea of an echo chamber and want people to disagree with us on things so that we have to explain ourselves.<br /> <br /> I do hope that we were not misguided by releasing our rules before they were entirely, utterly and completely finished, but since Gotham By Night was being taken down, we thought it would be best for there to be some sort of presence on the web for an overhaul of Scion so people could play it if they would want.<br /> <br /> Now, I wouldn't dream to say that ours is the best it could possibly be, or that it is perfect, for everything will have flaws, especially things not made by professionals, but this is just a little project that three friends are working on for fun. We don't have any budget, we don't make any money, we are just doing this for fun. Anyone can use our rules, or not use them as they wish. But, because of this, it is incredibly difficult for us to do all of these things. We would love to create a Book of Beasts for people to draw stats from, but we can't just snap our fingers and create one. It would be a very cool project to do one day, and I think a lot of interesting beasts and beings could be included, but currently we are trying to complete every Epic Attribute, Purview, and Pantheon Specific Purview.<br /> <br /> I do apologize that we are not up to professional standards, but we are not professional game designers, or developers. I do most of the work on the website, something which I have a lot of time to do since my classes are now over and I am pretty much house-locked as I recover from a medical procedure. Iry does the majority of the rules, since he has all of the mathematics expertise that myself and Aynie lack. Aynie comes up with the rough outline of Purviews, names things, and generally is creative which is something Iry and myself are shadows in comparison to her with.<br /> <br /> But, this is the entire design team of Scion 2.0. Three people who have many real life obligations to fulfill with more importance to Scion 2.0. It is how we relax, and try to make our games better. We do not have the time to create an equivalent of the Dungeon Master's Guide, or a Monster Manuel, for at the moment we are, as I have said, working on getting the core system finished.<br /> <br /> If you would ever like to continue poking at our works, and questioning us, you are more than welcome, and we would appreciate it. It is incredibly constructive in our mind for us to have to explain ourselves to others, even if we agree with them or not. I am sorry that we are not able to complete all of the projects you wish us to complete immediately, but, this is just how we are doing things at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T18:15:03-07:00","id":169378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Information Gathering:<br /> <br /> <b>I do not need to be told obvious facts about all of roleplaying</b>. Please stop doing that. It is deeply frustrating to read and made me ignore this thread on purpose for a while. If you do feel I really need to be told that RPGs require trust in the storyteller, you should not have a discussion with me.<br /> <br /> Of course it is trivially true that you will always need to trust the ST with the information he gives you, and of course a jackass genie can twist any statement on it's back and make any information given misleading. But as with all trivially true statements, it also fails to matter in the argument it is presented in.<br /> <br /> My point is that this power, in the way you have presented it, does not discourage this kind of behaviour. Despite your claims that this problem holds true for all information presented by the ST ever, your adaption of Mystery has some basic jackassery protection clauses built into it, while Chaos Theory does not. So either Chaos Theory is deliberately designed to be a gateway for jackass behaviour, or this is a design oversight. Take your pick or leave it, I'll not bother further with it at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your ST is the kind of person to be a jackass to you with those rules, then whatever rules you have, no matter how ironclad you make them, are going to be twisted to make them such. Rule 0 of RPing means that if you get the wrong person in the storyteller seat, then there isn't a game system that can protect you from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T00:22:06-07:00","id":169550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that this power, in the way you have presented it, does not discourage this kind of behaviour. Despite your claims that this problem holds true for all information presented by the ST ever, your adaption of Mystery has some basic jackassery protection clauses built into it, while Chaos Theory does not. So either Chaos Theory is deliberately designed to be a gateway for jackass behaviour, or this is a design oversight. Take your pick or leave it, I'll not bother further with it at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sincerely sorry if what we are saying is sounding offensive to you. It is not our desire to give you generic storyteller advice in response to your question, but your concern is directly related to the behavior of your storyteller. I may be misunderstanding you, but I am genuinely not sure why there needs to be an OOC jackass protection clause when being an OOC jackass should be discouraged at all times.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you could give us some examples? Can you provide exactly the kind of disclaimer you are looking for?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are still arguing beside the point. My argument is that a higher power level for boons than you have is warranted because they are often a lot more specific than epic attributes and knacks while the cost is the same. Since the pragmatic power of a tool depends on versatility and strength, boons backed up by purviews are still weaker than knacks backed up by epics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best course of action in this situation is for us to continue to compile feedback from other groups that are not our own. If many other groups have the same concerns after playing with those boons for a few months, then we can adjust them to be a little more powerful.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion also has absolutely no rules for what twenty successes on an Intelligence + Medicine roll even mean. And what the hell a player would get out of taking Arete (Medicine). The underlying problem with the game is that there is no functioning framework for anything. Powers and abilities just float in a big sea of nothing and arbitrary ST decisions. Is taking Arete in academic skill X a good idea? My gut says no, but it's completely up in the air, depending on who your storyteller is. And every time I poke you to find out what your idea of the framework is, the answer is &quot;that would be up to the ST to decide&quot;. You are not designing a game that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a hallmark of the World of Darkness system in general. The difficulties are established by the storyteller in an organic way that is usually based on percentiles (whether the storytellers are consciously aware of this or not).<br /> <br /> For example, you sit down and look at your group composition. In one group, your best fighters may be able to hit DV 20 about 40% of the time. You may decide that is a perfectly fine percentage, or you may decide that you prefer your players to have a higher rate of success, so you reduce DV down to 16, which gives your best fighters an estimated percentage of 60%. Now that you have a baseline, you tailor the enemies around those numbers based on how you want the enemies to perform. Maybe this next fight has one enemy that is very hard to hit, but also some little enemies that are weaker so that your second tier and third tier fighters can participate.<br /> <br /> In another group, your best fighters may be much more powerful, and require higher difficulties for you to maintain the same percentages. Or maybe you want different percentages for this group. It is not even the case that everything should even have perfect balancing. A group that completely neglects combat should have a few combat encounters that are appropriate challenges for them, but they should also be threatened once in a while with combats that are far above their head. The onus is on them to come up with a non-combat solution to those situations or they will be stomped. All the while your storyteller is judging the percentages and adjusting them as appropriate to meet the increasing power of the players.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you imagine a D&amp;D campaign where the ST absolutely *has* to design the opposition, down to the hitpoints and hardness of structures by arbitrary decree or fiddling around with enemy statblocks from two or five levels lower? Or set the DC for trapfinding, tracking and discovering a secret door all by himself?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I <i>always</i> run D&amp;D campaigns.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with pulling monsters or traps out of a book is that they are not remotely tailored for the capabilities of the party. I can understand the desire to have some nice examples so that you have a baseline to compare to, and that Scion provides a pretty shoddy list of examples in the first place, and that it would be really nice if we came up with a list of examples for our own... Maybe one day we will do such a thing. But that is going to take a considerable amount of man hours and will come after all the attributes and purviews are overhauled.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now some people *like* to improvise all of that and will throw out all of that guidance. But designing a game includes dealing with this kind of minutae, even if Scion ignored for the most part. Scion is an emaciated skeleton of a game. If you make it your mission to improve it, I would submit you will need to put all the missing meat on it, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree, but we are also curious to see if the 2nd Edition of Scion is a success or flop before we tackle really huge projects (beside the really huge projects we have already promised to do).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you literally do not know and apparently do not really care if your specialized Chaos boon is superior to &quot;a good whack with a legendary hammer&quot; at legend six.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apples and oranges. There are times when a good whack with a legendary hammer is the best solution to the problem, and times when Breakdown is the best solution to the problem.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nachtigallerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169282#post169282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'll forego any argument about design principles and restrain myself to pointing out glitches at this point. The gist of everything else I have to say is stated above.</div> </div> </div> </div>We definitely welcome any and all concerns. We are happy to discuss our own design philosophy and actively desire people to challenge our opinions. The most stable foundations are those built upon reason and consistency, not a bunch of people who agree with us just because we are who we are.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, we cannot agree with every proposal or concern. Not only does it become an issue of different design philosophies, but the more we strengthen and improve our rules the less changes will happen over any given period of time. We will probably never reach a perfect set of rules, but we hope to create a set that works smoothly for the greatest number of people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 06-15-2014, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:17:36-07:00","id":169881,"title":"","content":"I have to say, your project is pretty awesome. I've been looking for ages for a complete overhault of the system, and while I haven't tested it yet (I don't have a game running right now), it seems really good to me. I'm gonna have to translate most of it for my players, though.<br /> <br /> I skimmed through it, so I may have later questions. However, I don't understand the second boon of Me, Direction of Me. It says that the Scion gains a bonus to two abilities depending on the Purview. But I don't understand what is the extent of the bonus. Maybe it is because english is not my native language. Same thing for Gift Of Me, I don't understand how are you supposed to calculate the number of Phantom Dots you grant to your buddies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T10:57:28-07:00","id":169923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169881#post169881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, your project is pretty awesome. I've been looking for ages for a complete overhault of the system, and while I haven't tested it yet (I don't have a game running right now), it seems really good to me. I'm gonna have to translate most of it for my players, though.<br /> <br /> I skimmed through it, so I may have later questions. However, I don't understand the second boon of Me, Direction of Me. It says that the Scion gains a bonus to two abilities depending on the Purview. But I don't understand what is the extent of the bonus. Maybe it is because english is not my native language. Same thing for Gift Of Me, I don't understand how are you supposed to calculate the number of Phantom Dots you grant to your buddies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may not have been as clear as I could have been when I was transcribing the Boons and putting them into my own words, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> By saying, &quot;The Scion receives a bonus of their Me Rank,&quot; I mean that the Scion gains a number of bonus dice towards the two related Abilities equal to their total number of Me Boons connected to that Purview. So, while someone may have Me (Moon) at Rank 6, and Me (War) at Rank 2, they will only gain the effects of Direction of Me (War) as a +2, compaired to their Direction of Me (Moon) which will be at +6.<br /> <br /> Does that make more sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T11:46:15-07:00","id":169959,"title":"","content":"Oh, okay, so it's the same bonus for the Purview and the Ability. All right then, makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T12:25:50-07:00","id":169993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=169959#post169959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, okay, so it's the same bonus for the Purview and the Ability. All right then, makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, the bonus given to the two Abilities is equal to the number of Dots of Me purchased for that specific Purview.<br /> <br /> I am very glad you like what we have done, if you, or any of your players get any questions or concerns, be sure to poke us here or through email. We are happy to answer any questions you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T13:05:54-07:00","id":170047,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Happy Father\u2019s Day!</span></span></span><br /> </div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/birthrights/relics\" target=\"_blank\">Relic Page</a></span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><span style=\"font-size:48px\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons\" target=\"_blank\">Pantheon Page</a></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Firstly, the </span></span></span><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/birthrights/relics\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>Relic page</u></span></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> has been updated with four potential Relics per Pantheon, and the page with all of our example Relics are not located on the sub-page of the primary Relic page.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We also have our Divine Pronunciation pages up, thanks to Anne Ruthven giving us permission to repost her wonderful guide from the JSR website. We split them into two pages just to cut down on loading time, but it can be a bit of a slow load regardless - awesome things take a second or two!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">But, now on to what I assume people are far more interested in, a quick review of our plans in regards to the Epic Attributes and Purviews. Now, all of these are prone to change, though since they are the basic conceptual ideas of what we want the Purviews to do, I doubt they will change that much at all.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Epic Attributes</span></span></span><br /> <hr /><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u200bEpic Charisma -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> We hope to include a greater spread of powers in Epic Charisma so that all of the major forms of Charisma can be represented in powers. Currently, the charming Scions have the majority of the powers in Charisma, with some given to those who lead. We hope to expand this so the bold leaders, the kind charmers, and those who inspire great emotions, such as love, but also fear, hate, and so on are represented.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Epic Manipulation -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> We are fairly happy with Epic Manipulation at the moment, but of course we will have to rebalance things to better fit inside Scion 2.0. One of the areas that Epic Manipulation is lacking powers in successfully pulling off the social half of a disguise, and since it is such a common theme in mythology, it is likely to gain a knack or two.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Epic Appearance -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Epic Appearance sits in a continually weird spot. It has a lot of cross over with Epic Manipulation, and Epic Charisma mechanically, but it has some very cool Knacks. These Knacks will be rebalanced, and, of course, some new ones will likely be added. Additionally,we have been toying with the idea of Epic Appearance possibly augmenting your Charisma or Manipulation somehow, though that is very much a vague idea that may not come to pass.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Epic Perception -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The three mental Attributes are fairly strong at the moment, but Epic Perception needs an injection of knacks that allow you to sense even more things, such as ghosts (hopefully in a way that does not step on the toes of Death Senses), legend use (hopefully in a way that does not step on the toes of Unlidded Eye), and peering across dimensions (to see terra-incognita, or gaze down from your overworld at the mortal realm).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Epic Intelligence -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Epic Intelligence has some amazing powers, and though we are going to have to rebalance everything, there likely won't be much change. It would be nice to find a way to make Axiom more appealing though, since in all my five years of playing Scion, I have never seen it used once.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Epic Wits -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Epic Wits is filled with dice adders, which is something we are going to have to address, though the basic premise of these Knacks is going to be kept. There is not much needed to be added to Epic Wits in our mind, though we are sure we will come up with some nice little things to slip in there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Purviews</span></span></span><br /> <hr /><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Darkness -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Darkness is going to encompass the powers of night, fear, along with common darkness in all of its forms. We hope to have Darkness represent the idea of what exists outside the campfire's light, what exists outside the walls of the cities. The dark places of the world where humanity has not reached yet.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Death -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Death is fairly good already, though we are going to rejig the order of a lot of the Boons. The ghost based Boons are going to be lower tier, for high tier Demigods don't really interact with ghosts on an incredibly meaningful level from what we have seen, and it is more common at Hero. We hope to make the ghost based powers, additionally, capable of being used more often. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Earth -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Earth is fairly good at representing the powers of Earth Deities, though we want to include some powers of wealth under Earth, and giving it a power for becoming the land itself is also likely going to be present, for it is a very common theme for Earth Deities.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fertility -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> RAW Fertility is going to take serious investigation, because it is probably the purview that is most overwhelmingly worshipped by mortals in our estimation. And yet, most of the mythologically resonant ideas contribute more towards agriculture than something that can be used by a heroic scion in the heat of a moment. Additionally, there will probably be a power somewhere for the constant theme connecting Fertility and sexuality.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Fire -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> RAW Fire is all about the all consuming fire, and, while this is a mythological theme, it ignores those who inspire through fire, those who are the hearth and home, and also giving representation of great passion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Frost -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Frost has some problems with overall theme asides from 'snow, ice, and cold stuff' RAW. So, we hope to, while keeping much of the same powers, bring themes of destroying winter, sapping emotions, and such things. We hope to have Frost run counter to Fertility, destroying life, causing famines, and representing the fear that winter brought for many ancient peoples.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Guardian -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> RAW Guardian acomplishes its goals, but, we want to include more powers for beings who are not directly martial protectors. Those who watch over children, those who guard specific buildings, and the such. While there will be powers for the martial defenders, such as Thor, we hope that there will also be powers for people such as Hera who protect children and mothers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Health -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Powers of plague, and powers of healing are represented in Health already. But, we wish to further the powers of bringing life if we can find places for them. Giving people children, striking people impotent or barren, and such powers we hope to include.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Illusion -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Powers of tricks, and lies are already represented with Illusion, but we want to include powers for the dream Deities, though few they are.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Justice -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Justice is a deceptively powerful Purview, and we would like to continue that theme. While it should only be able to bring justice to those who have broken a law, we also want to include powers of rulership, for those who are the one true king, and such.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moon -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Madness, and serenity are the main themes of Moon we want to bring, along with some minor trends of secrets. Moon, being one of the three Celestial Purviews with so many different mythological themes across various cultures, is rather difficult to write for, and it will likely be one of the last we complete.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Psychopomp -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> RAW Psychopomp has a few glaring issues. Firstly, they are incapable of instant travel until Legend 10, and additionally, they just become travel batteries for their Band from what we have seen. We want to fix this issue by giving earlier quickened transportation, creating means of travel, hampering others travel, and such things are how we wish to address issue number one. The second issue has several things in the playtest stage, so we are eager to see how they turn out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sky -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> The vault of the Sky, breath, and so on are what we want to accomplish with Sky. GBN's current revision is very good, and we are probably going to draw a lot of inspiration from them. But, it will not be a word for word copy of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stars -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Oh Stars, you are so incredibly difficult. Stars is very likely going to take quite a long time to write, since there is a surprising lack of consistency through the ancient world about Stars. But, being eternal and unchanging is fairly common, in addition to navigation themes. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sun -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> RAW Sun descends into the modern idea of the Sun very quickly, which is something we want to avoid very much. Dawn bringing hope, light fighting the darkness, and blistering, hateful heat are what we want to evoke with our Sun, and hopefully we will.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thunder -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Storms, thunder, and lightning are the themes of Thunder. GBN very recently created the Purview, and we hope to continue the theme of barely controlled power that the Purview currently has. But, there, of course, are going to be some minor changes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">War -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> We want to streamline war along two primary themes. The general, who engages in tactics and logistics. And the champion, who inspires his allies through duels and single combat. While cultural powers like Raistrad are being moved to Guides and Relics, War is picking up a few powers to cause friendly fire accidents and the ability to fill everyone with fury and bloodlust.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{