further the powers of bringing life if we can find places for them. Giving people children, striking people impotent or barren, and such powers we hope to include.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sun -</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> RAW Sun descends into the modern idea of the Sun very quickly, which is something we want to avoid very much. Dawn bringing hope, light fighting the darkness, and blistering, hateful heat are what we want to evoke with our Sun, and hopefully we will.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely awesome. Those are my favourites purviews, along with Chaos and Animal, and I can't wait to see what you're gonna do with it! Especially with Fertility, my current Scion of Dionysus is going to love it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:55:46-07:00","id":170171,"title":"","content":"I like your work, especially the retainer part. Such an easy and amazing way to handle this birthright <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I noticed in your combat section that you are using dexterity in a lot of trait or derived trait, more than in RAW I think. Is it intended that dexterity is the easyest way to make a combat oriented character ? As I see it, it's dexterity VS strength + stamina. Is dexterity becoming a bit too powerful ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T16:52:41-07:00","id":170202,"title":"","content":"Actually, speaking as a player in Scion 2.0 games, I can say that Dexterity is less of a necessity to combat. You can choose, for the most part, to use Dexterity OR Strength (or Perception for ranged attacks) to make an attack, and either Dodge DV OR Soak DV to take the hit. This is unlike RAW Scion, where you need Dexterity to hit and Strength to do damage, and to take a hit, you subtract Dodge DV first before you soak it. Not to mention that Dexterity-based attacks can't do Aggravated Damage, as far as I remember. Basically, no, Dex isn't as necessary-to-combat as it was before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T17:08:01-07:00","id":170212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=170127#post170127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely awesome. Those are my favourites purviews, along with Chaos and Animal, and I can't wait to see what you're gonna do with it! Especially with Fertility, my current Scion of Dionysus is going to love it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I am very glad you are excited. Fertility is an incredibly difficult Purview because it was very much <i>the</i> most important thing for Agrarian cultures, which most of the cultures we draw Pantheons from are, but since Scion is very action adventure oriented, Fertility is an odd duckling. We are very much going to spend a lot of time to get across its colossal importance and keeping it in theme for the ancient world, while also having, hopefully, an equal number of flashy action adventure powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=170127#post170127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like your work, especially the retainer part. Such an easy and amazing way to handle this birthright <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I noticed in your combat section that you are using dexterity in a lot of trait or derived trait, more than in RAW I think. Is it intended that dexterity is the easyest way to make a combat oriented character ? As I see it, it's dexterity VS strength + stamina. Is dexterity becoming a bit too powerful ?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW Scion had a colossal dependence on Epic Dexterity for fighters, and it is something we have tried to stray away from. While it is technically easiest to just take Epic Dexterity, and use Dodge DV and use it for attacking, you don't really come out totally on top. Epic Dexterity is one of the less powerful both defensive, and offensive powers, but its strength comes from the fact that it is both, and gives you a lot of other features.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Epic Strength, and Epic Stamina, both being far more 'focused' than Epic Dexterity, can bring more to the table in their focused areas. Epic Strength brings a number of ways to deal with armor, and brings Aggravated Damage to the table, something which Epic Dexterity does not possess. Epic Stamina brings extra health boxes (deceptively helpful) and many different ways to, in broad terms, not to die.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if someone wishes to, they can use Epic Appearance as a physical defensive value through Game Face or Do Not Want. We have not totally revised the Epic Socials yet, so they may not be all fixed up properly.<br /> <br /> So, while someone can just flat out use Epic Dexterity, it is very much not required. It also must be remembered that you can't use a Knack from Epic Strength when making a Dexterity based attack, and vice versa. So, someone using Epic Dexterity as their primary mode of attack can't use Epic Strength's Aggravated attacks unless they are willing to use their lower Epic Strength to attack with. Additionally, someone with Epic Dexterity may not used the enhanced range powers of Epic Perception when attacking with their Epic Dexterity. So, while Epic Dexterity can be used for both attack and defense, it is defiantly not the king of either.<br /> <br /> I hope I explained that well. I am not the mechanics person, so if I have done a poor job, you will see Iry here in a while putting some corrections in. But, I am very glad you are enjoying out system. Always feel free to ask any questions, or make any comments!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 06-15-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T17:43:32-07:00","id":170222,"title":"","content":"Ok I'm convinced but you seem to say that aggravated damages are a big deal but the only reference I found is that it halves your soak DV. Is there another difference between aggravated and lethal damage ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T17:57:27-07:00","id":170226,"title":"","content":"Basically, damage progresses from bashing to lethal to aggravated, meaning that aggravated damage kills you much quicker than lethal. Iry mathed out the specifics a few pages back","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T18:12:29-07:00","id":170233,"title":"","content":"I would have thought &quot;lethal&quot; was, well...lethal.<br /> As opposed to &quot;aggravated&quot; which would be not so..lethal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T18:49:43-07:00","id":170249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=170222#post170222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok I'm convinced but you seem to say that aggravated damages are a big deal but the only reference I found is that it halves your soak DV. Is there another difference between aggravated and lethal damage ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated damage is horrific to take for two reasons. Firstly, if you are someone who relies on Soak DV, you are only able to use half of it to resist people. (Dodge DV can be similarly slashed through grappling.) But, secondly, as Griffinguy said, it is easier to just outright kill someone with Aggravated damage for the fact that the moment someone is filled with Aggravated, they perish. With Lethal damage, one has to still fill their health boxes with Aggravated Damage by having the Lethal Damage wrap over into Aggravated if you want to outright kill someone.<br /> <br /> Additionally, some Knacks, such as Self-Healing and Damage Conversion have to use their higher cost counterparts, Regeneration and Divine Damage Conversion to try to resist Aggravated damage, which some beings may not have.<br /> <br /> So, overall, if you want to just flat out slaughter someone, use Aggravated damage. Be it from Fire (Dragon's Breath), or Epic Strength, or some of the other Purviews we have not yet revised (I am sure Thunder will have some, and likely War), if you want to destroy someone entirely, Aggravated is the way to go.<br /> <br /> But, hey. If you are an Epic Perception Marksman, you can shoot a target pretty much no matter where they are through combining Clairvoyance and Divine Marksman, and it is far harder to hide from them. So, don't think that only Epic Strength is viable for total offensive combatants. I would be more afraid of offending Apollo than Ares.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T18:53:49-07:00","id":170270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=170233#post170233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have thought &quot;lethal&quot; was, well...lethal.<br /> <br /> As opposed to &quot;aggravated&quot; which would be not so..lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have kept the name Aggravated Damage, and the wrapping over mechanics from RAW Scion (and I also believe they are present in World of Darkness) since many people are more familiar with those systems than ours. We would prefer that people have some sense of familiarity with our system, and have kept some terms, such as Aggravated Damage for that reason. Soak DV was contemplated to be renamed Block DV once, and Psychopomp was debated if a name change to Travel was better suited, but since people were more familiar with the older terms, we kept them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T06:00:41-07:00","id":170654,"title":"","content":"Oh ok lethal damage no longer kill you outright. Then what you said make a lot more sense to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Perhaps you could write a part on your website combat section to explain how you need to fill your health box with aggravated damage to have your character dead. I'm sure it would help a lot of reader.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T08:52:12-07:00","id":170786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astoril</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=170654#post170654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh ok lethal damage no longer kill you outright. Then what you said make a lot more sense to me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Perhaps you could write a part on your website combat section to explain how you need to fill your health box with aggravated damage to have your character dead. I'm sure it would help a lot of reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Damage&quot; section under &quot;Combat&quot; should definitely mention that. Thank you for pointing out the absence!<br /> I rewrote the section to clarify the issue, as follows:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:Droid Sans\">&quot;When you gain enough bashing or lethal damage to be incapacitated, you immediately collapse into a relatively useless lump that can take no further actions. You may still whisper dramatically or make minor gestures, but nothing that would constitute an action. Once all your health boxes are full of bashing damage, any further bashing damage inflicts lethal damage instead. Once all your health boxes are full of lethal damage, any further lethal damage inflicts aggravated damage instead. When</span></span><span style=\"color:#073763\"><span style=\"font-family:Droid Sans\"> all your health boxes are full of aggravated damage, you are officially dead.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T20:11:08-07:00","id":180299,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hey everyone,</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We just need to let everyone know that Gotham By Night has asked that we take down their </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Artistry</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Magic</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prophecy</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sky</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thunder</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Purviews, and their </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dvoeverie</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Heku</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Me</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">, and </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ori</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We had been given permission to use their works, but because of some legal complications, they have asked us if we mind taking those things down. We entirely understand where Gotham By Night is coming from, and are happy to comply with their wishes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Because of this, those Purviews and Pantheon Specific Purviews will be missing from our site for a little while, which is something we do apologize for. We are entirely refocusing ourselves in order to try and resolve this, pausing our work on Death, War, and additional Pantheons for the time being in order to fill in these openings.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Me is going to be finished first, because we already have a mountain of research material on that pantheon, and the result will probably look similar to the old Me. I am going to spend my time working on doing research for the Orisha and the Bogovi so we can develop Pantheon Specific Purviews for the both of them. Aynie is going to begin to work on creative designs for a new Sky and Thunder.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">We are very sorry for any inconvenience this causes anyone running any games with our rules. We hope to get things back on track as soon as we are able. As always, if anyone has any questions, or suggestions, just post them here.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T20:22:11-07:00","id":180306,"title":"","content":"It might also be a good idea to put the news up on the update part of the website, plus the previous updates you did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3247-thyself","name":"thyself","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T20:35:37-07:00","id":180311,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much Thyself for that suggestion, both have been added to our updates page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T06:37:43-07:00","id":180749,"title":"","content":"Man, that's wild. Just those specific ones? Interesting. I hope you're all able to come up with something soon, good luck! Perhaps you could put out the hero-level boons as you create them?<br /> <br /> And, yes, Thyself made an excellent suggestion! If you guys can detail updates/changes to the site in that section regularly, that'd be great. Might I also suggest a blog to address questions/etc.? I believe it's relatively simple to create a Tumblr/Blogspot and integrate it into the site. Tumblr even has that wonderful Ask Box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T09:42:49-07:00","id":180944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=180749#post180749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, that's wild. Just those specific ones? Interesting. I hope you're all able to come up with something soon, good luck! Perhaps you could put out the hero-level boons as you create them?</div> </div> </div> </div>We will likely do that for the standard Purviews. Pantheon Specific Purviews tend to be written in one fell swoop after all the research has been concluded, so if we posted the lower level ones, it would only be for a day or two before the rest came up. Also, with Pantheon Specific Purviews, there is a lot of shuffling stuff around to try to include or remove specific ideas. I suspect this is likely because we are confined for space with the Pantheon Specific Purviews.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=180749#post180749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, yes, Thyself made an excellent suggestion! If you guys can detail updates/changes to the site in that section regularly, that'd be great. Might I also suggest a blog to address questions/etc.? I believe it's relatively simple to create a Tumblr/Blogspot and integrate it into the site. Tumblr even has that wonderful Ask Box.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we first made the site, we threw around the idea of having a blog as Gotham By Night had. But, we didn't think that we would be nearly able to be as active as them for both a smaller audience. If we get a lot of interest in the idea, we, back at the genesis of this idea, decided that we would make one. But, unless we get a great cry from the public, we are going to try to keep everything here, as to try to rekindle this community.<br /> <br /> But, as I said, if we have a lot of people clamoring for us to make one, we likely will. So, just post here, send a PM, or an email about it if you would and we will get back to you guys as soon as we feel like it is a desired thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T06:16:12-07:00","id":185465,"title":"","content":"Do you guys plan on creating any Character Sheets for Scion 2.0, or do you already have some made?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-01T08:28:16-07:00","id":185539,"title":"","content":"We have a template on Google docs that we cold possibly share / add to the site itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T18:01:28-07:00","id":189016,"title":"","content":"Wait! John's Scion resources shut down!?<br /> <br /> *Checks*<br /> <br /> Son of a...<br /> <br /> Well, guess that shows how far I am behind the times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T21:51:37-07:00","id":204657,"title":"","content":"I am sorry if this bothers you, but how goes the updates to project 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3247-thyself","name":"thyself","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T23:45:47-07:00","id":204705,"title":"","content":"Oh, it is not bothersome in the slightest, don't worry about that.<br /> <br /> Things are going slightly slowly at the moment since we are working on multiple fronts, but things are coming along. The three Purviews we are focused on at the moment are Storms (Thunder, Lightning, and Rain), Me (The PsP of the Anunna), and the PsP of the Bogovi which we have not worked on a name yet for.<br /> <br /> For Me, we are going for the same general 'feel' of Purview as before. It will be a Purview improving other Purviews, making the wielder of the Me of Flames greater at wielding the Fire Purview, and so on.<br /> <br /> For Storms, we are attempting to create a balance between the offensive thunder and lightning, with environmental effects, and rain powers. Rain was so, so incredibly important in the ancient world, and thus mythologically, but it is difficult to create powers using rain that players would be interested in. <br /> <br /> For the as of yet unnamed PsP of the Bogovi, the research I have done has lead me to decide that a PsP based around a personal cult would work best. Having a priest, a horse, and many other things that the Bogovi are very much not supposed to have, but have anyways. For, despite how much the Bogovi love their laws, not a single one of them actually follows them when it is inconvenient for them. So, everyone has a horse they ride in secret and have it kept by specific people in a specific location when they are not riding it in private, away from the gaze of their 'Over-King'.<br /> <br /> One of our trio has had some computer issues, which has slowed things. But, we are still working away to try to recover and get back to as we were before.<br /> <br /> Just as a side, when we get around to it, the Tuatha's Antagonist Titan is going to be the Titan of War. But, that won't be for a long time yet.<br /> <br /> As always, if anyone's got any questions or comments, feel free! Always happy to answer questions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T20:30:20-07:00","id":209777,"title":"","content":"I don't know if anyone has said any thing about this, I;ve searched through the posts but cant find anything. I have always enjoyed playing my Scion character as a type of Palladin. One whose able to protect and heal. I enjoy him as a Tuatha, normally a scion of Lugh. However I noticed Lugh does not have the Guardian or Health Purviews in this edition. I noticed that none of the Tuatha have these traits. However, almost all of them have the Purview of War. This seems to unbalance the Pantheon. Is there a reason for this or is it something that can change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Nothing is foolproof for a sufficiently talented fool.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","name":"bigwhitt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T22:53:21-07:00","id":209840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=209777#post209777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if anyone has said any thing about this, I;ve searched through the posts but cant find anything. I have always enjoyed playing my Scion character as a type of Palladin. One whose able to protect and heal. I enjoy him as a Tuatha, normally a scion of Lugh. However I noticed Lugh does not have the Guardian or Health Purviews in this edition. I noticed that none of the Tuatha have these traits. However, almost all of them have the Purview of War. This seems to unbalance the Pantheon. Is there a reason for this or is it something that can change?</div> </div> </div> </div>The changes to the Associated Powers and Associated Abilities of the Pantheons were done originally by John and Anne at Gotham by Night, but they have all been made to attempt to bring the profiles of these Gods better in line with their Mythological counterparts than RAW managed to do. So, there were some rather drastic changes to the Tuatha. But, I adore Irish Mythology and can explain every change you would like for them.<br /> <br /> So, the reason Lugh no longer has Guardian is there is not a single myth that I know of where Lugh is in the role of a guardian, or a protector. Lugh is not a warden on the walls, or a God who dispensed blessings to safeguard others. Additionally, I don't know of any cult worship of Lugh that identifies him as such a Deity. I have no idea why he was given it in RAW, but Lugh is not, and has never been (Historically) a Guardian Deity.<br /> <br /> Now, the reason they gave Lugh Health is that he once healed CuChulain when he was fighting at the ford. Also, sometimes he introduces himself as a physician or doctor when requesting entrance to Tara. But, neither of these are sufficient reasons to give Lugh Health. A single account of him preforming it, and him boasting about his ability to be a doctor don't particularly compare with Apollo slaughtering the Greek Army with plagues, or Mokosh bringing humanity into existence. Additionally, once again, we don't see any cult presence for Lugh as a healer or plague bringer.<br /> <br /> Now, the reason for the Tuatha having many members who have War is because they are composed of many War Deities. It's just how it has turned out for them. They are an incredibly war centered Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Lugh has War for he is the Champion of the Tuatha de Danann. He is their war leader, and warrior without peer. Wielding his great blazing spear and his sling.<br /> <br /> Nuada is the greatest King that has ever ruled Ireland, and has lead the Tuatha successfully in war against the forces of their foes many times. He lead his people against the Fir Bolg when they first invaded Ireland alongside The Dagda and Ogma.<br /> <br /> Ogma has War since he was the Champion of the Tuatha before Lugh, and lead the armies of the Gods against the Fir Bolg as I said. Additionally, we have evidence of Ogma being connected to the idea of 'eloquence', and getting armies ready for battle beforehand by speaking praises and other great oral works to them.<br /> <br /> The Dagda is a colossal man, wielding his great club and draging his other 'club' behind himself as he trudges through the battlefields. He has lead the Tuatha in warfare, and is written as a great warrior. Though, very importantly for the Irish, not a Champion.<br /> <br /> And, lastly, The Morrigan herself is a Goddess of battlefield frenzy, death, and destruction. Her crows pick out the eyes of the dead, and she flies over battlefields to strike blind fury into warriors. Additionally, she has brought the Tuatha secret knowledge on how to defeat their enemies in battle before, and has almost single handedly won battles for them.<br /> <br /> I do not understand though how this &quot;Unbalances&quot; the Pantheon though, would you mind terribly explaining what you mean so I can help work things out?<br /> <br /> But, in sum. The changes that we use to the God profiles are to keep them more in line with their mythological and and historical realities. To best represent the Gods of cultures long past through their own eyes as best we can. RAW did not do a spectacular job with this sort of thing in our mind, as can be seen through the large changes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I do want to add that the Tuatha represented are only the Major Gods (Legend 12 Gods). The Tuatha have three very skilled Health Gods (Dian Cecht, Airmed, Miach) though their powers, legends, and worship don't indicate that they would be on equal footing as the Tuatha we have listed. I am not sure for Guardian though, I know of no figures who serve as a protector in Irish mythology. But, all the more room for a new Scion to fill a void!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-27-2014, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T06:14:03-07:00","id":210059,"title":"","content":"Hello, thank you for the explanation. The reason that I thought it might unbalance them was because in the original game it seemed that each pantheon represented the entire set of purviews. If you wanted to create a scion who definitely had the Health purview there was at least one God who had it, allowing you to choose any pantheon you wanted because it matched your character concept. With Tuatha not having a god with Guardian or Health in the major gods that are listed I though it might unbalance the overall purview percentages represented in each pantheon.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wanted to specify that I wasn't being specific on the Health purview, I just used it as an example. If you have a character in mind I think you should find every purview represented in each pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Nothing is foolproof for a sufficiently talented fool.&quot;","edited":{"userid":981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","user":"bigwhitt","date":". 07-27-2014, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","name":"bigwhitt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T07:20:25-07:00","id":210161,"title":"","content":"Also, I happened to notice that the experience rules do not take into account a God's Associated powers or associated abilities for a reduction in experience cost Am I missing it somewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Nothing is foolproof for a sufficiently talented fool.&quot;","edited":{"userid":981,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","user":"bigwhitt","date":". 07-27-2014, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","name":"bigwhitt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T08:27:42-07:00","id":210217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=209840#post209840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The changes to the Associated Powers and Associated Abilities of the Pantheons were done originally by John and Anne at Gotham by Night, but they have all been made to attempt to bring the profiles of these Gods better in line with their Mythological counterparts than RAW managed to do. So, there were some rather drastic changes to the Tuatha. But, I adore Irish Mythology and can explain every change you would like for them.<br /> <br /> So, the reason Lugh no longer has Guardian is there is not a single myth that I know of where Lugh is in the role of a guardian, or a protector. Lugh is not a warden on the walls, or a God who dispensed blessings to safeguard others. Additionally, I don't know of any cult worship of Lugh that identifies him as such a Deity. I have no idea why he was given it in RAW, but Lugh is not, and has never been (Historically) a Guardian Deity.<br /> <br /> Now, the reason they gave Lugh Health is that he once healed CuChulain when he was fighting at the ford. Also, sometimes he introduces himself as a physician or doctor when requesting entrance to Tara. But, neither of these are sufficient reasons to give Lugh Health. A single account of him preforming it, and him boasting about his ability to be a doctor don't particularly compare with Apollo slaughtering the Greek Army with plagues, or Mokosh bringing humanity into existence. Additionally, once again, we don't see any cult presence for Lugh as a healer or plague bringer.<br /> <br /> Now, the reason for the Tuatha having many members who have War is because they are composed of many War Deities. It's just how it has turned out for them. They are an incredibly war centered Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Lugh has War for he is the Champion of the Tuatha de Danann. He is their war leader, and warrior without peer. Wielding his great blazing spear and his sling.<br /> <br /> Nuada is the greatest King that has ever ruled Ireland, and has lead the Tuatha successfully in war against the forces of their foes many times. He lead his people against the Fir Bolg when they first invaded Ireland alongside The Dagda and Ogma.<br /> <br /> Ogma has War since he was the Champion of the Tuatha before Lugh, and lead the armies of the Gods against the Fir Bolg as I said. Additionally, we have evidence of Ogma being connected to the idea of 'eloquence', and getting armies ready for battle beforehand by speaking praises and other great oral works to them.<br /> <br /> The Dagda is a colossal man, wielding his great club and draging his other 'club' behind himself as he trudges through the battlefields. He has lead the Tuatha in warfare, and is written as a great warrior. Though, very importantly for the Irish, not a Champion.<br /> <br /> And, lastly, The Morrigan herself is a Goddess of battlefield frenzy, death, and destruction. Her crows pick out the eyes of the dead, and she flies over battlefields to strike blind fury into warriors. Additionally, she has brought the Tuatha secret knowledge on how to defeat their enemies in battle before, and has almost single handedly won battles for them.<br /> <br /> I do not understand though how this &quot;Unbalances&quot; the Pantheon though, would you mind terribly explaining what you mean so I can help work things out?<br /> <br /> But, in sum. The changes that we use to the God profiles are to keep them more in line with their mythological and and historical realities. To best represent the Gods of cultures long past through their own eyes as best we can. RAW did not do a spectacular job with this sort of thing in our mind, as can be seen through the large changes.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, I do want to add that the Tuatha represented are only the Major Gods (Legend 12 Gods). The Tuatha have three very skilled Health Gods (Dian Cecht, Airmed, Miach) though their powers, legends, and worship don't indicate that they would be on equal footing as the Tuatha we have listed. I am not sure for Guardian though, I know of no figures who serve as a protector in Irish mythology. But, all the more room for a new Scion to fill a void!</div> </div> </div> </div>Using John &amp; Anne logic, none of those gods should have the War Purview as all of them were defeated by someone else. Meaning they don't have the War Avatar, since that would render them undefeatable or produce a stalemate in head to head fighting.<br /> <br /> I'll buy the Morrigan though. No one ever defeated her. <br /> <br /> It also looks like a lot of these viewpoints are pretty much based on just the Book of Invasions and the Tain. There are a lot of other stories out there. Admittedly, much harder to get at, where things other than war are dealt with (lots of marking the edges of fields, throwing things, political maneuvering, etc.). It's easy to think a pantheon is war oriented if the sources used are two battles. It would be like setting up the Greek gods just using the Iliad. <br /> <br /> Lugh probably should have War. But then, as Samildanach, you could give him ANYTHING, but he did fight and win a war quite handily. Since War is about tactics and strategy and not about combat prowess in most cases, then it's not a lock. <br /> <br /> Nuada, I'll buy 100%. He's a War god. One that got beat and mutilated, but still, he does the necessary deeds.<br /> <br /> Ogma. He gets to be Champion and he fights well, but a &quot;leader&quot; type? No. He's got hella Strength. But not War. (Champion means &quot;the guy who goes out and takes the 1 on 1 challenge. Not the general).<br /> <br /> The Dagda. No. He was King at some point, and he can fight damn good, but there is nothing to indicate War. More plowing and brewing and laughing. <br /> <br /> That would leave two with War as Associated..... Nuada and the Morrigan. Possibly 3, with Lugh.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ogma","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:02:12-07:00","id":210347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210059#post210059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, thank you for the explanation. The reason that I thought it might unbalance them was because in the original game it seemed that each pantheon represented the entire set of purviews. If you wanted to create a scion who definitely had the Health purview there was at least one God who had it, allowing you to choose any pantheon you wanted because it matched your character concept. With Tuatha not having a god with Guardian or Health in the major gods that are listed I though it might unbalance the overall purview percentages represented in each pantheon.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wanted to specify that I wasn't being specific on the Health purview, I just used it as an example. If you have a character in mind I think you should find every purview represented in each pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean. The the thing is, some cultures just have no concept of some Purviews. Many have no Gods with Frost, Illusion, or other things. It is incredibly normal really, since the Pantheons are representations for their culture's perspective on reality. So, therefore, some things just don't have Major Gods or any Gods at all connected with them. For example, the Norse have no one with Animal since Animals are very fundamentally a force which runs against the Aesir. (Odin's connections don't go as far to make him an Animal God, but are there likely to show how powerful he is, or at a further attempt to cast Odin in a 'other' role as the Cult of Thor grew in power).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210059#post210059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I happened to notice that the experience rules do not take into account a God's Associated powers or associated abilities for a reduction in experience cost Am I missing it somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I think I see the root of this problem. Gods don't give Experience discounts to their children, since it unbalances things for the exact reasons you stated above that you were worried about. Instead, if your Parent has a Ability Associated, you get a free Speciality, and if you have a Purview or Epic they have Associated, once per Game you may use a Knack or Boon from one of them for no cost at all. (Deceptively powerful) You can find it on our site <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/character-creation#TOC-The-Steps-to-Crafting-a-Scion\" target=\"_blank\">here </a>under &quot;Associated Abilities&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:33:59-07:00","id":210389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210217#post210217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using John &amp; Anne logic, none of those gods should have the War Purview as all of them were defeated by someone else. Meaning they don't have the War Avatar, since that would render them undefeatable or produce a stalemate in head to head fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, all of the Associateds we have up for the site, save for a few we fiddled with in the Theoi and one power on The Morrigan, are their own Associated powers. But, if being defeated by another means you don't get War, Ares does not get it for the jar incident and Diomedes wrecking him, Thor does not get it for he lost a wrestling match with Old Age, Horus loses it since Set beat him like a drum in their own physical combat, and so on. We, ourselves, don't use that to determine who gets War, and neither did John and Anne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210217#post210217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also looks like a lot of these viewpoints are pretty much based on just the Book of Invasions and the Tain. There are a lot of other stories out there. Admittedly, much harder to get at, where things other than war are dealt with (lots of marking the edges of fields, throwing things, political maneuvering, etc.). It's easy to think a pantheon is war oriented if the sources used are two battles. It would be like setting up the Greek gods just using the Iliad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I have read all of the ones we have primary documents for as far as I know, but I know that no one is infallable. Could you please link or write the names of some of these other sources? There are many stories from the Irish, and I was under the impression that over the last five years I had managed to consume all of the 'large' ones. Not just pertaining to the Book of Invasions and the Tain. I realize there are many of these that have nothing at all to do with War, such as Aengus searching for the woman, literally, of his dreams. Niamh of the Golden Hair yoinking Oisin off Ireland to Tir na nOg, Midir being a horrible king and entirely screwing up the entire Children of Lir situation. I have read more than just those, but I don't think it would really help for me to sit here listing every single one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210217#post210217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lugh probably should have War. But then, as Samildanach, you could give him ANYTHING, but he did fight and win a war quite handily. Since War is about tactics and strategy and not about combat prowess in most cases, then it's not a lock.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our version of War includes those who are Champions or other similar figures. Sun Wukong, Lugh, Thor, and so on. RAW War and even GBN's War had little to represent the way these figures filled their role as a War God, so we have included Boons to help them to function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210217#post210217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ogma. He gets to be Champion and he fights well, but a &quot;leader&quot; type? No. He's got hella Strength. But not War. (Champion means &quot;the guy who goes out and takes the 1 on 1 challenge. Not the general).</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said above, not all War Gods are leaders. This is true of John and Anne's associateds, and our own rendition of the War Purview. Additionally, though I can't find the quote in my handy Oxford Dictionary of Irish Mythology at the moment, is that Ogma's epithet &quot;Cermait&quot; or &quot;Of the Honeyed-Mouth&quot; has some possible connection with a tradition of speaking praise to your army ahead of time to try to get everyone sorted. Since he was Champion before Lugh, lead the armies of the Tuatha, and because of this, Ogma has War at the moment. Once again, this is John and Anne's associated, as all of the Tuatha are (Save for one of The Morrigans' Socials which we changed).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210217#post210217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dagda. No. He was King at some point, and he can fight damn good, but there is nothing to indicate War. More plowing and brewing and laughing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am least sure of The Dagda's War Associations, especially because he has explicitly needed The Morrigan's help with battle plans and the such before. But, it was what John and Anne gave him, and we have not changed it yet. For The Dagda, I also want to exchange his Epic Intelligence for Mystery. He has secret knowledge from the Otherworlds, feels more like Mystery to me.<br /> <br /> So, in sum. All of our Associations except for three are directly from Gotham by Night. Secondly, we don't use the rule that if a God was defeated before they can't have War, and neither did Gotham by Night. And, lastly, we have changed War so that it is more open, both to fill the role as the General, but the Champion as well, for many Gods are War Gods, but not leaders in battle.<br /> <br /> You are entirely welcome to not use these Associateds, some of them I want to change, but am currently up to my neck in Veles sleeping with Perun's wife and stealing his salt shaker. One other one that I know I want to change for sure is Aengus' Animal, and possibly his Perception. Animal certainly doesn't fit, in my mind. Very tangential, that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T10:40:48-07:00","id":210396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210389#post210389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, in sum. All of our Associations except for three are directly from Gotham by Night. Secondly, we don't use the rule that if a God was defeated before they can't have War, and neither did Gotham by Night. And, lastly, we have changed War so that it is more open, both to fill the role as the General, but the Champion as well, for many Gods are War Gods, but not leaders in battle.<br /> <br /> You are entirely welcome to not use these Associateds, some of them I want to change, but am currently up to my neck in Veles sleeping with Perun's wife and stealing his salt shaker. One other one that I know I want to change for sure is Aengus' Animal, and possibly his Perception. Animal certainly doesn't fit, in my mind. Very tangential, that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that our idea of Gods have a THING doesn't mean Avatar or BUST, it's roughly around &quot;would they be a God of this thing at Legend 8 or 9?&quot; If yes, then they've got it. While the three of us respect Anne's ability to research like there's no tomorrow, sooner or later, we'll probably have Associates that have nothing to do with GSR logic.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, in accordance to our new adjustment of War, the Tuatha can have all of those gods associated with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:18:17-07:00","id":210524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210059#post210059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, thank you for the explanation. The reason that I thought it might unbalance them was because in the original game it seemed that each pantheon represented the entire set of purviews. If you wanted to create a scion who definitely had the Health purview there was at least one God who had it, allowing you to choose any pantheon you wanted because it matched your character concept. With Tuatha not having a god with Guardian or Health in the major gods that are listed I though it might unbalance the overall purview percentages represented in each pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>When John and Anne began to revise pantheons, they sat down with as many primary documents they could get their hands on and tried to create associations that were as historically accurate as possible. What they discovered is that real pantheons have no sense of game balance! Some had no animal gods or fire gods among their most powerful members, while others had no health gods or prophecy gods. Often a pantheon might actually have a god who can do those things, but that god may not have been Legend 12. Other times there may be gods who use that purview, but they only dabble and would not have every dot of a purview.<br /> <br /> For the most part, we are going to be sticking with the massive amount of research that John and Anne have done because we also value historical accuracy. If a pantheon has too many of one thing, or seems to have nobody with another, then that is the way they really were (to the extent that we can research). It is a great opportunity for a new Scion to rise up and become a god of those things, or wrestle with the political atmosphere of being one god among many who have those things!<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210161#post210161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I happened to notice that the experience rules do not take into account a God's Associated powers or associated abilities for a reduction in experience cost Am I missing it somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we firmly believe that experience points are an OOC mechanic. We have removed every single knack and boon that changes the amount of experience you have to spend. Once per game, you may activate a knack or boon from one of your Associated Attributes or Purviews and the base legend and willpower cost becomes free. You must still pay for any legend and willpower cost beyond the base.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:54:09-07:00","id":210549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210524#post210524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is a great opportunity for a new Scion to rise up and become a god of those things, or wrestle with the political atmosphere of being one god among many who have those things!</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Scion could choose a purview that is not within the Purview list of their divine parent?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Nothing is foolproof for a sufficiently talented fool.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","name":"bigwhitt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:07:59-07:00","id":210602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210549#post210549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So a Scion could choose a purview that is not within the Purview list of their divine parent?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Scion has always been able to do that, even in RAW. There is nothing barring you from being able to take a Purview or Epic Attribute that is not favored with your Divine Parent. There is some encouragement in RAW due to the different exp costs, but we threw that out as quickly as we could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T15:18:23-07:00","id":210607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bigwhitt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210549#post210549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a Scion could choose a purview that is not within the Purview list of their divine parent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher is absolutely right. If your parent has Fire and Water, nothing mechanically stops you from taking Chaos and Prophecy. Because you only need to share one associated epic or purview with your parent, this gives you a lot of freedom to pick a god for roleplaying reasons instead of feeling pressured to pick a god with the most amount of associations like RAW. Our gaming groups have even seen a rise in people picking Lower Legend Gods!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T04:25:32-07:00","id":228980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=185465#post185465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you guys plan on creating any Character Sheets for Scion 2.0, or do you already have some made?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I wonder what they'll go with..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T06:43:08-07:00","id":229022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=228980#post228980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, I wonder what they'll go with..</div> </div> </div> </div>Currently we just use a blank google doc that, while not very fancy (or on the level of Mr. Gone) works out very well for the groups.<br /> <br /> If we were to do a character sheet, we'd probably have to actually find an artist because while Iry, myself, and Emmet have the writing part down, it's the making things pretty part we'll have issues with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T13:14:22-07:00","id":229491,"title":"","content":"A small issue of a sort...I don't like seeing the word &quot;fertility&quot; used for what is essentially &quot;Plant.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T14:41:22-07:00","id":229576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=229491#post229491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small issue of a sort...I don't like seeing the word &quot;fertility&quot; used for what is essentially &quot;Plant.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in the ancient world, the concept of the green and growing plant life was, incredibly commonly, tied hand in hand with the idea of sex and fertility of specific people, or all people. So, for that reason, we have kept the name of &quot;Fertility&quot; for the Purview controlling plant life, and all things green and growing. Fertility is a Purview for the fertility of the land, and commonly the fertility of the Deities or Titans who possess it.<br /> <br /> For example, Freyr is a God of Fertility, bringing growth and new things to the world. And, if you look into his cult statues, he is frequently depicted with colossally exaggerated genitals. This is also seen in Goddesses, such as Oshun, and many others, through exaggerated hips and breasts. One of the (suspected) earliest examples of this are the many different statuettes that have been referred to as &quot;Venuses&quot; by Archeologists and Anthropologists.<br /> <br /> Because of this, the later levels of Fertility are planned to have some powers related to sex. The one I suspect will be most definitely included is one directly linking the fertility of a specific geographic location (Be it the size of Mesopotamia to the size of Ulster) with the fertility of the God or Goddess in question.<br /> <br /> I hope that makes this make more sense Shadowflame, but you are welcome to change the name for your own game if you still don't like it. I suspect we will keep it as Fertility though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:50:51-07:00","id":229645,"title":"","content":"I get it. But it's seems easier to simplify because...y'know...plant. Sex to me is (ball deep) in the health purview...heh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T15:58:02-07:00","id":229650,"title":"","content":"So I noticed that the &quot;Summon Goblins&quot; Earth Boon refers to 2 other Earth Boons from JSR not included in Scion 2.0. <br /> <br /> Also, should I or my players actually come up with a boon to add in here or there, would you rather me post it here or email you folks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:32:43-07:00","id":229689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=229645#post229645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get it. But it's seems easier to simplify because...y'know...plant. Sex to me is (ball deep) in the health purview...heh?</div> </div> </div> </div>While it may be easier to simplify it, we're going for mythical accuracy, so, sex and sexuality is all about trees, the earth, and exagerated sexual characteristics. In fact, I'm probably going to push for all of the children based powers of Health to be put into Fertility. From what I know, prayers for children would go out to the Gods and Goddesses of life and so on, not the doctors. Though, sometimes there is overlap. But, it has not been discussed and we, as a group, may decide to go somewhere else with it.<br /> <br /> But, as always, feel free to change whatever you would like for your own games. If you've got any questions about doing so, feel free to ask. We really do understand that not everyone is as fenatic over holding the accuracy of the ancient world up, and we don't mind at all. We realize we are a bit out there from the standard audience because of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=229645#post229645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed that the &quot;Summon Goblins&quot; Earth Boon refers to 2 other Earth Boons from JSR not included in Scion 2.0.<br /> <br /> Also, should I or my players actually come up with a boon to add in here or there, would you rather me post it here or email you folks?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's incredibly weird, I have no idea why that has happened. Thank you very much for pointing it out, I will check to see if that is intentional somehow or not.<br /> <br /> And, if you have any ideas or suggestions, feel free to email them, or post them here. Whatever you and your group is most comfortable with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T22:16:52-07:00","id":229961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=229650#post229650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed that the &quot;Summon Goblins&quot; Earth Boon refers to 2 other Earth Boons from JSR not included in Scion 2.0.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Good catch! Goblins has been fully updated to Scion 2.0.</b><br /> *Dives back beneath an absolute mountain of PSP research*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T06:44:49-07:00","id":234139,"title":"","content":"Something in another thread I found provocative; Titans versus titans. Or perhaps better to say the older generation of Gods versus...perhaps the ideals that are incompatible with reality that have become incarnate, or something.<br /> More about the former than the latter, are we going to see a little love being thrown to those that supported &quot;cosmos?&quot; (Jord from Norse just got a lot of bad mouthing from Frigga and Hekate was one of the select few that Zeus honored, not that Zeus was such a pal to begin with) And perhaps see an equal treatment to those deities that really come across at times as despicable to shitty and more on the opposing team? (Tanit of Carthage and Moloch from Ammon. With friends like these...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:44:46-07:00","id":234313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=234139#post234139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something in another thread I found provocative; Titans versus titans. Or perhaps better to say the older generation of Gods versus...perhaps the ideals that are incompatible with reality that have become incarnate, or something.<br /> <br /> More about the former than the latter, are we going to see a little love being thrown to those that supported &quot;cosmos?&quot; (Jord from Norse just got a lot of bad mouthing from Frigga and Hekate was one of the select few that Zeus honored, not that Zeus was such a pal to begin with) And perhaps see an equal treatment to those deities that really come across at times as despicable to shitty and more on the opposing team? (Tanit of Carthage and Moloch from Ammon. With friends like these...)</div> </div> </div> </div>In our games, the mantle of Titan and God are morally neutral ones. There are Gods who are cruel, and brutal, and there are Titans who are benevolent in their own way. A being is given the label of Titan if they are distant from humanity, and are made to appear incredibly powerful. Being antagonistic towards the Pantheon of the culture they are from does tend to help one be labeled Titan over God, but that tends to be because the culture they hail from cast them as distant because of that.<br /> <br /> So, for example, The Morrigan is a Goddess. While she is powerful, cruel, and uncontrollable, she is also incredibly closely tied with the myths of the Tuatha. She is one of the most present, the most involved. And for that, she remains a Goddess. But, on the other hand, Danu is a Titan in our games. She is ancient, distant, and incredibly important to Irish mythology and the Tuatha, despite it being unlikely that she is malevolent. She is a Titan through her colossal importance tied with her incredible distance, from not just humanity, but her Tuath as well.<br /> <br /> There isn't as much an 'opposing team' in the games that have been run inside Scion 2.0 that I am aware of (Iry knows more about all the different games testing it out) in the form of the Titans. For example, in Aynie's game, Butterflies and Hurricanes, the Titans have not been playing an antagonistic role as much as the Pantheons have been playing the nemesis for each other. The Egyptians are on the brink of a civil war, the Teotl have taken over Mexico and immediately become incredibly insular, the Inuit and Aesir were about to march to war before the PCs derailed things, and so on. The Titans in Butterflies range from beings like Apep, desperately trying to consume the sun, to Coeus, who is observing with interest the fulfillment of The Prophecy of Zeus' son.<br /> <br /> I hope that answers your question Shadowflame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:29:49-07:00","id":234374,"title":"","content":"I'm not surprised of hearing a &quot;civil war&quot; within a pantheon in some games.<br /> It's just when I read of certain write-ups of titans in 1E, and the omission of others that most certainly deserve at least an honorable mention, well, history treated them far better that the creative use in 1E. (Yes, I understand that omissions are going to happen. There's just way too many floating around) Titans such as Prometheus who was tortured for the sake of humanity (or so it seems to me), I think should have been dealt better. I can easily see followers of him crusading against the unclean flames of Moloch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:53:08-07:00","id":234406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=234374#post234374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not surprised of hearing a &quot;civil war&quot; within a pantheon in some games.<br /> <br /> It's just when I read of certain write-ups of titans in 1E, and the omission of others that most certainly deserve at least an honorable mention, well, history treated them far better that the creative use in 1E. (Yes, I understand that omissions are going to happen. There's just way too many floating around) Titans such as Prometheus who was tortured for the sake of humanity (or so it seems to me), I think should have been dealt better. I can easily see followers of him crusading against the unclean flames of Moloch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Prometheus didn't steal fire for the sake of humanity. That's a really common modern misconception of the myths. What has to be remembered through readings of Greek Mythology is that humanity are like gnats. Prometheus stole fire to give it to humanity not for any love of them, but specifically because Zeus said that no one was to do so. It's a rather tricky chronology of events, mostly because it appears bits and pieces were changed over time, but this is Prometheus' timeline.<br /> <br /> 1. Zeus and the Theoi defeat the Titans and capture Olympus, imprisoning Atlas, Prometheus' brother, Iapetus, Prometheus' father, and killing Menoetius, another brother.<br /> 2. Prometheus teaches humanity how to trick the Gods to give them the worst parts of sacrifices by wrapping the grizzle, and bones in the hide of the animals to spite Zeus for the mistreatment of his family.<br /> 3. Zeus punishes Prometheus and humanity for this transgression. Prometheus is bound to the mountain and ect. Humanity has fire taken away from them to punish them for attempting to cheat the Gods of their sacrifices.<br /> 4. Hercules sets Prometheus free some time in the future.<br /> 5. Prometheus sneaks an ember of The Olympian Hearth out of Olympus in a reed and gives it to humanity.<br /> 6. Zeus creates Pandora to punish Prometheus by proxy through his brother, and once again punishes humanity by giving them all the horrible things lurking in Pandora's vase.<br /> <br /> Now, it is incredibly common that people see this act of Prometheus to be benevolent, but that tends to be from people reading modern values of religion into the situation. Gods who care about us are not common, especially to the ancient Greeks. The Illiad describes us as flies, living and dying in a blink. As far as we can tell, due to no worship, veneration, or thanks being given to Prometheus by the Greeks, we have to assume that they did not see Prometheus giving them fire as a act of benevolent kindness on his part. As best we can tell, Prometheus did it as one final act of spite against Zeus for the mistreatment of his family before vanishing from mythological record.<br /> <br /> People can use Prometheus any way they would like in their games, but as we run things as close to accurate as we can manage, Prometheus didn't do anything for a love of humanity. Prometheus did it because he has a lot of Vengeance. But, a fun plot point could be Prometheus taking advantage of this good press that has materialised for him over the years and using it to continue his vengeful strikes against Zeus, and possibly free his brothers and fathers.<br /> <br /> Just as a side note. Moloch's flames are probably not regarded as unclean by the Elohim (the Pantheon he is from) as Moloch plays an important part in the dance of life and death. Sure, from a modern standpoint, Holy Christ, he probably had children immolated for him. But, as with all things, we need to view them through the lense of the time. While we don't have exceptionally good records of the Elohim, we can assume that, while Moloch may be a colossal dick, he was doing something so important that people would let their children die in return for it. While whatever that was has been lost to time, and the whole thing may be Roman propaganda in the first place, we always have to remember to look past the base level of things and see the ancient world through their own lense rather than our own. No matter how horrific and, as we would see it, barbaric the practices may have been.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I just realized I don't believe I actually explained things, and devolved into an information dump. I'm sorry about that. If you have any questions or comments, just add them in. Some Gods, in a modern sense, are quite horrible, yes. And some Titans (Not Prometheus, but let's say Danu or Svarog) are, well, not colossal dicks seeking to destroy the world. (Svarog sort of does, but it's a really long story. His only role in existence is to rebuild the universe and recreate the Gods when it ends, so when he wakes up, he will assume it's time to start again.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-19-2014, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:20:11-07:00","id":234822,"title":"","content":"Well, if you're going to run things as close as possible, then Prometheus shines up like gold in comparison to the most of the pantheon, spite move on Zeus or no (which actually may recommend him better than most other deities especially if we were scrutinize Zeus say, and the &quot;heroes&quot; he gave birth to, typically from raping)....As for Moloch (I used the wiki article on him), you can't use the argument of &quot;what was acceptable then&quot; because we are speaking of the here and now,. If people can change (and we have on the whole) then the gods need to as well. They should not drag humanity back in time. That leads to barbarism. Child sacrifice should be viewed as a symbolic gesture of killing the future of humanity. And there certainly was plenty of that going around. (Have things changed today in that part of the world? The reality is rather grim, but were I to speak of gaming it up, I would say the future of humanity in such regions has definitely been stunted and could use a titan as Prometheus.)...That's one thing I liked about the Ragnarok book (among others), the idea that gods can change for the better (and worse). (A redeemed Fenris was cool)....I'm just not seeing much differences between the gods and...older gods and titans, except that some here and there were rotten shits, while others were not as bad....I guess I'm just hashing things out between real myth, and game myth in my own head. I understand that the titans in 2E will be more distant than an active threat. (wrong?) I'm more a fan of Nyx anyway...*shrugs*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:22:39-07:00","id":234866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=234822#post234822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if you're going to run things as close as possible, then Prometheus shines up like gold in comparison to the most of the pantheon, spite move on Zeus or no (which actually may recommend him better than most other deities especially if we were scrutinize Zeus say, and the &quot;heroes&quot; he gave birth to, typically from raping)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, entirely. To modern audiences, Zeus is a monster. In Butterflies, Zeus has recently been slain for his mistreatment of a second generation of Theoi, and what Hera saw as him begining to ignore her and further destroy her credibility as a Goddess of Marriage. But, at the same time, if that child of Zeus who stabbed him thirty times in the chest went to Prometheus and asked him why he gave fire to humans, he would say, &quot;To take revenge against your father.&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unless he was being played as particularly cunning, rather than just intelegent, in which case he could use the misunderstanding of his motives for his own gain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=234822#post234822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Moloch (I used the wiki article on him), you can't use the argument of &quot;what was acceptable then&quot; because we are speaking of the here and now,. If people can change (and we have on the whole) then the gods need to as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are entirely welcome to run your games as that Shadowflame, and anyone else is as well. But, that is not how we run ours. Within a year of the return of the Divine in Butterflies, The United States had become an Imperium under an underaged boy. Most of southern Canada merged into the growing Empire, Greece, Italy, Ireland, England, France, Southern Germany, In-land and Atlantic Spain, most of Turkey, and the Baltic regions all came under a single flag.<br /> <br /> Blood ran through the concrete of Tenochtitlan (Mexico City), throats were cut and chests maimed as bodies were thrown to the bogs, men were staked to the shores to offer Sacrifice in the Northlands, no Divine figures were allowed into western Russia and Eastern Europe on pain of Perun. Bagdhad became the city of Marduk as he returned and found Babylon missing.<br /> <br /> And, while no PC has looked into it, I am sure even worse things have happened. The world reverted. The Nordic countries quickly were swayed into being quite gay negative, and establishing very solid gender roles, the same as Mexico, and more.<br /> <br /> In our games, we run that the world very quickly falls under the sway of the Gods once more. Their children, holding in their hearts all the things we brand as 'modern' try to convince them otherwise, and sometimes they succeed. One of the four leaders of Mexico is gay, and she has not been killed for it. While that may seem entirely normal, it is a truely colossal shift, even if just one person is exempt.<br /> <br /> But, anyone is welcome to run it however they want. As I said, you can run your Gods, and your stories however you would like. This is just how we generally run things. We don't demand that everyone bows to our wishes, just that this is how we do it. People are welcome to do so, or not. But, we'll probably not be changing our stance on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=234822#post234822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leads to barbarism. Child sacrifice should be viewed as a symbolic gesture of killing the future of humanity. And there certainly was plenty of that going around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as a student of History, I get incredibly twichy about throwing around the word barbaric or any of its subsets. But, what has to be remembered about sacrifices in the ancient world is that they tended to be offering incredibly, incredibly important things. You would sacrifice a cow, an animal worth half a year's work for you, if you were a sustincance farmer for example. If you were a king, you would sacrifice one hundred. Just as any of those, things are important, so are the lives of humans.<br /> <br /> The symbolism of killing a child, no matter how morbid, can be seen in a thousand different ways. The Romans would wall up a young man from Gaul, and a young woman from Greece inside the walls of special buildings. That could symbolise starving, and leaving young love in the dark, to forever be forsaken. Or, it could also symbolise holding young love close, for eternity, and never allowing it to escape. So, saying that &quot;Child sacrifice should be viewed as a symbolic gesture of killing the future of humanity&quot; is wrong. It can be viewed as symbolically killing the future of humanity, but it doesn't have to. No one person's opinion is any more important than another's when dealing with symbolism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=234822#post234822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one thing I liked about the Ragnarok book (among others), the idea that gods can change for the better (and worse). (A redeemed Fenris was cool)....I'm just not seeing much differences between the gods and...older gods and titans, except that some here and there were rotten shits, while others were not as bad....I guess I'm just hashing things out between real myth, and game myth in my own head. I understand that the titans in 2E will be more distant than an active threat. (wrong?) I'm more a fan of Nyx anyway...*shrugs*</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again, we are not 2E. We are 2.0. We don't know anything that 2E is up to, and I can't remember what they have said about Titans unfortunately.<br /> <br /> But, the lack of a hard distinction between Gods and Titans is important to us. There is not a rule for us that there has to be a colossal difference. Sometimes there is, such as with Apep, who is for all intensive purposes mentally an animal in our games, or with Danu, who is loving and protective of her line (though disappointed and hurt by them as only a mother can be) but incredibly distant, having not spoken to her children in, at minimum, six thousand years. We intentionally run the line between Titan and God as shady. It is possible to have people change sides. In Butterflies, one of the PCs has a goal of breaking the Titans loose, and bringing those lost back into the fold of the Theoi. From Ouranos, to Atlas, to Typhon, he wants to open the doors to.<br /> <br /> Probably won't go well, you can't win every battle. But, it is possible. Typhon could come to Olympus, Atlas could serve as a negotiator between sky and earth, Eos could try to kidnap the young man and try to do as she does. Pan could decide to wander off into the forests and not return, taking the role of a Titan.<br /> <br /> I hope that is a suitable response Shadowflame. We really are not demanding that anyone do as we say with things like this, this is just how we do it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-19-2014, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T00:49:57-07:00","id":235156,"title":"","content":"This isn't even a &quot;We tend to do this, this way&quot; sort of deal. It's an &quot;Aynie runs the gods like this and she happens to be one of the three STs behind the Scion 2.0 project.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do run the gods as changeable as time passes ... to a point. They've been locked into fatebound roles and it would take more than simple eons to break those chains. My gods have, in Butterflies, been forced to wander the world for centuries as Legend 2 beings and while they picked up on some of the changin' modernity of the world, the majority went straight back to Bronze Age politics as SOON as they were given the power and option to do so. Those were the days they ruled.<br /> <br /> And yes, the PCs have not touched the world of Butterflies beyond their personal troubles but thereturn of the Divine was not welcomed everywhere and it went fairly dark in some places.... which directly ties into the next arc.<br /> <br /> But again, that's a personal game using the Scion 2.0 system. We have tried to keep our write-ups neutral without the influence of either my headcanon, or Iry's headcanon coming in the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 08-20-2014, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T15:05:32-07:00","id":235776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=210389#post210389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, all of the Associateds we have up for the site, save for a few we fiddled with in the Theoi and one power on The Morrigan, are their own Associated powers. But, if being defeated by another means you don't get War, Ares does not get it for the jar incident and Diomedes wrecking him, Thor does not get it for he lost a wrestling match with Old Age, Horus loses it since Set beat him like a drum in their own physical combat, and so on. We, ourselves, don't use that to determine who gets War, and neither did John and Anne.</div> </div> </div> </div>I repeatedly had this discussion with them. Again and again. Example after example. They are being inconsistent. John ADAMANTLY maintained that if a god EVER EVER EVER lost to anyone, he didn't have the Avatar, which meant he couldn't have the Purview. It was something that produces ridiculous results, (like Ares not having War, Athena not having whatever the crafting purview was that month, plus all those you name, plus all the others...), but it was 100% a part of the logic of their system. <br /> <br /> I guess if two War gods fought to a draw they could both have the Avatar, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> Giving everyone in the Tuatha War because they took part in battles and 3 battles are the most readily available source of information would mean you need to give all the Greek gods mentioned in the Iliad battle, since they were, ya know... around. Doing enough intervening that Zeus had to order them to stop. <br /> <br /> Even with serious fixing, War still leans towards being a leader, whether from the front, middle or rear, with a shield brother, a squad or an army. Unless you've redone the Avatar as well, it's still The General. Personal combat skill is more an Attribute (and Abilities if they mattered) thing. Ogma isn't a general. He doesn't lead. He's good at fighting. He probably has several War Boons, particularly the personal combat ones, but he's really characterized more by having Epic Strength. His &quot;honey tongue&quot; is more Epic Charisma and Wits (the way they've assorted the various things bards did in battle straddles both).<br /> <br /> In the end, I'd definitely go with War for the Morrigan and for Lugh and Nuada. I would nix it for Ogma and the Dagda. The Morrigan, of course, obviously. Nuada and Lugh because they were both leader through and in times of battle. Not Ogma, for the reasons listed above. Not the Dagda. Perhaps that's the reason the kingship passed to Nuada? Sorta a Moses/Joshua thing? The Dagda was a king in Tir in peace and in plenty. Sure he was hella a fighter, but he wasn't a war-leader, so he stepped down for the &quot;kid&quot; who was?<br /> <br /> A lot of the other mythology is preserved in annoyingly little snippets in the stories about how places got their names. I only have had access to a lot of it by having been close friends with a post doc in the Harvard Celtic Studies Program. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:06:49-07:00","id":235910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235776#post235776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I repeatedly had this discussion with them. Again and again. Example after example. They are being inconsistent. John ADAMANTLY maintained that if a god EVER EVER EVER lost to anyone, he didn't have the Avatar, which meant he couldn't have the Purview. It was something that produces ridiculous results, (like Ares not having War, Athena not having whatever the crafting purview was that month, plus all those you name, plus all the others...), but it was 100% a part of the logic of their system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we too disagreed with that system. We have not yet had a chance to revise all of the Pantheons, currently mulling over a revision to Virtues in order to make the Pantheon Specific Purviews we are rewriting flow better. We are not, as you phrased it, &quot;Using John and Anne logic&quot; for our revisions. We are going to change things as we go, but for the time, the Tuatha are fairly settled with their Associations. I would like to review Manannan, Ogma, The Dagda, and Aengus in the future though. Especially Aengus, he is going to be a mess. I just know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235776#post235776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving everyone in the Tuatha War because they took part in battles and 3 battles are the most readily available source of information would mean you need to give all the Greek gods mentioned in the Iliad battle, since they were, ya know... around. Doing enough intervening that Zeus had to order them to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, I would really like these other primary documents you keep referencing in passing. These myths, and stories that I personally feel that it is being insinuated that I have never read myself. Though I may be misunderstanding the tone of your posts, and that is not what you are saying, if you are, could you please let me know which ones I have missed? I really love Irish mythology, it has become my passion, and it worries me incredibly that I may have missed something so colossally important. <br /> <br /> But, I don't understand your logic of saying that, for example, Aphrodite would have to be given War just because they were present, and active during the Trojan War. We have not given War out to the Tuatha as a participation reward. As I stated in my previous post, all of them save for The Dagda (who I wish to revise anyways) have rather strong connections with War through their roles as Generals and Champions. They have not been given War for being there, Brigid will not be a War Goddess for partaking in those battles. But, those who lead, and those who played Champion to the tuath do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235776#post235776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with serious fixing, War still leans towards being a leader, whether from the front, middle or rear, with a shield brother, a squad or an army. Unless you've redone the Avatar as well, it's still The General. Personal combat skill is more an Attribute (and Abilities if they mattered) thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as I have said before Ajax, we are in the process of changing all of this. War is to be changed, The General won't be called that, and its 'mechanics' will be fiddled with to better suit this division between those who play at single combat, and those who lead. We have not published these changes to War, and I personally believe that, yes, we will be able to change war from only leaning towards being a leader. You are welcome to disagree, but I suppose we will see when we present our finished revisions of War.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235776#post235776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ogma isn't a general. He doesn't lead. He's good at fighting. He probably has several War Boons, particularly the personal combat ones, but he's really characterized more by having Epic Strength. His &quot;honey tongue&quot; is more Epic Charisma and Wits (the way they've assorted the various things bards did in battle straddles both).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no. Ogma has actually played General before, as I said. But, additionally, as we have said, our War is not going to be only for the generals. You will be able to go from Rank One, to Rank Ten without buying a single Boon specifically for those who wish to play General. And, just like that, no General will have to take Boons for the Champions and Warlords. Ogma's role as Champion, the day he leads the Tuatha into battle as their General, and his slaying of Tethra and claiming his magical sword for the moment have War associated with him.<br /> <br /> Additionally, as you mention his honey tongue and how that may relate to the role of Bards in warfare. I have seen a few references to something akin to inspirational speeches before battle, and a possible link to Ogma. My University's library, and those I have access to interlibrary loans from unfortunately do not possess the single book they make reference to, so I am not including it. (Can't use something without having evidence, of course.) But, if it turns out that these references are correct, and we feel that the evidence is sufficient, that is another possible count towards him possessing War. If it is something done exclusively for battle, and whatnot. Not just being an everyday application of Bardic skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235776#post235776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I'd definitely go with War for the Morrigan and for Lugh and Nuada. I would nix it for Ogma and the Dagda. The Morrigan, of course, obviously. Nuada and Lugh because they were both leader through and in times of battle. Not Ogma, for the reasons listed above. Not the Dagda. Perhaps that's the reason the kingship passed to Nuada? Sorta a Moses/Joshua thing? The Dagda was a king in Tir in peace and in plenty. Sure he was hella a fighter, but he wasn't a war-leader, so he stepped down for the &quot;kid&quot; who was?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe there is a point where The Dagda passes the role of King to Nuada. When the Tuatha first land in Ireland, Nuada is organising things. He is specifically mentioned to be the King of the Tuatha at that point. Nuada ceases to be King when his arm (or hand depending on the translation) is cut off by Sreng in this first battle for Ireland. From there, Bres is made King of the Tuath. After Bres reveals that beauty truly is only skin deep, Nuada has his silver hand (or arm) forged, and then his original hand (or arm) regrown by Miach.<br /> <br /> At that point, the Tuatha go to Bres and show Nuada, back to being perfect of body, and demand that he step down as King so Nuada can take over. Bres goes off in a huff, speaks to his mother, and goes to find his father, and his monstrous grandfather, Balor. While this is happening, Lugh shows up and does his Lugh thing, and when the army of the Formori, with Bres, Balor, and worse beings at its front, Lugh is made temporary King for he is both a great warrior and a leader in battle. During this battle with the Fomori, Nuada has his head cut off, and dies.<br /> <br /> But, really, could you please let me know which myths I have missed Ajax? What I'm missing? Because I really do not believe I have only drawn on easily acquired sources of information for the Tuatha. But, if I have, I really would love to know what they are so I can learn them as you have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T17:42:43-07:00","id":235963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235776#post235776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I repeatedly had this discussion with them. Again and again. Example after example. They are being inconsistent. John ADAMANTLY maintained that if a god EVER EVER EVER lost to anyone, he didn't have the Avatar, which meant he couldn't have the Purview. It was something that produces ridiculous results, (like Ares not having War, Athena not having whatever the crafting purview was that month, plus all those you name, plus all the others...), but it was 100% a part of the logic of their system.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is certainly true there were a few notable examples where he DID hold that position (especially regarding Pan and Sound), but I've had several conversations with him (antagonistic or otherwise) where he did not maintain such a position. There is also the very real possibility that he was trolling you. In either case, Anne almost never held that position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:26:33-07:00","id":236015,"title":"","content":"Without reference Im not really sure which you're talking about. Generally my view on reasoning for who has what changes per culture. The &quot;if they lose they dont get it&quot; thing generally only applied to attributes and never purviews. Although, like Iry said, I perhaps was just trolling. Without an exact reference though I cant be sure. I did however always find it important to have ground rules(like if they got beat in a footrace, they wouldnt have dexterity, unless there were shenanigans). But that is because without it, things get weird. At points, Thor is called the most intelligent and almost every goddess is called the most beautiful at some point. <br /> <br /> But most importantly, you shouldnt worry about appling things Ive said in the past to this project. They're doing something completley different and you shouldnt hang my baggage on it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1051-jsr","name":"JSR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T18:27:55-07:00","id":236018,"title":"","content":"I'm sure it's known without being mentioned, but I do feel the need to mention it anyway; wars and battles need more than a general/leader. And those in a battle shouldn't be granted the War purview unless it fits. And for the insistent Scion that doesn't fit into War, maybe select boons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:44:11-07:00","id":236093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=235963#post235963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is certainly true there were a few notable examples where he DID hold that position (especially regarding Pan and Sound), but I've had several conversations with him (antagonistic or otherwise) where he did not maintain such a position. There is also the very real possibility that he was trolling you. In either case, Anne almost never held that position.</div> </div> </div> </div>She did back him up. But I agree, overall, she did not. <br /> <br /> I think he was earnest in his beliefs about the rules, so, not trolling sensu stricto.<br /> <br /> It's besides the point though, I am happy you aren't using the logic as it really limits the game and does the opposite of its intent, which is to represent mythology in game terms. Denying war gods access to War b/c they got slapped around by a mortal or tricked into a jar..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:53:55-07:00","id":236099,"title":"","content":"<br /> I guess, I'd say the best way to get the really fun goofy stories would be to try to get your hands on good translations of the dindisechas. There's also a fair bit stuck in site reports on the arachaeology reports, particularly of the sidhe or raths mentioned in the larger scale stories. <br /> <br /> And you don't have to read 10 paragraphs describing one the enamel-work on one broach that one guy is wearing, but, oh, we don't have the rest of the story, so it pretty much ends there... (If you've ever suffered through <i>Early Irish Myths and Legends</i>). Not that that isn't great and off the beaten path, but the nice little bite size mini-stories have a lot of little choice bits.<br /> <br /> Not easy stuff to get to though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:42:55-07:00","id":236206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=236099#post236099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess, I'd say the best way to get the really fun goofy stories would be to try to get your hands on good translations of the dindisechas. There's also a fair bit stuck in site reports on the arachaeology reports, particularly of the sidhe or raths mentioned in the larger scale stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have read the Metrical Dindsenchas, specifically a copy from the early twentieth century, and the many other ones as presented by UCD, they are really quite brilliant, but, since there are hundreds of them (for anyone else reading, the Dindsenhas are collections of oral poetry detailing how different geographic locations in Ireland got their names. They are a lot like collections of short stories, but there are easily a few hundred of them.) do you know if any of them specifically support the suggested selective reading of the myths of the Tuatha that I've done? The same with the archaeological reports, do you have anything more... specific I guess? While there are not as many archaeological studies in Ireland as I wish there were, there are still quite a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=236099#post236099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you don't have to read 10 paragraphs describing one the enamel-work on one broach that one guy is wearing, but, oh, we don't have the rest of the story, so it pretty much ends there... (If you've ever suffered through <i>Early Irish Myths and Legends</i>). Not that that isn't great and off the beaten path, but the nice little bite size mini-stories have a lot of little choice bits.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal choice of collections of Irish Myths are Lady Gregory's works, specifically <i>Gods and Fighting Men</i>, and <i>Cuchulain of Muirthemne</i> for quick reference. Peter Berresford Ellis also has done a wonderful <i>A Dictionary of Irish Mythology</i> which tends to be for my even quicker reference needs. It has a home beside my keyboard.<br /> <br /> I have not read <i>Early Irish Myths and Legends</i> though, but I checked out the table of contents, and it covers the good standards of things. It is far more resent then my books from Lady Gregory, but I don't think there would be any massive differences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=236099#post236099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not easy stuff to get to though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I'm a history student. This stuff is nothing. I've had to read and transcribe pages upon pages of handwritten Lochmaster journals. Handwritten from the eighteen thirties. The fact that I don't have to spend an hour on every page, working out what in God's name is written on it by someone who was very obviously literate in the most generous of terms using a horrible splochy pen makes me so happy. There may be tons of content in the many different Dindsenchas, but at least they are legible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T23:28:59-07:00","id":236221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=236018#post236018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it's known without being mentioned, but I do feel the need to mention it anyway; wars and battles need more than a general/leader. And those in a battle shouldn't be granted the War purview unless it fits. And for the insistent Scion that doesn't fit into War, maybe select boons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Our new War is not solely for Generals/Leaders, but for Champions who give no shits about leading entire armies as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T20:37:13-07:00","id":244478,"title":"","content":"Hey, what's the latest on Heku, folks? I'm really interested in seeing what you all come up with, especially for a Boon such as JSR's 5-dot <i>Spread Ren</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T22:35:54-07:00","id":244552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=244478#post244478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, what's the latest on Heku, folks? I'm really interested in seeing what you all come up with, especially for a Boon such as JSR's 5-dot <i>Spread Ren</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We haven't done much with the Egyptian PsP yet, we are still working on Me, and the as of yet unnamed Russian PsP, but we just quickly talked about a few different possibilities for the Egyptian Pantheon Specific Purview.<br /> <br /> The three main ideas that Iry came up with off the top of his head, being the one of us which knows the most about the Egyptians, is using the Passage of Rulership, the many-parted soul, or possibly some of their ideas of reincarnation. Now, those are very much brief ideas, and we may not use a single one of them when we do reach the Egyptians to rewrite them, but those are likely the main possibilities.<br /> <br /> Currently, our ideas for Me are rather standard for the concepts of Me, though our focus is likely going to be more on the Me being a lot like a &quot;Divine Permission Slip&quot; or authority from the Great Gods of the Anunna to use some special powers. We have been sidetracked by this into possibly redesigning Virtues, and using this to work Order into Me. But, we may not do so.<br /> <br /> The unnamed Russian PsP is likely going to be based around their worship. Some parts of the idea of taking themes from other cultures, but more of focusing on the innate parts of Bogovi cults inside the cannon of their mythology. Such as having your own priest, and having the much desired horse. Most of this PsP will also technically be violations of the Bogovi's Divine Laws, but a large theme in the Bogovi's myths is the presence of these rules, and the Bogovi constantly doing their best to get around them. <br /> <br /> We have also been working with Griffinguy to revise the PsP of the Aztecs to attempt to give it more of a unique feel, and also avoid being entirely un-Aztec (cutting people's body parts off, and Familial Sacrifice both apparently are totally incorrect). We hope to actually avoid the Scion directly gaining power from making sacrifices until very late Demigod or after their Apotheosis, since all of the power needs to go to the Gods for their eternal battle. The powers will likely benefit the Scion in other ways, such as regenerating Virtue Channels, and other such things.<br /> <br /> Thunder (renamed Storms) and Sky are on the backburner slightly, as we are focusing on the PsPs for the moment. But, currently, our main obstacle is trying to find a way to make creating rain as important in-game as it is for the ancient cultures that would pray for rain and the such. There need to be powers to bring rain, and they need to be quite important, but how to make them mechanically attractive for players is being difficult. <br /> <br /> If anyone has any suggestions, we would, as always love to hear them. Be they about possible Egyptian PsPs, ideas for Me, how the Bogovi could function in violation to their own laws, and so on and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T10:39:16-07:00","id":246216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=236206#post236206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have read the Metrical Dindsenchas, specifically a copy from the early twentieth century, and the many other ones as presented by UCD, they are really quite brilliant, but, since there are hundreds of them (for anyone else reading, the Dindsenhas are collections of oral poetry detailing how different geographic locations in Ireland got their names. They are a lot like collections of short stories, but there are easily a few hundred of them.) do you know if any of them specifically support the suggested selective reading of the myths of the Tuatha that I've done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jaysus, you've read the Dinnseanchas! Fair play to ya!<br /> <br /> There are thousands of Dinnseanchas, extending from the 8th century to the modern day, although the version you have read (the volume from UCD) is the canonical version accepted by the Bardic poetic orders. Irish literature mainly divides into the Mythological cycle, the Heroic Cycle, the Fenian Cycle and underworld stories.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha really only appear in the mythological cycle, so if you've read &quot;The dream of Oengus&quot;, &quot;The Battle of Moytura&quot;, &quot;The wooing of \u00c9ta\u00edn&quot;, &quot;The nourishment of the house of the two vessels&quot;, &quot;About the taking of the Fairy mound&quot;, &quot;The destruction of De Derga's hostel&quot; and the &quot;T\u00e1in&quot;, you will have read most of the stories. There is also some material in the &quot;Book of Invasions&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha can appear sporadically in local, folkloric Dinnseanchas, so I'll look through the ones I have (they are not translated into English yet), what in specific would you like to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T11:53:34-07:00","id":246268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=246216#post246216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jaysus, you've read the Dinnseanchas! Fair play to ya!</div> </div> </div> </div>I, unfortunately, have gotten the tendency to get quite sick every year or so for the last three. So, during the first of those, I was so starved for something to do I started reading through them. They are so, so many of them, but that helped out quite a bit at the time, just for something to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=246216#post246216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are thousands of Dinnseanchas, extending from the 8th century to the modern day, although the version you have read (the volume from UCD) is the canonical version accepted by the Bardic poetic orders. Irish literature mainly divides into the Mythological cycle, the Heroic Cycle, the Fenian Cycle and underworld stories.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha really only appear in the mythological cycle, so if you've read &quot;The dream of Oengus&quot;, &quot;The Battle of Moytura&quot;, &quot;The wooing of \u00c9ta\u00edn&quot;, &quot;The nourishment of the house of the two vessels&quot;, &quot;About the taking of the Fairy mound&quot;, &quot;The destruction of De Derga's hostel&quot; and the &quot;T\u00e1in&quot;, you will have read most of the stories. There is also some material in the &quot;Book of Invasions&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I have read all of them. I'm not sure about &quot;About the taking of the Fairy mound&quot; though. Is that the story of Aengus taking Newgrange from The Dagda using the indefinite article trick? The name of the story sounds like it's the same, but I have never actually heard it named as that. <br /> <br /> It's really too bad we don't have any more stories involving the Tuatha, they really do have a very small batch of myths directly involving them compared to many of the other Pantheons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=246216#post246216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tuatha can appear sporadically in local, folkloric Dinnseanchas, so I'll look through the ones I have (they are not translated into English yet), what in specific would you like to see?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that would be incredibly kind of you. I'm not sure specifically what I am looking for though. I was just asking Ajax which specific stories from the Dinnseanchas, or specifically which Archaeological sites show that I have either been selectively reading Irish Mythology, or have just not read a sufficient amount of it to do work on the Tuatha. If you look at some of the previous posts on this page and the last, you should be able to see our debate. It was mostly over the involvement and importance of warfare in the myths, and giving many of the Tuatha the War Purview for their roles as Champions, Generals, and the like. Obviously not all of them, Brigid, Manannan, Dian Cecht, and a vast majority of the Tuath shouldn't have War associated, but a majority of the Legend Twelve Gods we have posted on our site do.<br /> <br /> If you know of any, of the Dinnseachas, or anything else, that subverts this, totally, please let me know. We are striving for accuracy as best we can, and I wouldn't want to make any blunders. But, the feeling I get, and from what I have read from people far more educated than myself on the subject, those figures deserve War.<br /> <br /> I do actually have a question though. Are those transcriptions of the Dinnseanchas in modern Irish, or the original old Gaelic they were recorded in? Just out of curiosity. From what I have seen, a lot of the old documents, such as the old legal documents, have had very few translations into English. They can be a colossal pain to get where I am because of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T11:13:58-07:00","id":248987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=246268#post246268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about &quot;About the taking of the Fairy mound&quot; though. Is that the story of Aengus taking Newgrange from The Dagda using the indefinite article trick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's it, it's a literal translation of the Gaelic name I know, I don't know its English name actually!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=246268#post246268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do actually have a question though. Are those transcriptions of the Dinnseanchas in modern Irish, or the original old Gaelic they were recorded in? Just out of curiosity. From what I have seen, a lot of the old documents, such as the old legal documents, have had very few translations into English. They can be a colossal pain to get where I am because of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The metrical Dinnseanchas volume that you have contains essentially all of the Dinnseanchas written in Old/Middle Gaelic that is still extant. They would have been standard knowledge for bards, part of their job being able to entertain/educate the nobility by answering questions relating to how towns, fields, rivers, e.t.c. got their name. There is also an element of snobbery in this as the Bards themselves spoke Classical Gaelic*, but would recite the Dinnseanchas material in the Middle Gaelic it was written in, with the result that others often didn't understand the Bards.<br /> <br /> Outside of this, there is far more Dinnseanchas in modern Irish (the collections I possess come to about ~1,000 A4 pages in 12pt print), gathered from people from all over the country from around 1750 to the modern day. I have checked through these to see what image of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann they give. It is essentially the same as the saga literature that you have read. Ogma appears several times as the explanation of how a stone arrived in a certain area (he threw it) and is a general strong man in local folktales. The other gods do not feature much in modern Dinnseanchas, so my conclusion is that the materials you have at hand are not only an accurate representation of the gods, but essentially the only representation of the gods. That is:<br /> <br /> (a) The metrical Dinnseanchas<br /> (b) The book of Invasions<br /> (c) The T\u00e1in<br /> (d) Minor texts that you can double check here to see if you've read them: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mythological_Cycle\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mythological_Cycle</a> (some of these texts repeat material from (a), (b), (c) or are just minor stories in which the gods make guest appearances)<br /> <br /> Other Dinnseanchas barely mentions them and they don't appear in folklore. Growing up for example, I would have only heard the Daghda mentioned in the common phrase &quot;an daghda!&quot; meaning &quot;indeed, really!&quot; or when I was told the T\u00e1in. <br /> <br /> *Also known as Early Modern Gaelic, the difference between it and Modern Irish is something like that between Modern English and Shakespeare, where as Middle and Old Gaelic are like Chaucer and Beowulf respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T22:34:38-07:00","id":249563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=248987#post248987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The metrical Dinnseanchas volume that you have contains essentially all of the Dinnseanchas written in Old/Middle Gaelic that is still extant. They would have been standard knowledge for bards, part of their job being able to entertain/educate the nobility by answering questions relating to how towns, fields, rivers, e.t.c. got their name. There is also an element of snobbery in this as the Bards themselves spoke Classical Gaelic*, but would recite the Dinnseanchas material in the Middle Gaelic it was written in, with the result that others often didn't understand the Bards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that is incredibly interesting. I loved the sections talking about all of the rules for the retinues that the different ranks of Bard were allowed, it's entirely fascinating because the numbers really do get to be rather colossal by the higher ranks, and any King they visited had to feed and shelter them all. It shows you an amazing amount about the culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=248987#post248987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of this, there is far more Dinnseanchas in modern Irish (the collections I possess come to about ~1,000 A4 pages in 12pt print), gathered from people from all over the country from around 1750 to the modern day. I have checked through these to see what image of the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann they give. It is essentially the same as the saga literature that you have read. Ogma appears several times as the explanation of how a stone arrived in a certain area (he threw it) and is a general strong man in local folktales. The other gods do not feature much in modern Dinnseanchas, so my conclusion is that the materials you have at hand are not only an accurate representation of the gods, but essentially the only representation of the gods. That is:<br /> <br /> (a) The metrical Dinnseanchas<br /> (b) The book of Invasions<br /> (c) The T\u00e1in<br /> (d) Minor texts that you can double check here to see if you've read them: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mythological_Cycle\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mythological_Cycle</a> (some of these texts repeat material from (a), (b), (c) or are just minor stories in which the gods make guest appearances)<br /> <br /> Other Dinnseanchas barely mentions them and they don't appear in folklore. Growing up for example, I would have only heard the Daghda mentioned in the common phrase &quot;an daghda!&quot; meaning &quot;indeed, really!&quot; or when I was told the T\u00e1in.<br /> <br /> *Also known as Early Modern Gaelic, the difference between it and Modern Irish is something like that between Modern English and Shakespeare, where as Middle and Old Gaelic are like Chaucer and Beowulf respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brilliant, I will look through some of those in between classes tomorrow. I've not had a chance to check out the minor texts yet, to see if I have read them, but I am going to dig into them in the library. Not really going to be doing much else for the time.<br /> <br /> Thanks so, so much for all of this An Fhuiseog. You're awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T22:41:03-07:00","id":249564,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">In accordance with Ajax's wishes I am removing all posts that directly reference his Private Conversations. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-06-2014, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T17:53:48-07:00","id":250253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I am posting here to show the continuation of our conversation, and our need to have the sources on things. The quoted section is from Ajax, and the following was my response. I decided it was best to just put it up to try to help explain both our reasoning behind using cited information, and why we try to exclusively use it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I really would like to reply to all of this Ajax, but can I please post these to the thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>No<br /> <br /> As previously stated in private communications, I was responding to your previous queries in an attempt to be polite and not &quot;disappear&quot; in the middle of the conversation. However, as I previously stated, I did not want to address matters in the public forum for private reasons. I expected you to respect my desire for privacy and am very disappointed that you did not do so. Especially as I notice you asked my permission, then did not wait for me to give it before you posted my comments then posted them again with your comments interspersed throughout.<br /> <br /> I believe that you have violated several of the forum rules by doing so, especially considering the tenor of your comments. As has griffinguy. I would appreciate it if you removed you both removed your posts that reference mine.<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T17:59:09-07:00","id":250254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I'm bowing out of this discussion for now. I won't be responding to your points in thread. If you wish a private reply, I'll see what I can do, time permitting. <br /> <br /> I have been an archaeologist, a lawyer, an professor in a number of fields, an academic administrator, a curriculum developer and am now coming back to archaeology (having never really given it up as an avocation, but it is truly sublime when your vocation and avocation are one... cf. Canon Theophilus, a Ring of Endless Light, Madeline L'Engle)&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to honestly say that I really appreciate the contribution you have made to this thread. Please understand that the single most overwhelming problem we are having right now is your inability to provide citations for your claims. As someone with such an impressive academic background, you know how incredibly dangerous and unprofessional it would be to take the word of someone over the internet who cannot verify his claims. I wish you the best of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T19:26:16-07:00","id":250316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=250253#post250253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that you have violated several of the forum rules by doing so, especially considering the tenor of your comments. As has griffinguy. I would appreciate it if you removed you both removed your posts that reference mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can feel where you're coming from in some ways. I earned my Ph.D and it would great if people just listened to me whenever I talk about something in my field. But that's not the way academic stuff works. What tenor are you talking about, anyway? I think they're being pretty reasonable asking for citations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T19:35:55-07:00","id":250322,"title":"","content":"Private Messages are not Private. There is/was no NDA or privacy contract. Whatever Watcher wishes to do with the PMs is his right, and as such, you (being a lawyer) should have been aware that anything you say on the internet will probably come up.<br /> <br /> That being said.<br /> <br /> Ajax, you walked into our personal thread about our personal Houserules and proceeded to effectively tell us that everything we were doing is wrong. All right, fine, that's your prerogative, If we are wrong in research, then back up your statements, which is all that's been asked of you. You have not, and in fact, have become offended that we are requiring of you the basic level of commitment towards any academic research before we take your word as gospel.<br /> <br /> I would be laughed out of a first year Intro to Whatever class if I did what you did. We're not belittling or demeaning your accomplishments or knowledge, but we would like citations for it. I even ask them of Griffinguy when I lean on him for mesoamercian knowledge because while I trust him to not bullshit me, I still like to see for myself if possible.<br /> <br /> Now, I would like our thread to return to being about the (belated) Scion 2.0 project and our next release(s). I am hoping to have War released by Monday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 09-05-2014, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T19:55:44-07:00","id":250331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=250322#post250322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Private Messages are not Private. There is/was no NDA or privacy contract. Whatever Watcher wishes to do with the PMs is his right, and as such, you (being a lawyer) should have been aware that anything you say on the internet will probably come up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah...that's one of the reasons why I never send out any really private stuff in a forum I have zero control over. I use personal email instead.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=250322#post250322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I would like our thread to return to being about the (belated) Scion 2.0 project and our next release(s). I am hoping to have War released by Monday.</div> </div> </div> </div>*chuckles*<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Irony, how I have <i>missed</i> you!</span><br /> <br /> I thought the War has already started.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T20:05:13-07:00","id":250334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=250331#post250331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah...that's one of the reasons why I never send out any really private stuff in a forum I have zero control over. I use personal email instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> *chuckles*<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Irony, how I have <i>missed</i> you!</span><br /> <br /> I thought the War has already started.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do not tempt me to put the ability to create Flamewars in the Avatar. I'll do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T20:15:55-07:00","id":250355,"title":"","content":"I find myself...intrigued.<br /> <br /> I need to change my shorts.<br /> I'll be back soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T09:28:25-07:00","id":250809,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">When we wrote that &quot;private information&quot; should not be posted under Rule 5, we intended that to include private messages and e-mails. That clearly wasn't explicit enough, so I'm going to say this under Rule XX: absolutely no more private communications are to be published without the consent of all participants. If you can't discuss a topic without revealing private information, then don't discuss it. If any further private information is posted, bans and other sanctions are likely.<br /> <br /> If you feel a private message violates a forum rule, please report it to the moderators. Don't post it for public consumption. The rules have been updated and clarified to make protection for private messages and e-mails more explicit.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your time.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T11:46:58-07:00","id":250960,"title":"","content":"To pre-empt this problem ever occurring again, if there is some branch of our project that you disagree with, and you want to be taken seriously as a contributor, we ask that you provide sources to back up your claims; or you'll be, unfortunately, ignored in favor of research and information that we actually do have. We don't want to ignore anyone, but &quot;Because I said So&quot; is not enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T10:07:08-07:00","id":273025,"title":"","content":"Just like Summon Goblins in Earth (which has been fixed), I've noticed that Salamander in Fire refers to &quot;Fire Control,&quot; which is a boon I don't see listed. It may be a good idea to check the other purviews that summon things for similar situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T16:13:41-07:00","id":273303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273025#post273025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just like Summon Goblins in Earth (which has been fixed), I've noticed that Salamander in Fire refers to &quot;Fire Control,&quot; which is a boon I don't see listed. It may be a good idea to check the other purviews that summon things for similar situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed Now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T16:17:46-07:00","id":273305,"title":"","content":"I know that you guys are reworking the various Purviews since they were mostly taken from GBN, and as far as I can tell the only &quot;finished&quot; ones are Animal and Chaos. It looks like you've got a few unique Boons scattered through the various Purviews, though--the 1-dot Boons and the 3rd-rank &quot;Aspect&quot; boons, for instance. Are you guys working on the Purviews in alphabetical order? I noticed the website hasn't been updated since June, and I know you guys are doing this for free and have real lives and etc. etc., but I'm itching to see what else you come up with. I really like what you've done so far.<br /> <br /> That said, I had a few mechanical questions: <br /> 1) Ride Animal and Animal Form both use a dice pool of Animal + Larceny, which seems unusual to me. What was your rationale for this? Also, why is there any dice pool at all for Animal Form? There don't seem to be any functions that depend on successes or anything. <br /> 2) Ghostly Figure (Death 3) seems to step all over Mother's Touch (Death 5.) Is there some other benefit to Mother's Touch that I'm just not seeing? I know you're still working on Death, but I just wanted to make sure I wasn't missing anything. Also, I know it's just fluff, but you didn't describe any physical changes from taking Ghostly Figure, like you did with other similar 3rd-rank Boons. <br /> 3) With regards to those 3rd-rank &quot;permanent attunement&quot; Boons--man, I really love these, but they're gonna wreak havoc on your ability to interact with the mortal world in any sort of subtle way without some significant investment in Appearance or Illusion. Flaming hair? Feathers and fur? Barnacles? Awesome, but likely to cause a stir when you go out for dinner. Is it just sort of assumed that by Legend 4 you're only interacting with other Legendary beings? <br /> 4) I like your Fate rules, but are they intended to add to or replace the normal Fatebinding system?<br /> 5) What sorts of guidelines do you have for relic powers? It looks like your example relics do surprisingly few things--mostly channeling purviews, swapping dice pool abilities, and reducing activation costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4009-wynterknight","name":"Wynterknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T18:14:44-07:00","id":273372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that you guys are reworking the various Purviews since they were mostly taken from GBN, and as far as I can tell the only &quot;finished&quot; ones are Animal and Chaos. It looks like you've got a few unique Boons scattered through the various Purviews, though--the 1-dot Boons and the 3rd-rank &quot;Aspect&quot; boons, for instance. Are you guys working on the Purviews in alphabetical order? I noticed the website hasn't been updated since June, and I know you guys are doing this for free and have real lives and etc. etc., but I'm itching to see what else you come up with. I really like what you've done so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for taking an interest! While we have not had any MAJOR updates since June (primarily because I have been working 60-70 hours a week) we have been making small updates here and there. We have a few big ones lurking in the wings which should be coming out in the near future.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Ride Animal and Animal Form both use a dice pool of Animal + Larceny, which seems unusual to me. What was your rationale for this? Also, why is there any dice pool at all for Animal Form? There don't seem to be any functions that depend on successes or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Larceny is the ability used in creating disguises, and the activation roll for those boons sets the difficulty for others to notice that you are not really an animal. This may or may not matter to your character! One of our players has all the Larceny and successfully pretends to be a crow (in combination with some empathy rolls). Another one of our players has no Larceny and just enjoys being an animal even though nobody but mortals mistakes him for a real animal (we joke about every one of his animal forms having a giant frozen beard).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Ghostly Figure (Death 3) seems to step all over Mother's Touch (Death 5.) Is there some other benefit to Mother's Touch that I'm just not seeing? I know you're still working on Death, but I just wanted to make sure I wasn't missing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mother's Touch will be going away as we work on Death. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I know it's just fluff, but you didn't describe any physical changes from taking Ghostly Figure, like you did with other similar 3rd-rank Boons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good catch! Fixed now.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) With regards to those 3rd-rank &quot;permanent attunement&quot; Boons--man, I really love these, but they're gonna wreak havoc on your ability to interact with the mortal world in any sort of subtle way without some significant investment in Appearance or Illusion. Flaming hair? Feathers and fur? Barnacles? Awesome, but likely to cause a stir when you go out for dinner. Is it just sort of assumed that by Legend 4 you're only interacting with other Legendary beings?</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly can do interesting things to your interactions with mortals, but you have the choice to take appearance changes that can be covered up with some heavy clothing. You might still be discovered even then, because Fate has a habit of making the store more interesting. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) I like your Fate rules, but are they intended to add to or replace the normal Fatebinding system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Completely replace Fatebinding, but not Fateful Aura (which is more of a storyteller tool).<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273305#post273305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) What sorts of guidelines do you have for relic powers? It looks like your example relics do surprisingly few things--mostly channeling purviews, swapping dice pool abilities, and reducing activation costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are certainly common (within reason), but we also have a huge number of relics that have unique powers across all the games we playtest on. The only problem with putting up a large number of relics with unique powers is that they tend to have a lot of context you guys would not see (a unique power on one character might be unbalanced for another character, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":484,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","user":"Iry","date":". 10-05-2014, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T20:04:53-07:00","id":273442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273372#post273372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larceny is the ability used in creating disguises, and the activation roll for those boons sets the difficulty for others to notice that you are not really an animal. This may or may not matter to your character! One of our players has all the Larceny and successfully pretends to be a crow (in combination with some empathy rolls). Another one of our players has no Larceny and just enjoys being an animal even though nobody but mortals mistakes him for a real animal (we joke about every one of his animal forms having a giant frozen beard).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, okay, that makes more sense. I keep forgetting that there's no Subterfuge skill in Scion; Larceny feels weird as a &quot;disguise&quot; skill, but I suppose it is the best choice. (Also, I completely misread this at first and thought you had somebody trying to play a sneaky cow, which led to some hilarious mental images.)<br /> <br /> I love the addition to Ghostly Figure.<br /> <br /> And I totally understand about the relics; that area always seems to be one of the most open to interpretation from group to group. You've got some interesting relics on your site, I just noticed that the majority of them use those three options I listed. They gave me some great inspiration, though.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the quick responses!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4009-wynterknight","name":"Wynterknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T20:39:23-07:00","id":273448,"title":"","content":"All right, I need a bit of help. Based on the Pantheons available in Scion 2.0, as listed on the site, who would be considered &quot;Master of The Way&quot; for each? That is, I'm asking for each Pantheon's leading user of Psychopomp. I'm thinking Hermes, Heimdall, Eshu, Susano-o, Quetzalcoatl, and Anubis so far, but was hoping for more input.<br /> <br /> For inquiring minds, I'm running a game and we're about to start a story involving these masters. The band needs to strike a deal with each, from a list, in order to help Susano-o keep a... being... trapped somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T22:09:44-07:00","id":273491,"title":"","content":"While Hermes is definitely the best-known psychopomp in Greek myths, I'd say Hecate was almost as equally well-known for moving between realms--she owned a bit of the World, the Underworld, and the Heavens, after all. Hermes is the &quot;official&quot; psychopomp, though, and was the one who guided souls to Hades, so he'd honestly be my choice. <br /> <br /> I'd say Odin is the premier psychopomp of the Norse gods, rather than Heimdall; I'm not really sure why Heimdall even has psychopomp other than his role as guardian of the Bifrost bridge, whereas Odin was all about gallivanting around the multiple planes of existence and also claimed all sorts of dead souls (warriors fallen in battle, human sacrifices, etc.) for his own.<br /> <br /> Mannanan mac Lir would be my choice for the Tuatha, what with his associations with the otherworld and the lands of the dead.<br /> <br /> The Anunna and Bogovi don't really have any psychopomps that I can remember. I don't think the idea is as important to those mythologies. I know zilch about the Yazata, but they also don't have any listed deities with psychopomp, so that might not be a thing that factored into their myths, either.<br /> <br /> I <i>think</i> Agni is the premier psychopomp of the listed Hindu gods, but I'm not nearly as knowledgeable about non-Western mythologies. Ganesha is described as the God of Obstacles, so maybe him? I'd have to do <i>so much research </i>to answer this.<br /> <br /> Is Susano-o actually a psychopomp? I don't remember that factoring into any myths I've heard about him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4009-wynterknight","name":"Wynterknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T16:35:00-07:00","id":275047,"title":"","content":"Varygoode seems to have most of the big-name psychopomps from most of the Scion 2.0 pantheons, and Wynterknight's suggestions cover some of the others, so I decided to take a look at some Mesopotamian gods to see who might be considered psychopomps by game rules. First, according to JSR's original Anunna supplement, Tammuz has psychopomp associated, so he's one possibility (though he doesn't have it associated in 2.0, so he probably isn't the 'Master of the Way' as you put it). Other than him, I did a quick search of Mesopotamian gods on wikipedia and found only one who might function as a psychopomp; Ninshubar, who is described as being a messenger and a traveler for the other gods, as well as having enough similarities with Hermes that some believe the former may be an earlier version of the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4010-thenotorioussmp","name":"TheNotoriousSMP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T20:17:50-07:00","id":275167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wynterknight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=273491#post273491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think</i> Agni is the premier psychopomp of the listed Hindu gods, but I'm not nearly as knowledgeable about non-Western mythologies. Ganesha is described as the God of Obstacles, so maybe him? I'd have to do <i>so much research </i>to answer this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agni is the conduit between Gods and men, as the being that carries the fruits of sacrifice to the Gods and must be present at every Hindu ritual. He also purifies the dead and releases the soul from the body, but he does not actually guide the soul to the Underworld...that is the job of Pushan, an obscure Vedic era God of journeys and meetings. Yama himself turns up to guide souls occasionally, but those are all for special VIPs like Savitri's husband Satyavan.<br /> <br /> Ganesha is the God of travel (specifically safe and unhindered travel) but he rarely does much travelling himself. It all depends on what you're looking for here...if by psychopomp you mean actual psychopomps, as in guys who guide to dead to the Underworld, use Pushan. If, on the other hand, you mean 'greatest user of the Psychopomp Purview', then I'd suggest going with Agni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T18:12:06-08:00","id":306297,"title":"","content":"Any updates from you fine folks? My games are still going strong!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T18:07:15-08:00","id":308686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>varygoode</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=306297#post306297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any updates from you fine folks? My games are still going strong!</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to be perfectly honest and admit that 70 hour work weeks are absolutely crushing, which is directly impeding progress on most of our projects (especially things like the Anunna and Russian PSPs). War looks like it is the closest to being finished, so we should be putting that up relatively soon.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, because it was absolutely necessary for several of our own games... We did a complete overhaul of the associated abilities and purviews for the Tuatha. We decided to throw out the &quot;Only Legend 12&quot; restriction, which always seemed rather arbitrary. <b>Brigid</b>, <b>Dian Cecht</b> and <b>Goibniu</b> have (re)joined the roster! <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Tuatha de Danann</span></a></div> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T09:52:50-08:00","id":309244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=308686#post308686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We did a complete overhaul of the associated abilities and purviews for the Tuatha. We decided to throw out the &quot;Only Legend 12&quot; restriction, which always seemed rather arbitrary. <b>Brigid</b>, <b>Dian Cecht</b> and <b>Goibniu</b> have (re)joined the roster! <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/pantheons/tuatha-de-danann\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:36px\">Tuatha de Danann</span></a></div></div> </div> </div> </div>hmm..A small nitpick, but on that opening page for them I'd say the Morrigan needs a bit of editing. The sentence structure is off a bit;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Droid Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Though she pledges allegiance to the Tuatha, it is a wise Scion who remembers that she is a force of chaos and slaughter, and not even Nuada has the ability.</i></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T13:20:26-08:00","id":309422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=309244#post309244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small nitpick, but on that opening page for them I'd say the Morrigan needs a bit of editing. The sentence structure is off a bit;</div> </div> </div> </div>The end of that sentence got eaten somehow. Fixed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T05:01:56-07:00","id":1122671,"title":"","content":"What can you tell me about the plans for the Animal Purview? I would also like to inquire about emotional manipulation, would this lead to a purview or would it be done through knacks. By the the way, the Kami document was epic! Thank-you for including the dragon daughters of Ryujin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","user":"Manannansun","date":". 07-30-2017, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T05:05:30-07:00","id":1122672,"title":"","content":"And just one last question. When are the Aesir due to be completed? I apologize if I seem rude, but I found it funny that one of the most popular pantheons remains unfinished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","user":"Manannansun","date":". 07-30-2017, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:33:45-07:00","id":1122775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1122671#post1122671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can you tell me about the plans for the Animal Purview? I would also like to inquire about emotional manipulation, would this lead to a purview or would it be done through knacks. By the the way, the Kami document was epic! Thank-you for including the dragon daughters of Ryujin.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Animal Purview is actually complete, it was either the first or second Purview to be totally translated over. Is there anything you are looking for in an Animal Purview revision that it doesn't have? I could talk to Iry about it later today if it is.<br /> <br /> For emotional manipulation, that is broken up across various Purviews and Epic Attributes. Darkness and Negative Epic Appearance have some Fear and Terror elements. Sun, and Charisma have overwhelming Hope and Adoration in there. Fire has some 'Supercharged Emotion' powers. Epic Manipulation and Epic Charisma are the 'core' pieces for playing with emotions though. The <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/epic-attributes/charisma#TOC-Emotion-Knacks\" target=\"_blank\">Emotion chain</a> of Epic Charisma Knacks are my personal favorite. <br /> <br /> If you want to play someone who works like Cupid, or other Love-Causing entities, the way we have normally addressed it in our games is through very powerful Relics altering how Engender Love works. Making it cheaper, potentially free when targeting mortals, making it permanent (that would be up there in power with The Helm of Darkness or Lugh's Spear though) and other such little twists to the power. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1122672#post1122672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And just one last question. When are the Aesir due to be completed? I apologize if I seem rude, but I found it funny that one of the most popular pantheons remains unfinished.</div> </div> </div> </div>At one point the Aesir were someone I was looking at revising, but they have since fallen to the wayside for two big reasons which I can explain.<br /> <br /> First off, we are waiting for Scion Second Edition to come out. We want to get our hands on the new system and see if we want to make a swap, and if we do, we need to decide how we want to go about using our updated Pantheons. We have not stopped working on Scion though, myself and Sacerdos have been stockpiling research, making in-depth outlines, doing all the 'fluff,' the cultural notes, potential Deity lists, that sort of thing for Pantheons. With luck, when Scion Second Edition comes out, we will be able to get three or four Pantheons up and running far quicker than normal. <br /> <br /> And that ties into our second reason. When we finished the Kami, Sacerdos and myself spent some time talking about what to do next. The Kami were a 'step up' from other Pantheons I had prodded at previously. It was a massive undertaking which I wouldn't have been able to complete by myself for a ton of reasons. I want to keep up that level of writing and research, I want big, stupidly long Pantheons with cultural notes, talking about fun little bits of cosmology, everything. I initially was thinking of looking at the Aesir, or the Shen, but we decided to not revise a Pantheon in favor of creating entirely new ones.<br /> <br /> These new Pantheons we have stockpiled research for are intentionally all non-European, we want to widen up the choice for people.<br /> <br /> The Shiunesh, the Pantheon of the Hittite Empire are amazingly fun. A Pantheon who frequently almost brings total extinction to their mortal population for failing to honor them correctly. They really serve as a nice little addition to the Eastern Mediterranean, the Pantheon having a real-world long time friendship with the Netjer. Gotham By Night had started looking into writing up the Shiunesh before they closed their doors, so we thought it would be nice to quench anyone's thirst that had been kicked off by that.<br /> <br /> The Abosom, the Pantheon of the Ashanti Empire, are also awesome. Where the Shiunesh are <i>very</i> 'classical Scion' with a Titan War, imprisoned Titans, all of that, the Abosom are a big jump away from standard Scion. They have a Supreme God who makes sure that mortals have a nice life more or less, a very friendly cosmology. They don't have any imprisoned Titans, or have a ton in that department at all. Nothing openly antagonistic on the scale of Apep or even just a random Fomori. They are the cultural group who has Anansi hanging around with them who is also really awesome.<br /> <br /> The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s, the Pantheon of the Haida First Nation are also great. They are again a slight deviation from your standard Scion Pantheon. They have a Supreme God, but they are nowhere as involved as Nyame and more or less just stay distant from the world and even the Supernatural Beings themselves. Xhuuya, commonly known as Raven, is from this Pantheon and he is a ton of fun. They have three 'groups' of Divine Entities, rather than having one single 'group' as many Pantheons do. Essentially, they have three different Overworlds each with its own internal hierarchy. The <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hlk\u2019yaans x\u00e0aydaraay, the Supernatural Beings who reside in Diidguii, The Forest. The T</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">saran x\u00e0aydaraay, the Supernatural Beings who reside in Siigee, The Sea. The </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sg\u0101\u2019na x\u0101\u2019-idAga-i, the Supernatural Beings who reside in </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Q\u014d\u2019ya-iq\u0101\u2019gAn, The Sky.<br /> <br /> The Enduri, the Pantheon of the Manchu, are the group we are still digging into. I am helping Sacerdos with them, he has the reigns for them, and is doing a great job. We have both been very busy with finishing our final years of our Undergrads, and working, so they are not yet finished. But, with luck, I should have some free time coming up to hammer into them and actually read the articles and take notes for Sacerdos. They are a really cool Pantheon from what I have seen so far, almost all Goddesses, and they have an amazing creation myth. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:52:37-07:00","id":1122781,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info watcher. I look forward to seeing the results. Good luck with your undergraduate degree, may I ask what your major is? I majored in Religious Studies and focused on modern polytheism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T13:12:50-07:00","id":1122786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1122781#post1122781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the info watcher. I look forward to seeing the results. Good luck with your undergraduate degree, may I ask what your major is? I majored in Religious Studies and focused on modern polytheism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have actually just finished my degree, graduated last month. I was all ready to sit down and grind away at the Manchu, but then I managed to net a summer job doing historical writing, so that's put the brakes on again. My undergrad is in history, no official focus, but I specifically chose classes that would help me with my MA in Celtic Studies. I spent most of my undergrad looking at Christianization attempts, both the successes and failures, as well as medieval European Christianity, and courses on early Ireland.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T20:53:09-07:00","id":1122891,"title":"","content":"If you like the Scion 2e system, are all the additional pantheons intended to continue being free or will be sold as part of the community content licensed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:27:57-07:00","id":1122914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingCarnival</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1122891#post1122891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you like the Scion 2e system, are all the additional pantheons intended to continue being free or will be sold as part of the community content licensed</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say for sure, not without seeing the rules for the community content, and with that information having a conversation about it. I don't really want to say any more than that just in case it gives the wrong idea somewhere, but we have already discussed the vague idea, and there is no schism or anything. When those rules are in the community's hands, we will have a more in depth conversation amongst ourselves about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T10:52:06-07:00","id":1132697,"title":"","content":"What sort of psp would you give the Plant Annwn or the Plant Don?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T11:32:02-07:00","id":1132719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1132697#post1132697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of psp would you give the Plant Annwn or the Plant Don?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, a particularly tricky question. I have done some course work on Welsh literature, but they are not the region I am best at. The Irish and the Gauls are the two Celtic regions I am best versed in, the Welsh, despite having read a bunch of their literature, is something I haven't explored as deeply as Ireland or Gaul.<br /> <br /> I can think of some concepts that might be fruitful for a Pantheon Specific Purview however. The one that I have batted around in my head the most is the idea of Fate, but in an entirely different way than the Aesir approach it. What Welsh literature is particularly valuable for is illustrating a perception of Fate which is rather unique compared to the other Western/Northern European groups. Where as the Aesir have a predeterministic Fate system, that What Will Be, Will Be, the Welsh can be seen operating on a different wavelength. Llew Llaw Gyffes and Math fab Mathonwy both have 'Fate Clauses' on them. Math fab Mathonwy must have a virgin footholder when he is not at war or he would die. Llew Llaw Gyffes has a really weirdly specific series of clauses relating to his death. This idea is most evident with the 'Death Clauses,' but they exist in other areas, such as the curses Arianrhod places on her son Llew, all of which are conditional which allows Math to help skirt around them.<br /> <br /> The exact mechanical system for this would probably really depend on the Fate system someone is using, but I have some rough drafts of a revised Wyrd I was fiddling with a few years ago for the Aesir that I can plunder for ideas. I would probably make it very hard to die if the specific clauses were not fulfilled, perhaps impossible to die if they are not. (which may sound like a strong power, but I would rate it middling at best. Not being able to die just means you'll get your head cut off and carried around like Bran) I would include ways to place these conditional effects on people, both for good and bad, and a series of Boons that increase the mechanical function of your own personal ones.<br /> <br /> Now, this may sound like it has the same problem as RAW Geasa, as 'Fuck it up and Die,' mechanics are just not fun for the Storyteller or Player. Thankfully, Welsh mythology shows us that while these clauses need to be fulfilled to kill someone (if it is a death-conditional and not like, 'You will never have a name least it come from my own lips' sort of thing) it doesn't mean that the person <i>will</i> die. Llew has all of his clauses filled, and <i>almost</i> dies. He becomes mortal, it is possible for him to have died, but he manages to pull through, though he is in disgusting shape from the wound he was given until he heals up. Really brought him to the brink.<br /> <br /> From the little digging I can do, I think this concept is called 'Tynged,' but sadly my University isn't big on medieval Welsh literature, so I don't have a massive amount of resources on hand for this one. I can find the concept mentioned a few times alongside <i>Wyrd</i> as a Fate system though in some articles in passing, so I think it might be the right name. Wikipedia for some reason links it with the Geasa, which I don't entirely agree with. It feels fare more like the Norse concept of <i>Wyrd </i>than the sacred pledges / taboos of the Irish.<br /> <br /> I would probably start the PsP off with a Boon that places one of these Tynged on the Scion, I would probably start off with a Death Clause one, have the player outline one situation that needs to be filled for them to be mortal. (Not invulnerable) The exact breakdown of what the Boons would be would depend on the Fate system in play though since this PsP would probably build very heavily off that mechanical skeletal structure.<br /> <br /> While I have only given a few examples of Tynged in the literature, I am fairly sure there are several more floating around in the other Branches and perhaps some of the other literature. I think it could be tied into the Arthurian themes of the later stuff as well, &quot;Whomsoever Pulls This Sword,&quot; sounds like a Conditional Clause not a Predetermined thing. The rule isn't &quot;Arthur Pendragon Will Pull This Sword Out and Be King of all Britain,&quot; but &quot;<i>Whomsoever</i>.&quot; I think there are several Tynged-esque ideas in the story of Culhwch and Olwen as well.<br /> <br /> I hope that proves somewhat helpful!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:37:41-07:00","id":1132857,"title":"","content":"Thank-you again Watcher, I am of course aware of the &quot;death clauses&quot; but was completely unaware of Tynged. And this gives me a large number of ideas. Not to mention the concept jives with some idle speculation I have been having. Also I believe it's Gwydion not Math who aids Llew in bypassing the restrictions placed by Aranrhiod not Math. Anyways I appreciate the information, I'll put it to good use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-22T17:59:01-07:00","id":1132865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1132857#post1132857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank-you again Watcher, I am of course aware of the &quot;death clauses&quot; but was completely unaware of Tynged. And this gives me a large number of ideas. Not to mention the concept jives with some idle speculation I have been having. Also I believe it's Gwydion not Math who aids Llew in bypassing the restrictions placed by Aranrhiod not Math. Anyways I appreciate the information, I'll put it to good use.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are absolutely right, I was writing that bit and going. &quot;Wait, was it the king? That wouldn't make sense since the foot-thing...&quot; but ignored my gut. It's absolutely Gwydion who helps Llew through his youthful misadventures. If there is anything else I can help with, just let me know. The Welsh are not my strong point, but hopefully I should have access to a bunch of books on the topic soon-ish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T09:26:34-07:00","id":1133044,"title":"","content":"Sorry to bother you again Watcher, and I know it isn't your forte but can you offer some suggestions on Purviews for Arawn of Annwn? I am currently stumped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T13:15:00-07:00","id":1133136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1133044#post1133044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to bother you again Watcher, and I know it isn't your forte but can you offer some suggestions on Purviews for Arawn of Annwn? I am currently stumped.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I can suggest some Purviews. I assume you've got the Epic Attributes and Abilities sorted out for him?<br /> <br /> <b>Illusion </b>is a big thing for Arawn, disguising himself and Pwyll flawlessly as the other for an entire year. That is a particularly potent use of Illusion. Lasting a long time, not getting noticed, functioning at great distances, all of that. So, I would be entirely comfortable giving him the Illusion Purview.<br /> <br /> Then, next I would suggest considering the <b>Animal</b> Purview, specifically <b>Animal (Pigs, Hounds)</b>. If you are looking at using the 2.0 rules for this, then the Animal Purview includes the conceptual branch of the 'Hunter' as well as the 'Beast' so this would be appropriate for Arawn. The major time we see Arawn in the texts is when he is on a hunt with his strange otherworldly hounds. Later on in folk tradition, these hounds show up as creatures hunting across the land, being turned into Hell Hounds rather interestingly. Whatever their function, most likely as just hunting hounds, they are a decent part of Arawn's myth. Normally I wouldn't give Animal for such a reason, <i>however</i> there is something else. Arawn gives pigs to Pwyll's son Pryderi as part of a continuation of friendship. From what I remember of the text, these are not 'just' magic pigs. These are the first pigs anyone has ever seen, and they're insanely valuable because of that. So, having some animals doesn't give you the Animal Purview, even if they are fancy animals. <i>However</i>, giving humanity a new species of animal to farm, <i>that</i> is really 'up there' in the Divine-tiers, so in conjunction with the other bits, I would give him <b>Animal (Pigs, Hounds)</b>.<br /> <br /> After these two, I would consider giving him <b>Justice</b> for three reasons. Firstly, he is the king of his own special domain. This alone doesn't really give someone Justice, but having an important tie to Kingship does help a bit. Secondly, when he rules Pwyll's lands, everything is perfect and generally awesome, suggesting that Arawn is a <i>really good</i> king, which again, alone doesn't justify the Purview, but is a bit of a help. Lastly, and most importantly in my mind, is that he tested Pwyll's morality. He had not expected Pwyll to refrain from sleeping with his wife while disguised as himself, a theme that will show up many times in the future of Welsh literature (both people doing so, such as Uther, and people not, such as Gawain-kinda). He is so impressed by this, he and Pwyll forge a friendship that will outlast Pwyll's own life, and Pwyll is given high honors. The morality test part of this, especially since this is the genesis point of a very important cultural theme, and the kingship bits I feel does a fairly good job justifying <b>Justice</b> for Arawn.<br /> <br /> The big challenge you have organizing Arawn's set is the nature of Annwfn / Annwn is. There is no evidence of it being an Afterlife until later on when Arawn starts getting linked up with Satan in medieval folklore. From what I know (which, again, not my area of expertise at all) is that the later reconstruction efforts painted Annwfn as an Afterlife, drawing evidence from the connection with Satan, and the place being underground. The Satan connection is, in my mind, not really evidence of much at all. He is conflated with almost anyone, no matter if they actually have anything to do with each other symbolically, or through cosmological function. I would say that the conflation was likely just rooted in an attempt to fit Arawn into the folk-christianity of the time, that sort of thing happens a lot. The 'Underground' image of Annwfn, which is sometimes used to explain it as a Afterlife, I disagree with for two reasons. Not all Afterlives are underground, and somewhere just being underground shouldn't flag it as an afterlife. Secondly, the whole 'Underground' bit only started with the conflation with Satan, and therefore has no root in the original stories. The realm is described as a otherworldly kingdom, on the surface, and on the Welsh peninsula somewhere. So, I personally would <i>not</i> give Arawn the Death Purview. However, if you want to run Annwfn as an afterlife, in which case Arawn should have Death.<br /> <br /> So, in sum. Animal (Pigs, Hounds), Illusion, Justice. At least, using Scion 1e. I expect that it will be far easier to flesh Pwyll out in 2e looking at the Purviews names they have given us.<br /> <br /> I will also add that this isn't how I normally go about giving Purviews. I feel that it's really important to have a grasp on the whole Pantheon and what everyone is up to before handing out Purviews and Epic Attributes. I treat each Pantheon on their own terms, so what might justify Epic Strength for one of the Tuatha wouldn't justify it for one of the Theoi for example. Further, I consider it to be important to work out what each Pantheon has 'going on' for themselves. For example, writing up all of the Theoi in a vacuum, and they will all end up with Epic Appearance. Writing the Theoi up in the context of their Pantheon, then you will see that while everyone is beautiful beyond mortal comprehension, some are more beautiful than others, and <i>they</i> are the ones who get Epic Appearance. Let each Pantheon set their own bars essentially, it helps keep things working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T15:45:27-07:00","id":1133196,"title":"","content":"Thank-you Watcher. Arawn has been on my mind a lot ever since I started researching his depictions in media, especially in Scion which I felt was highly inaccurate. I am creating a database of modern faerie depictions which of course includes kings, queens, and Christanized Deities. Anyways, while we are on the subject, how do you feel Manawydan differs from Manannan? Finding modern accounts of Manannan as the faerie king of Mann actually gave me the idea to begin with. And what do you think Rhiannon's relationship to Arawn is exactly? Rhiannon is implied to be from Annwn, so does this mean Arawn sent her to Pwyll as some sort of test? Perhaps she's his daughter? What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T18:04:19-07:00","id":1133235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1133196#post1133196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank-you Watcher. Arawn has been on my mind a lot ever since I started researching his depictions in media, especially in Scion which I felt was highly inaccurate. I am creating a database of modern faerie depictions which of course includes kings, queens, and Christanized Deities. Anyways, while we are on the subject, how do you feel Manawydan differs from Manannan? Finding modern accounts of Manannan as the faerie king of Mann actually gave me the idea to begin with. And what do you think Rhiannon's relationship to Arawn is exactly? Rhiannon is implied to be from Annwn, so does this mean Arawn sent her to Pwyll as some sort of test? Perhaps she's his daughter? What are your thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that sounds quite neat Manannansun. I would be interested in seeing it whenever you find it in a presentable state.<br /> <br /> I can't remember where he was mentioned in Scion, I assume in Companion in the odd Underworld section they gave the Tuatha in RAW. Now, modern accounts I can't really say anything for. I work primarily with the medieval and early medieval literatures with only a dabbling in later folklore. Nothing that I would call modern, nothing from the last two centuries in the least. Straying away from what is written, getting into the realm of reconstruction, that is the point where my usefulness ends.<br /> <br /> Manannan and Manawydan are rather different figures in my readings of them. Sure, they may have at one point been a shared figure somewhere along the line, but they have been rather heavily changed by time, and by their recorders. Manawydan is wise, but not quite a magical trickster. He lacks the unending wealth of Manannan, and lacks any lands. In fact, that is likely the most important division of their characters. Manannan's connection to the oceanic otherworlds of Irish tradition is rather core to his character, while on the other hand, Manawydan lacks any connection to the ocean, and <i>very specifically</i> has no kingdom. He is spoken of in the texts of being this odd Landless Noble, a very strange concept. His lack of lands and wandering nature is important to him. But, nothing to do with the water, he just walks around Wales. Manawydan is more upstanding, lacking the Trickster angle to the degree that it defines Manannan, and is one of Arthur's many knights in the early lists.<br /> <br /> There might be a shared name, or possibly an ancient shared connection between the pair, but they are massively different. Their personalities are different, their positions within their respective literatures is different, their potential divine function is quite different. All they have is the name.<br /> <br /> For Rhiannon and Arwan, I don't think that she really has anything to do with him at all. A primary feature of Rhiannon in my reading of her character is that she has agency. By making it all part of some test by Arwan I think that agency that is very obviously being given to her by the author of the text is removed. We meet Rhiannon's father in fact, and he ins't Arwan. His name is Hyfaidd Hen (Hyfaidd the Old) and his lands are not otherworldly as Annwn is. Pwyll seems to know of Hyfaidd the Old since it forms a part of Rhiannon's introduction to him, there wouldn't be much of a point of her including it if Pwyll didn't know who she was talking about. I don't know where the implication she is from Annwn is, sure she's an otherworldly woman, but she's really just from around the block geographically. I don't think that there is any reason that Arwan would have for testing Pwyll at this point, Pwyll has already slain Arwan's one rival, ruled Annwn well, and did not sleep with Arwan's wife. In-character, I can see no reason Arwan would be testing Pwyll again, and the text never suggests it.<br /> <br /> Rhiannon is just a local titulary entity, she is a Soverignty figure in the text, that sort of thing. I don't think there is any relationship with Arwan past that they would meet each other one day since Arwan is so Pro-Pwyll and she has always loved Pwyll. Sure, they are both magical, otherworldly people, but there is never any suggestion that there is any connection between the two in text. There's also no suggestion that Bran, or Manawydan are related to either of them (before the third branch at least for Manawydan and Rhiannon). They are all magical and semi-Otherworldly, but they all seem to be operating in their own little areas.<br /> <br /> I think Rhiannon's agency is big though, she can't have been sent by Arwan without compromising the character she is written with. She has chosen to love Pwyll, and no one is allowed to marry her without her consent. Big stuff for the period. She even does the Niamh thing where she rolls up on her mortal boy-toy and sort of tells him that they're going to be lovers. Making her part of some test by Arwan undermines her character, and there doesn't seem to be any support in the text for such a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T02:59:01-07:00","id":1133311,"title":"","content":"Why no love for the Allied or Yankee pantheon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />? ((i am one of those heretics that actually liked em &lt;.&lt;))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T14:41:39-07:00","id":1133555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1133311#post1133311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why no love for the Allied or Yankee pantheon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />? ((i am one of those heretics that actually liked em &lt;.&lt;))</div> </div> </div> </div>Alas, we are not big fans of the World War Pantheons, or the Atlantean Pantheons. We are working towards keeping things as mythically accurate as possible, and the Pantheons from the World War II section of Companion are just not up to snuff. With luck there will one day be replacements for them which are more accurate, looking into Slavic, and various First Nations Pantheons is something that quite interests me. With luck a Haida Pantheon should be somewhere on the horizon to help flesh North America out a bit more for example. (They will be done in a similar scale to the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nn03gHFj_tgASkDPGbI1FgtTBff88OrgioSJzyIvEbY/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Kami revision</a> we did)<br /> <br /> I entirely understand that other people really do like those Pantheons though, and that's totally cool! They're just not really in the remit of our project. If you want help figuring out some houserule'd information for those Pantheons, or want some help researching the figures involved with it Caedus, I would be happy to lend you a hand though! Just let me know if there is anything I could do to help you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 08-24-2017, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T07:22:35-07:00","id":1133780,"title":"","content":"I don't know where it ended up, but there was a really great breakdown written by Telgar. It went down the list and described each member of those Pantheons and what they probably were by Scion standards. Things like Pecos Bill being a demigod, Paul Bunyan being a giant with a nemean (or typhonean) ox, one of the Russian soldiers being a nationalistic ghost that would possess soldiers and lead them to brave deeds until they died, and Betsy Ross just being a nice little old lady.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T18:33:35-07:00","id":1135649,"title":"","content":"Does the artistry purview cover acting as well as film?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T18:50:16-07:00","id":1135653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1135649#post1135649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the artistry purview cover acting as well as film?</div> </div> </div> </div>Artistry covers pretty much most forms of human artistic or technological creation. Acting and film both totally fall into the realm of the Purview. A Scion may devise a Relic monologue using the Artistry Purview for example. Actually preforming the play or movie in question might use Epic Manipulation though, similarly to how creating a magical bow uses Artistry, but to use it you need to use Epic Strength, Dexterity, or Perception.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense? Inspiring others to be good actors, editors, or film makers is totally part of Artistry. Creating a script, or a musical score, or editing a draft of something is also Artistry. But, actually <i>using</i> the 'tool' that has been created starts to enter the realm of the Epic Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T05:15:22-07:00","id":1136895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1133196#post1133196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finding modern accounts of Manannan as the faerie king of Mann actually gave me the idea to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, modern accounts I can't really say anything for. I work primarily with the medieval and early medieval literatures with only a dabbling in later folklore. Nothing that I would call modern, nothing from the last two centuries in the least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manann\u00e1n Mac Lir became extinct within modern folklore. It's possible that he may have survived as a character in the stories of some of the minor dialects, however all the folklore collections from the major dialects don't contain a single story mentioning him (I have just checked all them to confirm).<br /> <br /> Even within Classical literature (1150-1700), tends to say he was really a man named Oirbsean and very little narrative content on him can be found. I've checked a few Classical poems and seen no proper mention of him, but I'll keep looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T10:55:52-07:00","id":1136966,"title":"","content":"Actually got the time to check through my collection of Classical Poetry today. He isn't mentioned once, outside being identified as the name sake of a lake (under his &quot;real&quot; name Oirbsean).<br /> <br /> Although to give you an idea of how forgotten these characters were, a storyteller from the late 19th century knew Lugh Mac Eithleann as &quot;C\u00fa Chulainn's father from the Sidhe&quot;, the Daghdha had to be explained as &quot;the King of the Sidhe&quot; (even though &quot;An Daghdha&quot; still survives as an exclamation meaning &quot;oh really!&quot;) and the M\u00f3rr\u00edoghan is described by two separate storytellers as &quot;an ancient genius in battle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:18:57-07:00","id":1140541,"title":"","content":"Hi Watcher!<br /> I have a couple questions that you can probably answer. If a Irish Scion with Justice 4 Code of Heaven activates the boon in response to someone asking them to leave a place of business, that they were previously a valued client at does this work as an instance of Hospitality Breeching? It seems to me that it does since the owner welcomes a customer inside, offers them amenities, treats them like a honored guest, which is the same thing the Tuatha would do when welcoming a guest. In fact isn't the business essentially the owner's home while they work? If I am correct, what would Justice 5 An Eye for a Eye do in this instance, or indeed in any instance of hospital breeching? Would it allow them to make a highly valued customer or friend reject them? Or would it be something else?<br /> <br /> Secondly, when using Magic 8 The True World, does this also enact Justice 4 Code of Heaven? This would seem logical, especially if a deity with both purviews used it. Or is this incorrect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","user":"Manannansun","date":". 09-15-2017, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T12:50:49-07:00","id":1140604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1140541#post1140541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Watcher!<br /> I have a couple questions that you can probably answer. If a Irish Scion with Justice 4 Code of Heaven activates the boon in response to someone asking them to leave a place of business, that they were previously a valued client at does this work as an instance of Hospitality Breeching? It seems to me that it does since the owner welcomes a customer inside, offers them amenities, treats them like a honored guest, which is the same thing the Tuatha would do when welcoming a guest. In fact isn't the business essentially the owner's home while they work? If I am correct, what would Justice 5 An Eye for a Eye do in this instance, or indeed in any instance of hospital breeching? Would it allow them to make a highly valued customer or friend reject them? Or would it be something else?<br /> <br /> Secondly, when using Magic 8 The True World, does this also enact Justice 4 Code of Heaven? This would seem logical, especially if a deity with both purviews used it. Or is this incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'm more than happy to help answer your questions!<br /> <br /> So, for Hospitality. Having someone in your store wouldn't necessarily count as inviting hospitality to someone, the rules about it are both very complicated, and very simple. Depending on your social class, mostly detailed by your profession, you were given certain rights. One of these was the right to ask for hospitality from someone. Now, depending on your rank, and the rank of the person you are asking hospitality from, they may or may not have an obligation to provide hospitality on request.<br /> <br /> In the legal tracts, this is mostly a bunch of charts noting the rank of the asker, the rank of the askee, and then some extra notes such as the size of the retinue that needs to be supported. For example, a farmer would have to always give a King/Chieftian hospitality, giving them food, drink, and somewhere to sleep. The farmer was not expected to provide this for the entire retinue of their royal guest. Comparatively, if a Provincial King asked a Regional King/Chieftian for hospitality, the Regional Chieftian would be expected to provide for the King's retinue (up to a certain number, it's very detailed.)<br /> <br /> So, simply refusing to serve someone wouldn't be a violation of hospitality. Doing business with someone doesn't mean they are providing you hospitality, even if you are buying food, or shelter from them. However, you could ask for hospitality from them, and they might be expected to give it to you. If you were in a legal position to request hospitality, and they refused, that would count as a violation of Hospitality law and they could be compelled to pay you a fee based on their own rank, and your rank. <br /> <br /> If your character, and the store owner are both free individuals (not slaves) than they would be expected to provide hospitality for you. But, you must request it, and they must refuse before it would be a violation of hospitality. Depending on what profession your character is, the exact details would vary.<br /> <br /> Using <i>An Eye for an Eye</i> would likely have someone refuse them hospitality the next time they asked. It specifically has to be an echo of the broken law, so refused hospitality causes refused hospitality, theft causes theft, etc. So, if they refuse your character hospitality and you use the Boon, the next time they ask anyone for hospitality, it will be refused. Why? That will be up to the Storyteller. It might be that their friend who they just asked for hospitality from is out of town, but it couldn't cause their friend to dislike them, or cause a customer to stop using their services. <br /> <br /> Using <i>The True World</i> doesn't enact <i>Code of Heaven</i>, though I can see how it might sound like it does. <i>The True World</i> imposes one own's Pantheon's narrative concepts, and cosmology on the local area. It makes the natural laws of one's own Pantheon override everyone else's for a time. So, a Theoi Scion could use the Boon to bring Theoi cosmology as utterly dominant in the local Scene. Whichever of the Celestial Twins is active at the time would be able to see the area clearly from their chariot, Kami of objects might momentarily cease to be until the effect ends, Theoi Fate rules become active (inexorable, but enforced by the Gods), that sort of thing. It doesn't, however, make Greek or Roman laws or social customs become the norm.<br /> <br /> So, if you used it in Ireland, Dublin wouldn't become like downtown Athens culturally, but wherever you are would essentially become Hibernia. It would still be a far off, barbaric land, and outside the reach of Roman Law, but it would be a place defined by Roman cosmology. If a Tuatha Scion used the Boon in Greece, people wouldn't be compelled to follow Brehon Law, but the line between Mortal and God would become muddied like it is with the Irish, Professions might become semi-magical, bad kings would result in local fertility problems, etc.<br /> <br /> If a Deity who has both Boons uses both Boons, then they could totally work together. But, <i>The True World</i> doesn't natural cause the same effect as <i>Code of Heaven</i> by itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T14:47:20-07:00","id":1140650,"title":"","content":"Thanks Watcher! Could I also ask how certain social relationships work in accordance with Tuatha values, such as: romance, friendship, social media followers, etc. And how do certain factors such as declaring love, unfriending people, and such work in accordance with the Tuatha hierarchy? Lastly how would Tuatha relationships intermesh with those of modern society? I sincerely apology if these are nonsensical or stupid questions. I am just trying to figure out how the Tuatha and their scions would interact with modern society and how mortals would be expected to react. All of this is based on Scion 2e's premise that people just ignore what &quot;shouldn't&quot; be possible according to their personal beliefs and those of mainstream society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T16:52:05-07:00","id":1140672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manannansun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/155803-scion-2-0-project?p=1140650#post1140650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks Watcher! Could I also ask how certain social relationships work in accordance with Tuatha values, such as: romance, friendship, social media followers, etc. And how do certain factors such as declaring love, unfriending people, and such work in accordance with the Tuatha hierarchy? Lastly how would Tuatha relationships intermesh with those of modern society? I sincerely apology if these are nonsensical or stupid questions. I am just trying to figure out how the Tuatha and their scions would interact with modern society and how mortals would be expected to react. All of this is based on Scion 2e's premise that people just ignore what &quot;shouldn't&quot; be possible according to their personal beliefs and those of mainstream society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't worry about asking questions! There are no stupid questions, I am always happy to answer any that I can. I'll just break these down into sections so it's easier to read.<br /> <br /> <b>Social Relationships</b><br /> Love is a very common theme in the medieval Irish literary texts. Modern ideas of love would mesh very well with the way the Tuatha see it, except with a dash of magic, and lethal sickness tied in. The texts have this theme of the Wasting Sickness, a really interesting concept. A Wasting Sickness strikes someone when they are in love, but, for some reason, can't physically access that whom they love. These people are bedridden, and literally waste away as they can't eat anything, slowly dying. CuChulain, Bobd Derg, and Aengus Og all fall ill through these sicknesses, and it takes the outside intervention of another to help snap them out of it. (Emer chases Fand off from CuChulain, Aengus finds Bobd Derg's lover, and Aengus is assisted in finding his beloved by The Dagda) So, in the love department, it fits in with modern ideas. Over the top and lethal, but that's par the course for the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> Friendship is something that we don't see much in the Mythological Cycle, but we see it in the Ulster and Finnian Cycles. The one challenge we have is that, since these are stories, we don't ever see a 'normal day,' there has to be drama or there's no point in this being a story. So, the Friendships we see are normally ones under a lot of stress. CuChulain and his fellow Ulster Heroes are all thick as thieves, and in the Tain we see these Friendships put to the test as situations conspire to have CuChulain's friends set against him. Fergus mac Roich is a friend / father figure to CuChulain, and even though the pair are on opposite sides due to Fergus being incapable of making good life choices, they are still good friends who respect each other. There are several points where they both help one and other even to their own detriment. Conall Cernach is an older hero, but a ferocious friend of CuChulain who goes on the warpath when he is killed, slaughtering everyone who had anything to do with it. And then there's Fer Diad who CuChulain is <i>very close friends</i> with, hugging, kissing, sleeping in the same bed close. That's a whole other thing, but yeah.<br /> <br /> So, Friendship is pretty much just like ours, except set in a narrative so constantly under threat due to the needs of a narrative for drama. <br /> <br /> Now, Social Media is something something I hadn't considered before. The Tuatha would be those really overly dramatic people always up to shit more or less, but the idea of following, unfollowing, and that sort of thing, <i>that</i> would be a mess. That stuff would be taken dangerously seriously. Unfriending someone would be a really fierce social declaration that could really sour relationships and cause knock-on effects through a tribe. Friending someone could equally cause social friction. What would probably happen is everyone had very specific outwardly facing friend lists, friends with folks you didn't like, not friending friends of yours who would cause political messes. Unfriending someone who was above you in social rank would be a <i>mess</i>, I don't have any real textual examples to look to, but breaking up of friendships, or airing political dity laundry in the public like that's not something that would work well within the tight knit, incredibly dramatic social system we see in the texts.<br /> <br /> <b>Modern Society</b><br /> Now, love the Tuatha as I do, their ideas of social relationships wouldn't work awesomely in modern society due to how their society was structured. Kings at the top, noble warriors below them, then trained professionals, everyone else, and then slaves. They were an <i>incredibly</i> classed society, complicated as shit. They were working with a class system that was, while theoretically mobile to a degree, so strict that your legal rights depended on what your rank was. Add to that the fact that the top of the social ladder is a Divine King, something modern society doesn't click much with, it would probably be rather tricky.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem, however, is the exaltation of violence. The society the Tuatha are from / are an echo of / are a fabricated reference to (depending on what theory floats your boat) a society that exalted violence. Killing, raiding, taking slaves, all of this was a primary feature of society, and shaped the structuring of their society. Killing someone for wronging you is totally not cool modernly, but totally a legitimate (if not always legal) idea for the Tuatha. Add to that their Honor-Price system, and you get an even trickier class problem. The wealthier you are, the more you can inflict physical or social damage on other people by simply paying a fine. Implement this in our modern society with such a massive disparity between the wealthy and the not, and you would have the wealthy totally able to kill, maim, and worse to people with no real recourse for it. They would pay the fine, but it would be pocket change.<br /> <br /> <b>Divine and Mortal Interactions</b><br /> Relationships between the Tuatha, their Scions, and Mortals would be a bit messy. For one, the Tuatha are a raiding, slaving, colonizing people who don't see anything wrong with that at all. Add to that the fact that they probably <i>really want</i> to take Ireland back from the Sons of Mil means that there would likely be conflict. The Tuatha are colonizers, Irish mythology is a story of mass colonization, and the Tuatha would be more than happy to just roll up on mortal Ireland and subjugate the mortal population. In my games, what I have generally keeping this at bay is all of the big names being dead. But, honestly, the danger to Ireland isn't the Fomori, it's the Tuatha. The Fomori want to tax people, and have client kingdoms. The Tuatha want <i>Ireland</i>, that's all they want, and they have slaughtered native populations (Fir Bolg) to do it before, and would be willing to do it again. The Tuatha are a dominating force, they want Ireland, and will accept no other options.<br /> <br /> Now, ignoring all the problems with slavery, explotation of lower classes, strict social higherarchy, class systems, and general yucky social systems like that, there is one other big challenge with the relationship. The Tuatha, and their Scions, live these really dramatic, over the top lives. They are The Best and they are The Worst. There is no capacity of being in the middle ground, everything is Awful and Awesome. You fiercely defend your own supremacy, all the while trying to usurp others to nick their honor from them. It is a rather vicious social system, the focus on the best and greatest would create conflict everywhere. Every Tuatha Scion who doesn't win Best Actor would be up there drawing knives and walking on stage. The one who does win Best Actor is probably horrifically pissed they didn't also win Best Supporting Actor, Best Director, and Best Editor. The Olympics would suddenly be a <i>very dangerous</i> place to be. Any contest would be taken lethally seriously. From county fair, to the Nobel Peace Prize, the Tuatha <i>need </i>to be seen to be awesome and better than everyone else, including other members of the Tuath.<br /> <br /> <b>In Sum</b><br /> Ignoring the Social System of the Tuatha, on an individual level they would fit into modern society fairly well. They would be behind the times with women, sexuality, and that sort of thing, but they wouldn't be too bad. The big challenges is that their Social System is something that most modern people would be very uncomfortable with, the fact that they are more than willing to purge Ireland, or enslave it's population, and the fact that they have no chill.<br /> <br /> The Theoi are often described as a bunch of teenagers given Superpowers, the Tuatha are like if you removed someone's capacity to do anything not to the maximum passionate level, gave them super powers, and made them regard violence as a totally okay solution to most problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"